pmc:BasharNonInterferenceDirective a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The non-interference directive"@en, "Die Direktive der Nichteinmischung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says his people hold strictly to a rule that a young civilization is left alone while it does not consciously grant that others exist with whom it might speak; their existence is pressed on no world until it shows willingness to communicate in positive and loving ways. Since the governments humans have made still deny their existence, that chosen belief may not be violated, and contact is limited to quiet individual contacts as occasions arise."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMessengerCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not follow the messenger instead of the message"@en, "Nicht dem Boten statt der Botschaft folgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The speaker gives as one reason for speaking through a channel instead of appearing that humans tend to follow a messenger and neglect the message; if his people appeared in bodies and spoke these words, people would bow to them. He does not want to be held in awe or taken for a saviour, and says that too many would hand their power to his kind, which they decline. Information is to be taken up only if one finds it works for oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "A caution the channelled speaker directs against the reception of himself."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:BasharBlueprintReceiving ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharTestingWhatWorks a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Taking up the information only where it works for oneself"@en, "Die Information nur übernehmen, wo sie für einen selbst funktioniert"@de ;
    skos:definition "The speaker says he reflects how certain ideas served his own people so that listeners may adapt and adopt them, but only if they find for themselves that the ideas work; each listener judges for himself what the material amounts to and whether it is of use."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharInteractingAsEquals a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Opening the door: treating one another as equals"@en, "Die Tür öffnen: einander als Gleiche begegnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Humans open the way to contact not by wishing for it but by showing more desire to meet one another as equals; only in doing so among themselves do they make the vibration that would let Bashar's people come into this dimension and be seen face to face."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOpenContact a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Open, face-to-face contact as equals"@en, "Offener Kontakt von Angesicht zu Angesicht unter Gleichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state the speaker says his people wait for: meeting humanity physically and openly, interacting as equals and exploring creation together, at which point the speakers would no longer be needed as teachers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Very Low Frequency; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEqualityYieldsContact a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Interacting as equals produces the vibration for open contact"@en, "Begegnung als Gleiche erzeugt die Schwingung für offenen Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treating each other as equals is said to produce the vibration enabling Bashar's people to enter human dimension and meet humans directly."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharInteractingAsEquals ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharOpenContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEqualityBeforeContact a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Equality among humans before open contact"@en, "Gleichheit unter Menschen vor dem offenen Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Open contact is said to come only once humans meet one another as equals; wishing for contact alone does not open the door."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharInteractingAsEquals ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharOpenContact ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without it the vibration that allows the visitors through is not created and they remain unseen." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFrequencyGaps a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Hiding from oneself creates gaps that lower one's frequency"@en, "Selbstverbergen erzeugt Lücken, die die Frequenz senken"@de ;
    skos:definition "An energetic reason is said to hold the visitors back: a society of people who conceal things from themselves has gaps in its energy field, which make it seem to vibrate slowly and low. Beings willing to be fully themselves are said to run at a higher frequency, and humans can raise theirs and pass through their transformation with a bare minimum of negative manifestation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Very Low Frequency; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFrequencyShockCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Contact without matched frequencies can cause psychotic shock"@en, "Kontakt ohne angeglichene Frequenzen kann psychotischen Schock auslösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Compared to a fast gear jammed against a slow one: if the two meet physically before their frequencies are matched, the visitors' frequency would push human vibration upward and bring buried material to the surface to be faced, which can break some persons psychotically. Hence no physical meeting without a meeting of minds or an agreed purpose at a fitting time; if it has not happened, listeners should trust that the moment has not yet come."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:BasharOpenContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Very Low Frequency; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharGovernmentContactClaim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Governments know of the visitors; physical meetings with officials"@en, "Regierungen wissen von den Besuchern; physische Begegnungen mit Amtsträgern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked for proof, Bashar says the sessions aim to validate the listeners' existence, not his, and he cannot force belief. He states that Earth's governments are well aware of his people, that society is layered so that many lack the data while many mainstream members of government have it, that several civilizations have already interacted with Earth, and that members of his society have met members of a government physically."@en ;
    skos:note "A claim about the world that could in principle be checked; the work names no government, date or place."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharContactPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction: open landing and full involvement within decades"@en, "Vorhersage: offene Landung und volle Beteiligung binnen Jahrzehnten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says that open contact is approaching and could become relatively common within two to three decades, though at present most of human society does not want it and would meet it with fear and panic. Asked how soon, he says that within thirty to fifty years at most the changes on Earth will make the world ready to be fully involved with his civilizations, and he closes by saying open, joyful interaction lies only a few years away."@en ;
    skos:note "A dated prediction and therefore testable. The chapter fixes the present as 1987; two to three decades gives roughly 2007 to 2017 for contact being relatively common, thirty to fifty years gives 2017 to 2037 as the outer bound for full involvement. The outcome is a public one, open landing and communication, and failure would fall on the prediction; the text however makes it conditional on humanity's decision and timing, which leaves the blame open to be placed on the audience."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a deadline (thirty to fifty years at the outside from about 1987) with an observable outcome, open interaction with the visitors' civilizations; the speaker also says that should humanity decide no, his people will leave."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, closing passage; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTransformationalAgePrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction: the transformational age and a unified planet in about forty years"@en, "Vorhersage: das Zeitalter der Transformation und ein geeinter Planet in etwa vierzig Jahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The present life is called the transformational one. Accelerated change is said to have run on Earth for some forty or fifty years and to run as long again, the date of speaking (given as 1987) being the halfway point; the planet stands at the edge of becoming strong, peaceful and creative, a unified planet in about forty years, while most individuals at their combined average pace will need only some twenty to twenty-five. As a measure of the rate, each single day now is said to bring as many connections to levels of consciousness as one to three years did a decade earlier. Great changes are announced for the next few years."@en ;
    skos:note "A dated prediction and therefore testable: from the stated halfway point of 1987, a unified planet around 2027 and the end of the accelerated phase around 2027 to 2037; for most individuals, completion some twenty to twenty-five years out, about 2007 to 2012."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a deadline with an observable outcome, a unified, peaceful planet; the text sets no measure for unified, and puts no blame on anyone in advance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Highly Focused; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLimboState a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Limbo State: feeling disengaged during the shift"@en, "Der Limbo-Zustand: Gefühl des Ausgekuppeltseins während des Wandels"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked whether the acceleration explains why many feel spaced out, Bashar affirms it: the shifting of gears is under way and many coast along like a car with the clutch held out, not engaged."@en ;
    skos:note "A felt state explained as a symptom of the transition; not entered as a sign of success, since nothing is promised from it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Highly Focused; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBeliefsSetTheLimit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The universe supports one exactly as far as one believes"@en, "Das Universum trägt einen genau so weit, wie man glaubt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Created with free will, humans receive from the universe only as much as they declare themselves ready to handle; whoever buys into the belief that they can do only so much is supported that far and not further. Many fear ecstasy and hold self-limiting beliefs, so that when things go well they ask how long it can last and the universe at once cuts it off. People have always got what they believed they could get, or deserved; deservability is a central issue for most."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharGuiltOppositeOfLove a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Guilt as the true opposite of love"@en, "Schuld als das wahre Gegenteil der Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Earth is said to be unmatched among known civilizations in its expertise in guilt. Guilt always perpetuates limitation and separation and keeps one from one's own empowerment and connection to the Infinite Creation. Hate is the dynamic polar expression of love, but guilt its mechanical opposite: love is total self-worth and creativity, guilt the belief in lacking worth, which stifles creativity; hate still assumes one deserves something, guilt denies that one exists. It keeps at bay happiness, ecstasy and creativity, which are one's birthright, and has become the ethic of a society that thinks nothing worth having comes without suffering and that a painful story is more real than a happy one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Introducing Guilt; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharRemovingGuilt a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Removing guilt from one's toolbox"@en, "Die Schuld aus dem eigenen Werkzeugkasten entfernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allowing oneself to see that the tool of guilt is no longer needed and setting it aside; joined to it is extending to oneself the trust the Creator shows by letting one exist: treating oneself with unconditional love and respect and allowing oneself to shape life the way one would like it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Your Birthright; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharCreatingWhatOneDeserves a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating and attracting what one knows one deserves"@en, "Erschaffen und Anziehen, was man zu verdienen weiß"@de ;
    skos:definition "The capacity promised once guilt is gone: the expansiveness and vitality of one's birthright, and the ability to create and attract consciously the things one knows one deserves, with the recognition that no good thing is too simple or too fine to be real, with no exception at all."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Your Birthright; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharGuiltRemovalYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Setting guilt aside yields the ability to create what one deserves"@en, "Das Ablegen der Schuld bringt die Fähigkeit, Verdientes zu erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once one realizes guilt is no longer needed and takes it out of the toolbox, one gains one's birthright and can consciously create and draw in what one deserves."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharRemovingGuilt ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharCreatingWhatOneDeserves ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Your Birthright; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDesireImpliesAbility a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No desire is given without the ability to fulfil it"@en, "Kein Wunsch ohne die Fähigkeit, ihn zu erfüllen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because one exists, All That Is evidently holds that one deserves to exist; one who exists with the wish for peace, joy and ecstasy was created with the matching ability to attract it, and the mere awareness of this is said to be enough to bring it. The universe does nothing pointless, has always supported everyone fully, and the ability to conceive an idea is itself the sign of the ability to create it. Humans are multidimensional creators, infinite creators made in the Creator's image."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Your Birthright; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBeliefCreatesReality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Physical reality is the product of belief or of fear"@en, "Die physische Wirklichkeit ist das Produkt von Glauben oder Furcht"@de ;
    skos:definition "As one thinks, feels and believes, so one experiences the physical reality around one, always and without exception; it is the product of what one holds possible, or dreads, since fearing a scenario amounts to believing it the likeliest reality. Even physicists are said to be finding that thought drives physical reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Your Birthright; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharChangingTheDefinition a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Reading a situation for its belief and changing the definition"@en, "Eine Situation auf ihren Glauben hin lesen und die Definition ändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Situations are said to come not to show that one is stuck or has failed but to reveal the beliefs one has taken on. Facing an unwanted situation, one recognizes that only a belief could have let it in; seeing the belief now on the surface around one, one grasps its definition and, if one does not prefer it, changes it to one that one does. Then one puts all the trust that built the negative scenario into knowing that reality will mirror the new definition."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Your Birthright; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharRealityMirrorsNewBelief a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reality reflecting a changed belief as strongly as the old one"@en, "Die Wirklichkeit spiegelt einen geänderten Glauben ebenso stark wie den alten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The result promised for changing a definition: physical reality, the built-in self-regulating mechanism that brings unconscious beliefs to conscious view, reflects the new positive belief just as firmly as it reflected the one not preferred."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: an observable outcome (the surroundings change to mirror the new belief), with no deadline and no count; the text does not say what an unchanged situation would mean, and the failure is placed by implication on the believer's remaining belief."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Your Birthright; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDefinitionChangeYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Changing the definition yields a reality that mirrors it"@en, "Die Änderung der Definition bringt eine Wirklichkeit, die sie spiegelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Changing the definition of a belief one has seen in a situation and trusting fully in the change is said to make reality reflect the new belief."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharChangingTheDefinition ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharRealityMirrorsNewBelief ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Your Birthright; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTrustAfterRedefinition a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Change the definition first, then apply full trust"@en, "Erst die Definition ändern, dann volles Vertrauen anwenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The trust that once built the unwanted scenario is to be used after the definition has been changed to a positive one."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharChangingTheDefinition ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharRealityMirrorsNewBelief ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Your Birthright; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharJoyDrummedOut a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Joy is trained out of most children by age three"@en, "Freude wird den meisten Kindern bis zum dritten Lebensjahr ausgetrieben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Everyone is said to be born with full capacity for a joyful life, but the way society is built drums that out of most by the age of three, after which they take on the beliefs society says are needed to survive."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Your Birthright; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMastersOfLimitation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Humanity as the Masters of Limitation"@en, "Die Menschheit als Meister der Begrenzung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Long ago humanity chose as a group to focus strongly into physical matter, and with that came the ability to forget being the creators of one's reality, a kind of catch-22 in which a certain degree of focused limitation brings forgetting with it; the momentum then had to be played out. Humans are now waking and remembering, which is why contact is beginning. As one of the most sharply focused and fastest civilizations known, they have experienced more limitation faster than nearly any other, hence the nickname, which is not meant as an insult. Their example taught another civilization that forgetting is possible, and gave Bashar's people a master key for helping other limited worlds."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Highly Focused; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section How Could You Forget?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharIntegrationAcceleration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Integration accelerates geometrically: synchronicity and no accidents"@en, "Integration beschleunigt geometrisch: Synchronizität und keine Zufälle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Limitation breaks things into complex steps to be lived one after another; once a world starts to unify and opens to positive ideas it accelerates geometrically, everything is within, one lives spontaneously in the moment and literally makes less time. Life becomes interlinked coincidence and synchronicity, one is always where and when one should be, meeting just the people one needs. There are no accidents and never were."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Begin to Unify; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 1 Masters of Limitation, section Highly Focused; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 2, Peace in Our Time
#

pmc:BasharNoNuclearAnnihilation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A collective agreement that humanity will not destroy itself by nuclear means"@en, "Eine kollektive Übereinkunft, dass die Menschheit sich nicht nuklear vernichten wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some seven years before the session, humans are said to have reached a general unconscious collective agreement not to annihilate themselves with nuclear weapons; the apparent rise in violence is the last remnant of such ideas surfacing now that it is safe to bring them up and look at them. In any case nuclear self-destruction would never have been permitted, because it would rip through the fabric of other dimensions of space and time and harm uninvolved civilizations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMissileDeactivationClaim a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Association craft are said to have disabled missile launch systems"@en, "Raumschiffe der Vereinigung sollen Raketenstartsysteme lahmgelegt haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says governments have long known their nuclear devices would not have worked: craft of the Association stationed themselves above missile silos and dampened all launch mechanisms electromagnetically, in repeated demonstrations to governments and military, so that the nuclear tension between the superpowers has since been largely for show to keep standing. Several governments are said to hold extraterrestrial craft, from which they derived some technology but not fluently, lacking concepts of consciousness and unable to penetrate some materials; such principles fail when used for self-gain, being integrative. The information will leak out bit by bit as people let governments serve rather than rule them."@en ;
    skos:note "Claims about the world that could in principle be checked; no silo, date or government is named. The questioner's mention of a craft that crashed forty years before is answered only obliquely."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section Governing Government; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharEngagingGovernmentLovingly a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Engaging one's government lovingly and offering alternatives"@en, "Der eigenen Regierung liebevoll begegnen und Alternativen anbieten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Approach governments not with accusation or anger but in an unconditionally loving and sharing way, telling them one believes in peace and that simpler ways exist, and suggesting alternatives. To find the few representatives of clearer vision, simply be that vibration and be equal to them; be bold and loving in a very practical way, take back the responsibility handed over to the levels of society, participate, and act as if it were one world, feeling as much at ease in the halls of government as anywhere else."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section Governing Government; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNoBarriersToGovernment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No barrier to any level of government: invitations and openings arrive"@en, "Keine Schranke zu irgendeiner Ebene der Regierung: Einladungen und Gelegenheiten kommen"@de ;
    skos:definition "What is promised to one who radiates the one-world frequency: no level of government anywhere is closed to one; one is invited or opportunities present themselves of their own accord, and one flows into settings where a hint or a talk over tea is possible. Governments may then shift their programmes toward sharing what they hold."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: an observable outcome (invitations, openings into government settings), with no deadline or count; the condition is phrased as an absolute, but the text does not say what follows if no door opens."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section Governing Government; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLovingEngagementYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Being the vibration of one world opens every level of government"@en, "Die Schwingung der einen Welt zu sein öffnet jede Ebene der Regierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Radiating the frequency of one world and engaging government in a loving way is said to remove every barrier to government and draw invitations and openings."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharEngagingGovernmentLovingly ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharNoBarriersToGovernment ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section Governing Government; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBeliefIsAction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief and action are one"@en, "Glaube und Handlung sind eins"@de ;
    skos:definition "What one firmly believes, one acts on; action and belief are not separate but a single thing. The more freedom of action one allows oneself, the fewer occasions one makes to sit and complain about how things are."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section Governing Government; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharIndividualAsLever a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Every individual move acts as a lever on the whole society"@en, "Jede Bewegung des Einzelnen wirkt als Hebel auf die ganze Gesellschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each person chose to be in this society now, and would not be here unless they were to make a difference. All levels of civilization, physical, mental, emotional and spiritual, are diversified out of one primal homogeneous energy field, the layers of an onion, and one remains connected to all of them; the outer world reflects every idea explored within, and all travel through space is inner movement mirrored as a symbol. Every small move therefore shifts the whole society, which is like a fluid in which others feel the currents one makes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, opening section (question: how can one individual make a difference); read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharRadioactivityPolymerPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction: polymers that bind radioactive waste within twelve to fourteen years"@en, "Vorhersage: Polymere, die radioaktiven Abfall binden, binnen zwölf bis vierzehn Jahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some researchers are said to be starting to find polymer or plastic materials able to bond molecularly with the residue of toxic, specifically radioactive, waste and contain it so that radiation no longer passes the barrier; they may exist within twelve to fourteen years. They will be nearly bio-organic, modelled on biochemical arrangements in DNA and RNA, with an affinity for heavy elements; absorbing them sets up a magnetic matrix, and what leaves the far side is a particle polarized in a new way, still existing but harmless. Electromagnetic bubbles could also isolate such substances and alter or neutralize them, but humans lack the technology and the frequency is not given, since the future is in flux and discovery must be left to them."@en ;
    skos:note "A dated prediction and therefore testable: twelve to fourteen years from the late 1980s, about 1999 to 2003, with an observable outcome, a polymer barrier that stops radioactive emission. Failure would fall on the prediction, though the speaker hedges that the human future is still in flux."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a deadline with an observable outcome; no one is blamed in advance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section Toxicity / Radioactivity; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFrequencySeparatesUniverses a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "At a higher frequency old toxic substances cease to affect one"@en, "Bei höherer Frequenz wirken alte Giftstoffe nicht mehr"@de ;
    skos:definition "When each person's vibration rises, substances made at the lower frequency will no longer affect the body, belonging to another reality no longer in step with the new one; a separation of universes can be created. A society that bases its power and technology on electromagnetic or gravitic principles will make no more toxic or radioactive by-products; such methods have existed for decades but been suppressed because they do not serve those who control technology."@en ;
    skos:note "The suppression of electromagnetic energy methods is a claim about the world; no researcher, method or date is named."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section Toxicity / Radioactivity; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPlanetaryTurnPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction: humanity recognizes better ways and transforms the world within about twenty years"@en, "Vorhersage: die Menschheit erkennt bessere Wege und verwandelt die Welt binnen etwa zwanzig Jahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked whether humans are killing the planet, Bashar says yes for now but not finally: they are forcing themselves into a corner, and within roughly twenty years as a society they will recognize more efficient ways and transform the world very fast, almost overnight once the recognition is made."@en ;
    skos:note "A dated prediction and therefore testable: about twenty years from the late 1980s, roughly 2007 to 2010."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a deadline with an observable, if loosely defined, outcome (a rapid transformation of how the world treats the planet); no one is blamed in advance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section Toxicity / Radioactivity; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSargonNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Sargon of Akkad as an Orion incarnation"@en, "Sargon von Akkad als Orion-Inkarnation"@de ;
    skos:definition "The historical Sargon of Akkad is called a very strong Orion incarnation, credited with founding by the sword what the text calls the Arabic Empire, which therefore rested on Orion principles; the Middle East is said to have received through such incarnations some of the strongest negative energies on Earth."@en ;
    skos:note "The text's ascription of the Arabic Empire to Sargon of Akkad is recorded as the text gives it."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Sargon of Akkad" ;
    pm:nameRole "a historical conqueror said to have been a very strong Orion incarnation" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section The Middle East; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOrionsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Orions, in Bashar's account"@en, "Die Orioner in Bashars Darstellung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A people whose principles are said to have founded the conquests in the Middle East; in those times they believed that only through struggle and conflict could one express or know oneself, and their incarnations brought strong negative energy to Earth."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Orion; the Orions" ;
    pm:nameRole "an extraterrestrial people of negative orientation whose members are said to have incarnated on Earth" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section The Middle East; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMiddleEastAsCrucible a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Middle East as the repository of the planet's negativity"@en, "Der Nahe Osten als Sammelbecken der Negativität des Planeten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Having never learned that unconditional love is the ultimate power, people there are said to have sought domination as their only way of relating to Creation, and to have spent much energy in past lives on war. The region is the crucible around which other cultures turn, playing out the rest of the world's negativity in a small theatre and thereby freeing others to change; once they stabilize, the greatest changes can occur there. They can learn that everyone is as powerful as needed to have whatever he wants without harming anyone, and that blending all ideologies lets each express its own most easily."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section The Middle East; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTyrantAsReflection a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A tyrant as the collective reflection of a culture's negative beliefs"@en, "Ein Tyrann als kollektive Spiegelung der negativen Glaubenssätze einer Kultur"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked about a ruler in Iran who killed many, Bashar says such a person only mirrors the negative beliefs collected over centuries in that country and in the whole civilization; others have done so and more will. People raised to think themselves weak take domination and harm for power, which is a sign of powerlessness: they thrash in their own nightmares, feeling themselves die inside."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section Negativity Personified; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMiddleEastPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction: the spark in the Middle East, 1997 to 2000, and a world government by 2011 to 2013"@en, "Vorhersage: der Funke im Nahen Osten, 1997 bis 2000, und eine Weltregierung bis 2011 bis 2013"@de ;
    skos:definition "The culture of Iran is to change rapidly within the next decade, the whole area being utterly transformed. A spark will touch off an emotional chain reaction across a wide region: from 1997 to 2000, with consequences running to 2011, the area will change as never in recent history, the spark being the recognition that what people fight is the creeds and barriers that separate them, not one person. Around 1997 a tumultuous upheaval of social, political and religious understanding will come; before 2001 a new model for how the world and a government could develop will issue from there, and the groundwork for a government of the world is to be laid by 2011 to 2013. Violence may escalate and the social structure may break down, though it need not; the sword of Sargon will then reflect light."@en ;
    skos:note "A dated prediction and therefore testable, with several dates: complete transformation of the area within a decade of the session, an emotional chain reaction from 1997 to 2000, a new template for world government from the region before 2001, and its foundation laid by 2011 to 2013."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: several deadlines with observable outcomes; no one is blamed in advance, but the speaker adds that the violence need not happen, leaving the route open."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section Negativity Personified; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section The Sword of Sargon; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTriumviratePrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction: a triumvirate of the USA, the USSR and China"@en, "Vorhersage: ein Triumvirat aus den Vereinigten Staaten, der Sowjetunion und China"@de ;
    skos:definition "The transformation is not toward any present label but toward the unification of the planet. Soon the three great powers, the USA, the USSR and the People's Republic of China, will form a triumvirate that sets the example on which the rest of civilization can build its own world peace and world government; from then national borders will begin to dissolve over the following hundred years."@en ;
    skos:note "A prediction with a loose date (soon) and a long horizon (borders dissolving over a hundred years after the triumvirate). The Soviet Union named as one of the three ceased to exist in 1991."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a deadline in the vague form of soon, with an observable outcome, the formation of the three-power association; no one is blamed in advance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section A New Triumverate; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharMirroringLoveToTheMiddleEast a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Sending love and mirroring positive change to the Middle East"@en, "Liebe senden und dem Nahen Osten positive Veränderung spiegeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each person sends love, acting on whatever stands for the light and love true to them, to be a shining example and a mirror all around that core, reflecting its potential for positive change; and takes whatever avenues of service open up to share who one is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section A New Triumverate; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharIrresistibleReflection a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A reflection of love the region can no longer resist"@en, "Eine Spiegelung der Liebe, der die Region nicht mehr widerstehen kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "The more the surrounding world changes and acts on its love and light, the brighter it is mirrored back, until the weight of the love sent becomes too great for them to withstand."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section A New Triumverate; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMirroringLoveYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Mirroring love to the region yields a reflection it cannot resist"@en, "Liebe zu spiegeln bringt eine Spiegelung, der die Region nicht widerstehen kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sending love and being a mirror of positive change is said to build a momentum of love and light that the region at last cannot resist."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharMirroringLoveToTheMiddleEast ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharIrresistibleReflection ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section A New Triumverate; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharJudgmentalChangeCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not to approach the region as if out to change it"@en, "Der Region nicht begegnen, als wolle man sie ändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The help offered is not to go to them looking as if one means to change them or judging that they ought to change; one only takes the openings that come to share oneself."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharMirroringLoveToTheMiddleEast ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section A New Triumverate; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharConquestNeedsConsent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No world is conquered that does not vibrate to being conquerable"@en, "Keine Welt wird erobert, die nicht auf Eroberbarkeit schwingt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those with conquering intent do not get far; humanity's vibration has changed so that a warlike civilization would barely find Earth, and none such is within hundreds of light-years. Breaching space and time needs a highly integrated attitude, which makes a warlike nature unlikely; a warlike traveller would probably arrive dispersed. Interstellar war is improbable given the distances and room for expansion; each civilization is its own reality until worlds agree to share frequencies. What conquest exists is mostly psychic seduction: a people consents to hand over its power and responsibility to another that promises to meet its needs; without consent it cannot happen, and even that is rare."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section War-Like Planets; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharKnowingOneIsNotOfThatVibration a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing oneself not to be of the vibration of conquest"@en, "Wissen, dass man nicht von der Schwingung der Eroberung ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Given as the best safeguard against being conquered: simply to know oneself as not belonging to that vibration or idea."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section War-Like Planets; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharUnfindableToConquerors a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being unfindable by a conquering civilization"@en, "Für eine erobernde Zivilisation unauffindbar sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "A conquering race, not sharing the same reality, would never find such a world; arriving at what it takes to be that planet, it would find it apparently uninhabited."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: in name only, since the outcome (a conqueror finds the planet empty) is not one the person protected could observe."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section War-Like Planets; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNotOfThatVibrationYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing one is not of that vibration makes one unfindable to conquerors"@en, "Das Wissen, nicht von jener Schwingung zu sein, macht für Eroberer unauffindbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing oneself not to be of the conquering vibration is said to place one in a reality a conquering civilization does not share, so that it would never find one."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharKnowingOneIsNotOfThatVibration ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharUnfindableToConquerors ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section War-Like Planets; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharLovingPeace a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Loving peace instead of hating war"@en, "Den Frieden lieben, statt den Krieg zu hassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Peace comes not from hating war but from loving peace: be peace, live it, breathe it and share it, with unconditional love for all, which is said to transform the whole world in an instant."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section Star Wars (closing question); read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHatingWarCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Hating war reinforces it"@en, "Den Krieg zu hassen verstärkt ihn"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who believes in peace need not hate war; hate only reinforces what one says one does not prefer, since it is what one focuses on."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharLovingPeace ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section Star Wars (closing question); read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharPeaceClockMeditation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The Peace Clock, step one: a minute of peace meditation at noon"@en, "Die Friedensuhr, erster Schritt: eine Minute Friedensmeditation am Mittag"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every day at noon in one's own zone of time, for a whole minute, meditate on world peace in whatever way is comfortable, seeing or imagining the world enjoying peace and harmony. As each time-zone slice, a twenty-fourth of the planet, does so in turn, a wave runs round the globe day after day."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section The Peace Clock; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharSpreadingThePeaceClock a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The Peace Clock, step two: spreading the noon meditation"@en, "Die Friedensuhr, zweiter Schritt: die Mittagsmeditation verbreiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Share the noon minute of meditation with as many as possible: individuals, cities, communities, states and nations, and the radio and television media, which might mark noon with a minute of silence, a tone or a comment, so that everyone participates."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section The Peace Clock; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPeaceClockStepOrder a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The Peace Clock: meditate first, then spread it"@en, "Die Friedensuhr: erst meditieren, dann verbreiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The project is given in two numbered steps, the daily noon meditation and then the sharing of it."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharPeaceClockMeditation ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:BasharSpreadingThePeaceClock ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section The Peace Clock; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFourthDensityShift a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "An electromagnetic momentum spinning the world into fourth density"@en, "Ein elektromagnetischer Schwung, der die Welt in die vierte Dichte dreht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The capacity promised from the Peace Clock: the rotating focus generates an electromagnetic thrust round the planet that will all but spin the world, before one knows it, into fourth density and into synchronicity everywhere, accelerating it so fast that, if the goal is reached by 2000, much will happen from that year that one will scarcely believe; the foundations of one world can be laid between 1990 and 2000."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section The Peace Clock; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPeaceClockYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The Peace Clock yields the momentum into fourth density"@en, "Die Friedensuhr bringt den Schwung in die vierte Dichte"@de ;
    skos:definition "The daily noon minute of meditation, done slice by slice round the globe, is said to create an electromagnetic momentum carrying the planet into fourth density and synchronicity."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharPeaceClockMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharFourthDensityShift ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section The Peace Clock; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPeaceClockGoal a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Peace Clock goal: every person meditating by 1 January 2000, one world founded by 2011 to 2013"@en, "Das Ziel der Friedensuhr: jeder Mensch meditiert bis zum 1. Januar 2000, eine Welt gegründet bis 2011 bis 2013"@de ;
    skos:definition "The stated aim is to have every single individual on the planet doing the noon minute by 1 January 2000; then the foundations for one world can be laid between 1990 and 2000, no later than 2011 to 2013, and there will be peace in our time."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a deadline (1 January 2000) and a count (every single individual on the planet), both observable. The promised result is made conditional on reaching that count, which no one could check and which practically cannot be met, so the failure of the prophesied one world falls on the participants who did not spread it far enough."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: if the goal is met by 2000, many scarcely believable things will begin to happen from that year; observable in principle, unspecified in content."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 2 Peace in Our Time, section The Peace Clock; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 3, Harmonic Wave
#

pmc:BasharHarmonicConvergence a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Harmonic Convergence as a nodal point of overlapping cycles"@en, "Die Harmonische Konvergenz als Knotenpunkt sich überlagernder Zyklen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Explained mechanically as an energy event: many cycles of frequency and consciousness overlap at a node, both reinforcing and cancelling one another, opening a gateway like a vacuum or limbo. In that state of floating disorientation one can perceive all probable realities and choose which one to create on the planet. The labels people put on it are not wrong but may limit or misdirect."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFortyYearCycle a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The forty-year cycle of a society and the forty days of an individual"@en, "Der vierzigjährige Zyklus einer Gesellschaft und die vierzig Tage des Einzelnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every civilization has its own cycles and convergences. Human consciousness on Earth repeatedly runs a cycle of forty orbits, in which changes come about that let one see things polarized by a hundred and eighty degrees from forty years before; religious literature uses forty years for the change of whole cultures and forty days for one person's change. The transformational age spans some eighty years, and the present is its literal midpoint."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section The 40-Year Cycle; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHarmonicWaveTemplate a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The harmonic wave template: four harmonics, points a to d, thirteen gateways"@en, "Die Schablone der harmonischen Welle: vier Harmonien, Punkte a bis d, dreizehn Tore"@de ;
    skos:definition "A diagram like a lotus or mandala, said to be the mechanical tool by which Bashar's people gauge the momentum of a society and when its ideas will play out. Its centre, point a, is the Harmonic Initiation of 1947, the year the society began, perhaps covertly, to recognize that extraterrestrials exist; yellow petals run forty years out to point b, the Harmonic Convergence of 1987; larger orange petals reach point c, the Harmonic Identification about 2017; and where the inner circles touch the outer one lies point d, the Harmonic Synchronization forty years after 1987. The widest points of the yellow and orange petals are two polarity resonance manifestations. Thirteen points including the centre are gateways or vortices, thirteen being the transformational gate number that makes one face what one hid, hence the superstition around it. The Fibonacci series and, with lines removed, the yin-yang symbol are said to be found in it, the latter derived from it."@en ;
    skos:note "The printed diagram the text refers to (yellow, orange and green areas) is not present in the full-text layer; the description here follows the prose."@en ;
    dcterms:date "1987-08" ;
    pm:compiledBy "Bashar through Darryl Anka, in Blueprint for Change" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section The 40-Year Cycle; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section Star Trek; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section Your Own Space Craft; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharOverlayingTheTemplate a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Overlaying the harmonic wave template on a society"@en, "Die Schablone der harmonischen Welle über eine Gesellschaft legen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once one has found the cycle of orbits a society runs on, one lays the template over it and reads off when, in the rest of its transformational age, given changes will arrive."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section The 40-Year Cycle; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharStarTrekManifestation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Star Trek as the culture's two polarity resonance manifestations"@en, "Star Trek als die beiden Polaritätsresonanz-Manifestationen der Kultur"@de ;
    skos:definition "At the two widest petal points a society usually brings forth, through an art form, its strongest image of how it relates to other worlds; the second amplifies the first. For Earth the first fell halfway between 1947 and 1987, in 1967, when the Star Trek programme began, and the second in 1987, when it was relaunched in updated form. Earth is said thereby to fit the template perfectly, which is why the programme has lasted and spread worldwide."@en ;
    skos:note "Offered as evidence that the template fits; it is read off after the fact and was not announced in advance, so it is not counted as a sign of success."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section Star Trek; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHarmonicIdentificationPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction: separation into a parallel Earth around 2017, own spacecraft, full membership in the Association by 2027"@en, "Vorhersage: Trennung in eine parallele Erde um 2017, eigene Raumschiffe, volle Mitgliedschaft in der Vereinigung bis 2027"@de ;
    skos:definition "About thirty years after 1987, roughly 2017, comes point c, the Harmonic Identification, when the frequency of the reality each prefers begins literally to separate from all others and places one on the parallel Earth one is most aligned with; at point d, the Harmonic Synchronization, that becomes the only experience on one's Earth. Point c also marks when society will be able to join Bashar's people in spacecraft of its own, built on technology like theirs, perhaps five years earlier; that capacity is due by 2017 provided it holds to the template, as it very probably will. By 2027 Earth will belong entirely to what is called the Galactic Association of Worlds, as absolute equals."@en ;
    skos:note "A dated prediction and therefore testable for its public parts: human spacecraft comparable to the visitors' by about 2012 to 2017, and Earth a full equal member of the Association by 2027."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: deadlines (2017, perhaps 2012; 2027) with observable outcomes; the text makes the 2017 date conditional on society keeping to the template, which places a miss on the society. The separation into parallel Earths is constructed so that no one on the remaining Earth could observe it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section Your Own Space Craft; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), opening section (point c); read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharBecomingThePattern a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming individually the pattern of the reality one wishes"@en, "Einzeln zum Muster der gewünschten Wirklichkeit werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coming together and focusing consciousness on any undertaking of harmony, love and light, and each individually becoming the pattern for the reality one wants to experience."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section Your Own Space Craft; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharWorldBecomesItsVision a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The world accelerating toward the reality its people envision"@en, "Die Welt beschleunigt sich hin zu der Wirklichkeit, die ihre Menschen sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bit by bit each person adds to the world's ability to become the world envisioned: change comes very fast, the now separate social, economic and political levels begin to blend, and those so aligned can use the combined energy to step up to new levels of awareness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section Your Own Space Craft; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBecomingThePatternYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming the pattern yields rapid change toward the envisioned world"@en, "Zum Muster zu werden bringt raschen Wandel zur ersehnten Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Focusing together on harmony and each becoming the pattern of the desired reality is said to impact the planet and let it change quickly in that direction."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharBecomingThePattern ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharWorldBecomesItsVision ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section Your Own Space Craft; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOctaveMonthGateway a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The octave month as a gateway for blending masculine and feminine"@en, "Der Oktavmonat als Tor zur Verbindung von Männlichem und Weiblichem"@de ;
    skos:definition "Among the many convergences and gateways in a year, this octave month (the session is dated August) is called a very strong one, chiefly for blending all places on the planet and the energies within each person, above all the masculine and feminine aspects."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section Your Own Space Craft; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharGateOfTheMoonDream a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The dream of the Gate of the Moon: an androgynous being stepping out"@en, "Der Traum vom Tor des Mondes: ein androgynes Wesen tritt heraus"@de ;
    skos:definition "A dream communication in which Bashar's people took part through the channel: in a place standing for many places at once, Hawaii, Japan, India, beings wait on a plateau above an ocean for an entity to emerge from a gate known as the Moon Gate and also as the Sun Gate. The being is masculine and feminine at once, in a white sarong, partly Pleiadian, tied to events at Fuji, Shasta and Hawaii, whose triangle spans the Pacific basin and marks the strong return of Lemurian energy. It stands for the blending of masculine and feminine in each person and the integration of all segregated aspects of consciousness into one whole, so that the planet can turn into the one individual the age requires and meet other whole worlds."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section The Dream; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharUnderstandingOwnSymbols a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Consciously understanding one's own symbols and taking responsibility"@en, "Die eigenen Symbole bewusst verstehen und Verantwortung übernehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allowing oneself consciously to grasp what one's own symbols, dreams and imagination stand for in terms of one's own blending and awakening, and taking responsibility for one's life and its creations: waking up now."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section The Dream; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSmoothTransformation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Staying awake through the Convergence: a smooth, harmonious transformation"@en, "Wach bleiben durch die Konvergenz: eine sanfte, harmonische Verwandlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "One who has understood one's symbols will be awake through the Convergence and after; the changes on the planet become blending and smooth harmony, the formerly unconscious images flow together, and one recognizes physical reality as simply a waking dream."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section The Dream; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharUnderstandingSymbolsYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Understanding one's symbols yields a smooth transformation"@en, "Das Verstehen der eigenen Symbole bringt eine sanfte Verwandlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Waking up now by understanding one's own symbols is said to make the planet's transformation one of smooth harmony, without the need to be shaken awake."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharUnderstandingOwnSymbols ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharSmoothTransformation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section The Dream; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharGeophysicalWakeUp a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Geophysical upheaval as the unconscious alternative to waking up"@en, "Geophysische Umwälzung als unbewusste Alternative zum Erwachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many see the Convergence negatively, as a shaking up perhaps with geophysical change; Bashar says that if people consciously understand their own symbols, no unconscious manifestation of such change will be needed to wake them."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: an observable outcome (geophysical changes) with no deadline or count, placed on the people who did not wake up; the text does not say such changes will come, only that they become unnecessary."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section The Dream; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSymbolsBeforeSmoothChange a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Conscious understanding of one's symbols before a smooth transformation"@en, "Bewusstes Verständnis der eigenen Symbole vor einer sanften Verwandlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only if one is willing to understand one's own symbols consciously will one stay awake and the change be gentle."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharUnderstandingOwnSymbols ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharSmoothTransformation ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Otherwise an unconscious manifestation of geophysical change may be needed to shake one awake." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 3 Harmonic Wave (August, 1987), section The Dream; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 4, Living on the Edge
#

pmp:BasharWakingUpNow a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking up now: knowing one deserves happiness without a trial by fire"@en, "Jetzt erwachen: wissen, dass man Glück ohne Feuerprobe verdient"@de ;
    skos:definition "Waking up within oneself now and recognizing that one deserves happiness without first passing through ordeals, so that one does not need to be shaken awake; treating any forecast of catastrophe as an opportunity to see which reality one believes truer, not as a decree."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section The Fluid Future; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Economic Resources (question on an axis shift); read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExemptionFromCatastrophe a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not experiencing a catastrophe even where it happens"@en, "Eine Katastrophe nicht erleben, selbst wo sie geschieht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever recognizes no need for such a tool will not experience it even while staying in a place that does; if enough people in a locale understand this, the whole locale will not experience it. One who does not need it will be drawn, without planning or trying, into a situation that removes one from a place whose majority insists on catastrophe. Those who know they need no trial by fire draw themselves to places where the energy is felt as a restructuring rather than destruction."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: an observable outcome (one is not harmed, or is moved away beforehand, or the locale is spared), with no deadline; the count of how many are enough for a locale is not given."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: those very afraid of the shift draw themselves to sites of destruction, and a person who clings to an outworn belief, refusing to trust his flow, may need violence to break his grip, or may even leave physical life to start afresh; the failure is placed on the person's fear and belief, with no count or deadline."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section The Fluid Future; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Economic Resources (question on an axis shift); read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Old Perspectives; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharWakingUpYieldsExemption a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Waking up now yields exemption from catastrophe"@en, "Jetzt zu erwachen bringt Verschonung von der Katastrophe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing one deserves happiness without a trial by fire is said to keep one from experiencing catastrophe, by being spared on the spot or drawn away beforehand."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharWakingUpNow ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharExemptionFromCatastrophe ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section The Fluid Future; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLivingOnTheEdge a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Living by choice in seismic regions to learn to direct power"@en, "Freiwillig in Erdbebengebieten leben, um Macht lenken zu lernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many enjoy earthquakes and gather where the earth is seismically most active, such as the listeners' California, because the energy spurs them to creativity; they learn to steer this energy instead of fearing it and to identify with the power within, which exceeds any quake ever recorded. Feeling it outside shows them how much power they are, and they choose to let it restructure without destroying."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFluidFuture a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The future is fluid: a forecast is one probable reality"@en, "Die Zukunft ist fließend: eine Vorhersage ist eine wahrscheinliche Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Probable realities are many, and any forecast of catastrophe is one perception of one bandwidth; knowing that energy stands behind that probable future, one need not stay on its frequency, and it does not necessarily mean moving house."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section The Fluid Future; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharFollowingExcitement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Following what is most exciting, including where to live"@en, "Dem Aufregendsten folgen, auch bei der Wahl des Wohnorts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following what excites one most; applied to place, one goes where one is most excited to be, surrounding oneself with an environment suited to who one is being, without thinking of it as fleeing destruction."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section The Fluid Future; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Old Perspectives; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLocaleSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sign that one may safely stay where one lives"@en, "Zeichen, dass man sicher bleiben kann, wo man lebt"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one follows one's excitement and attracts no situation that takes one away, and the place one lives remains the most exciting place to be, that is to be taken as a sign one can stay there and nothing will interrupt one's chosen path."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: an observable absence (no situation arises that would take one away) combined with one's own felt excitement; no deadline or count, and the sign cannot be told apart from ordinary life staying the same."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section The Fluid Future; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExcitementLocaleYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Following excitement places one where one needs to be"@en, "Der Begeisterung folgen bringt einen dorthin, wo man sein muss"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following what is most exciting is said either to bring an opportunity that removes one from a place set on catastrophe or to confirm that one may remain safely."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharFollowingExcitement ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharExemptionFromCatastrophe ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section The Fluid Future; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAtlantisReplay a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Halloween as the eve of the destruction of Atlantis; the United States as its replay"@en, "Halloween als Vorabend der Zerstörung von Atlantis; die Vereinigten Staaten als ihre Wiederholung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked on 1 November, Bashar says All Hallows Eve marks the day before Atlantis was destroyed about eleven to twelve thousand years ago, 1 November the destruction itself and 2 November the day following, remembered as All Souls and All Saints. The present issue repeats the self-destruction of the planet Maldek and, on a smaller scale, the cycle of Atlantis; the United States plays Atlantis, with similar technology and political position and many of the same souls, now deciding whether to destroy the world again. All chose to be here to see that it does not happen."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Atlantis; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharRaMaterialDensityDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against the Ra Material: no one has left this density because no one wanted to"@en, "Gegen das Ra-Material: niemand hat diese Dichte verlassen, weil niemand wollte"@de ;
    skos:definition "A questioner cites the Ra Material for the statement that no one has left this density since the time of Jesus. Bashar answers that it is not that no one could leave but that no one wanted to: the transformation is so attractive that souls choose to stay and return, and thousands of civilizations and dimensions besides look on, all wishing to add momentum to the transformation's group karma."@en ;
    skos:note "An explicit dispute with a named work as the questioner reports it; the other side is not read here and the wording attributed to the Ra Material is the questioner's."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Atlantis; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharEconomyOnEachOther a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Founding the economy on people, not on a symbol"@en, "Wirtschaft auf Menschen gründen, nicht auf ein Symbol"@de ;
    skos:definition "To move through the economic shift: let people themselves back their services instead of a symbol, interact directly between individuals with borders removed, reapportion resources and shift priorities, share responsibilities in any task or company and rely on everyone's resources instead of hoarding or fearing others; create a kind of republic of ideas."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Economic Resources; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNoLack a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No lack and no overpopulation, only distribution; an economic shift without depression"@en, "Kein Mangel und keine Überbevölkerung, nur Verteilung; ein wirtschaftlicher Wandel ohne Depression"@de ;
    skos:definition "The economic structure is shifting and the old one may have to fall apart, to some degree, but there need be no depression: it can be regrown and transformed into a global economy unlike economics as known. There is no real lack on the planet and no actual overpopulation, only a distribution of people and resources that makes it seem so."@en ;
    skos:note "Partly a prediction without a date: a major economic shift and a global economy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Economic Resources; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNeutralCircumstances a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Circumstances are neutral; the effect received follows the meaning one gives"@en, "Alle Umstände sind neutral: die gegebene Bedeutung ist die empfangene Wirkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "No situation carries meaning in itself; all are blank and zero, and one supplies the meaning. Positive meaning yields a positive effect, negative meaning a negative one, as simple mechanics. One experiences the reality one is the vibration of and cannot experience one that one is not; any negative forecast is an offer to choose which energy to vibrate with."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Choosing the Positive; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPredictionsAsProbability a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "There is no prediction of the future, only a sensing of probable energy"@en, "Es gibt keine Vorhersage der Zukunft, nur ein Erspüren wahrscheinlicher Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked about Nostradamus, Edgar Cayce and others who foretell catastrophe, Bashar says no future is absolute: a prediction senses which idea has most momentum at the moment it is made, valid only if the energy does not change. Predictions exist to show where the energy is so that one can change it; once known, a prediction often makes itself obsolete, since awareness of it changes the energy."@en ;
    skos:note "Bearing on the work's own dated forecasts: by this account a forecast that fails can always be read as energy that changed, so the doctrine makes the speaker's predictions unfalsifiable from within."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Choosing the Positive; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFearReinforcesPrediction a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Fear of a prediction makes it more likely"@en, "Furcht vor einer Vorhersage macht sie wahrscheinlicher"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hearing a prediction and believing one cannot change the energy, so generating more fear, reinforces the very energy the prediction detected and makes it likelier to come true."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:BasharPredictionsAsProbability ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Choosing the Positive; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOldPerspectivesDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ancient catastrophe prophecies reflect a belief that change needs destruction"@en, "Alte Katastrophenprophezeiungen spiegeln den Glauben, Wandel brauche Zerstörung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Prophecies are made within their own time. Ancient sensings of the culture's future, named with Nostradamus and Edgar Cayce by the questioner, followed a belief that great transformation could only come once everything existing had fallen apart. Things must come apart so that a new reality can replace them, but breaking down can be creative, simply a willingness to let something change; such predictions now show only where society still stacks its belief that ecstasy must be earned by ordeal, and awakening to one's deserving has already changed much of that energy."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute with named prophets as the questioner introduces them; their works are not read here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Old Perspectives; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharChangingPredictedEnergy a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Taking a prediction as an offer and changing the energy"@en, "Eine Vorhersage als Angebot nehmen und die Energie ändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "On hearing a forecast of catastrophe, take it not as a law of the universe but as an offer to examine where the energy is said to lie; if one does not prefer it there, change it by pursuing what excites one, serving others and behaving as one who knows ecstasy is deserved. Each person is then a channel through which the energy meant for violent upheaval can be turned to constructive ends."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Old Perspectives; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharChangingEnergyYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Changing the predicted energy spares one and one's area"@en, "Die vorhergesagte Energie zu ändern verschont einen selbst und die eigene Gegend"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking a prediction as an offer and acting on excitement and service is said to free one from needing the experience; if enough people in an area realize together they need no catastrophe, the whole area's energy can change and the event need not occur there."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharChangingPredictedEnergy ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharExemptionFromCatastrophe ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Old Perspectives; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNoAccusationOfEntities a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No accusation toward channelled entities who foretell catastrophe"@en, "Keine Anklage gegen gechannelte Wesen, die Katastrophen ankündigen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Of entities channelled elsewhere who describe earthquakes, floods and famine: they are not lying, and when what they say strikes no chord in one there is no call to accuse them; what they share is a potential reality with much momentum behind it, fed by many people's fears. One should meet them as an equal and not treat their information as stronger than what one knows within."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharDearEntityLetter ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Channeled Predictions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharDearEntityLetter a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The letter to a channelled entity that foretells catastrophe"@en, "Der Brief an ein gechanneltes Wesen, das Katastrophen ankündigt"@de ;
    skos:definition "When given catastrophic information through a channel and one feels conviction about it, one may answer the entity, perhaps in a letter: thanking it for sharing out of love, telling it that the catastrophic version is not the reality one prefers as co-creator, that one chooses to face all parts of oneself and accept every situation as serving positively so that one's own transformation need no catastrophe; acknowledging that some may believe only catastrophe makes change last; asking its help with ideas so that as many as possible see that lasting change needs no trial by fire; affirming that ecstasy is one's birthright; and asking how to accelerate so that the transformation can take its gentlest and most loving form."@en ;
    skos:note "The work gives the full wording of a model letter; the definition paraphrases its parts."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Channeled Predictions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEasierNextStep a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A geometric difference to the world's next step"@en, "Ein geometrischer Unterschied für den nächsten Schritt der Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each who uses such a situation, sharing with conviction and not accusing, standing up as the person one knows oneself to be, is said to make a geometric, logarithmic difference to how easily the whole world takes its next step; even a single person adds that much energy to a positive and loving transformation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section What You Are; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDearEntityLetterYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Answering catastrophic channelling with conviction eases the world's transformation"@en, "Gechanneltem Katastrophenwissen mit Überzeugung antworten erleichtert die Verwandlung der Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Using a catastrophic channelling as an occasion to state, without accusation, what one knows to be true is said to make a geometric difference to the ease of the world's next step."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharDearEntityLetter ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharEasierNextStep ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section What You Are; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMaterialUniverseIsYou a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The material universe is what one is; integration dissolves the illusion"@en, "Das materielle Universum ist, was man ist; Integration löst die Illusion auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "All of physical and emotional reality around one is oneself reflected back in different forms. To explore limitation, humans made themselves a reality whose immediate cognition is a material reflection apparently outside, so that they feel they live inside matter instead of being it. In integration they blend dream, imagination and physical reality, pass through disorientation, confusion, limbo and surreal moods, and see through the illusion of matter, a tool that has served well."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section What You Are; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPersonalityConstruct a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The personality as an artificial construct; the soul is not human"@en, "Die Persönlichkeit als künstliches Konstrukt; die Seele ist nicht menschlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "What one takes for one's personality is an artificial construct, not what one is. The essence, a soul or primal energy consciousness, can project itself as any form, and is not intrinsically human even though people habitually picture a disembodied soul as human; many civilizations of third and fourth density look humanoid, and to Bashar's people humans are the humanoids. Disorientation while moving from the third density to the fourth comes from glimpsing a non-human point of view. Later in fourth density people will cease to be humaniform, and passing to fifth density, non-physical, they become the focused energy matrix in the field of All That Is they really are; one also exists simultaneously in other guises, human, humanoid and not human."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Personality Construct; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharViewingFromEssence a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Viewing from the essence, not expecting human sense"@en, "Aus der Essenz schauen, ohne menschlichen Sinn zu erwarten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allowing oneself to see from the standpoint of one's essential being, as everything and nothing, a principle or idea, and no longer limiting oneself by demanding that all of it be intelligible in human-shaped terms; at times, as suits one, looking through the eyes of aspects of oneself unrelated to humanity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Personality Construct; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharClarityInTransition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "New clarity about the confusing events of the shift"@en, "Neue Klarheit über die verwirrenden Ereignisse des Übergangs"@de ;
    skos:definition "Much of what now occurs while passing from the third density into the fourth may take on new clarity, and one's perspective broadens in many ways."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Personality Construct; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharViewingFromEssenceYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Viewing from the essence yields clarity in the transition"@en, "Aus der Essenz schauen bringt Klarheit im Übergang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Viewing from one's essential being, without demanding human sense, is said to bring clarity to the disorienting events of the shift and broaden perspective."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharViewingFromEssence ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharClarityInTransition ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 4 Living on the Edge, section Personality Construct; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 5, The Second Coming
#

pmc:BasharNoRightAndWrong a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No right and wrong: judgment as the choice of the negative"@en, "Kein Richtig und Falsch: Urteil als Wahl des Negativen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In dialogue with a Christian questioner who calls himself a sinner, Bashar says right and wrong do not exist, only the choice between a positively and a negatively manifesting reality. The positive integrates one with All That Is; feeling separate from it breeds isolation and the need to dominate, from which come war, disease and the like. Judgment itself is a negative choice; knowing what one prefers requires invalidating no one. Unconditional love grants validity to everything in creation for its own sake and trusts that everyone will finally be all right; nothing can be lost except into a separation one creates, so the phrase lost soul contradicts itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharYouAreGod a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Each person is God; everything perceived is one's own creation"@en, "Jeder Mensch ist Gott; alles Wahrgenommene ist eigene Schöpfung"@de ;
    skos:definition "If God, which Bashar calls All That Is, is everything and everywhere, no one can be outside it: each is God and God knows it, though people do not. Physical reality is a symbol, an illusion if one likes; everything is vibration and one can perceive nothing one is not, so every person one perceives is one's own version, one's creation. All beings are so many angles from which God views itself, and much exists simply because it can."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Only Son; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSecondComing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The second coming as the recognition of the Christ in each person"@en, "Die Wiederkunft als Erkenntnis des Christus in jedem Menschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The labels and definitions society has placed are the only thing that keeps people from seeing that they are all the Christ. What is called the second coming is no single person's arrival but each individual on the planet recognizing the Christ that he or she is and living accordingly, so that together they create heaven on Earth as children of God. Christ appeared physically far more than once, each time to show that everyone shares in it and that the power to create one's reality belongs to God's own nature; the age that received him could only think in terms of ruler and ruled and made him a saviour."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Second Coming; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Only Son; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharActingAsTheChrist a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Looking in the mirror and acting as the embodiment of Christ"@en, "In den Spiegel schauen und als Verkörperung Christi handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever seeks the incarnate Christ consciousness should look into a mirror at home and from then on behave as that incarnation; applying to oneself his saying about being way, truth and life, and meaning it, feeling the vibration it gives, instead of quoting what he said."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Second Coming; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, closing passage; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharActingAsChristYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Acting as the embodiment fulfils what the Christ consciousness meant to impart"@en, "Als Verkörperung zu handeln erfüllt, was das Christusbewusstsein vermitteln wollte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting as if one were the embodiment of the Christ is said to fulfil what the Christ consciousness sought to give everyone, which is the second coming lived by each."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharActingAsTheChrist ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharSecondComing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Second Coming; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFollowingJesusCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not follow Jesus; be like him"@en, "Jesus nicht folgen, sondern ihm gleich sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked about dedicating one's life to following Jesus, Bashar says Jesus did not want to be followed but to be equalled: following places one apart and beneath, when the way he showed was to be equal and reflect that energy, all being Christ consciousness as he was. Removing one's power from oneself and placing it elsewhere sets a limit that denies one's very existence; followers end up quoting him instead of feeling the vibration themselves."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:BasharSecondComing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, opening section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, closing passage; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBibleDispute a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Bible as a conversion text holding a fraction of what Jesus said"@en, "Die Bibel als Bekehrungstext, der einen Bruchteil dessen enthält, was Jesus sagte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says the biblical literature holds less than ten per cent of what Jesus ever said, and much of that misread by the understanding of its time; the Bible was written not to record history but to convert, is true for those who wrote it, and contains misinterpretation, as every written account does that wraps ritual round what happened. The sayings were not set down until about fifty-seven years after his death. The saying 'I am the way' is glossed as: I show the vibration of integration, equal to All That Is, which you will come to know in yourself only by being as I am. Jesus used for himself the title son of man. God, being unconditional love, does not force an interpretation, yet all of the Bible is God's word as its writers were also God. Fixing on one passage as ultimate truth narrows one's view to a part of the whole."@en ;
    skos:note "An explicit dispute with the Christian tradition and its scripture, conducted with a questioner in the session; the other side is not read here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Second Coming; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Only Son; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharTalkingToHigherConsciousness a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Talking with one's own higher consciousness"@en, "Mit dem eigenen höheren Bewusstsein sprechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked how he knows what Jesus said, Bashar says his people sense into humanity's mass consciousness and higher levels of consciousness, which know themselves equal to the Christ consciousness; he does not expect to be taken at his word, and says anyone can speak to his own higher consciousness in the same way."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Second Coming; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHigherConsciousnessConcurs a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One's higher consciousness telling one what Bashar says"@en, "Das eigene höhere Bewusstsein sagt einem, was Bashar sagt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The promised result of speaking to one's higher consciousness: once one allows it, it will tell one exactly what Bashar is saying."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: an inner report announced in advance (one's own higher consciousness agreeing with the speaker), with no deadline or count; a different answer is not provided for, so the sign doubles as the test of whether one has really reached it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Second Coming; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHigherConsciousnessYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Speaking to one's higher consciousness confirms the teaching"@en, "Das Gespräch mit dem höheren Bewusstsein bestätigt die Lehre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allowing oneself to talk to one's own higher consciousness is said to yield the same information Bashar gives."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharTalkingToHigherConsciousness ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharHigherConsciousnessConcurs ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Second Coming; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharJesusNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Jesus of Nazareth, one facet of the Christ consciousness"@en, "Jesus von Nazareth, eine Facette des Christusbewusstseins"@de ;
    skos:definition "Jesus of Nazareth is called a single facet of the whole Christ consciousness, the world spirit; each world and civilization has a version of its own, and the Christ consciousness of Earth is the combined consciousness of all its people, with which Bashar's people interact directly to serve. Jesus is said to have known his own Godhood and to have reflected that others can do the same. He travelled to the region of India around the ages of seventeen and thirty, had a connection with Egypt, and made many out-of-body journeys."@en ;
    skos:note "The travels to India and Egypt answer a questioner's reading on the years missing from the Bible; they are claims about history."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Jesus of Nazareth; Jesus Christ" ;
    pm:nameRole "a facet and physical manifestation of the Christ consciousness, the combined consciousness of Earth" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Only Son; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, closing passage; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMaryNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Mary, the feminine pole of the Christ"@en, "Maria, die weibliche Polarität des Christus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Mary, the mother of Jesus, is called an unrecognized physical manifestation of the direct Christ consciousness, its feminine pole, since the collective Christ always has male and female."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Mary" ;
    pm:nameRole "the feminine pole of the Christ consciousness" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Only Son; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharShakanaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Shakana, the combined consciousness of Bashar's world"@en, "Shakana, das vereinte Bewusstsein von Bashars Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "In an old language no longer used by Bashar's now telepathic society, the combined consciousness of their whole world was called Shakana; it, Earth's Christ consciousness and the joined consciousness of every other world make up the Infinite Creation together."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Shakana" ;
    pm:nameRole "the collective consciousness of Bashar's world, its counterpart of the Christ consciousness" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Only Son; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExistenceBeforePurpose a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Existence precedes purpose: All That Is creates because it can"@en, "Das Sein geht dem Zweck voraus: Alles, was ist, erschafft, weil es kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "Existence simply is, always; time lies inside All That Is, not the reverse. Ultimate truth and purpose are concepts within existence, which was there before purpose and needs none to go on; All That Is expresses itself in every way it can for no reason but that it is the Creator. Whatever one can conceive is real on some level."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section The Only Son; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharRelationshipWithAllThatIs a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being All That Is and relating to it at once"@en, "Zugleich Alles, was ist, sein und sich darauf beziehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Symbols of belief are valid for whoever holds them and will change; what one believes does not matter so long as the belief springs from unconditional love of All That Is and of oneself, since belief creates one's reality. Answering that he lacks a relationship with God, Bashar says he holds both: he knows he is All That Is and that All That Is relates to him as higher consciousness, creating whatever relationship he wishes, each as real; for his people the felt ecstasy is that relationship."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section Changing Symbols; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEndOfSeparationPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction: the whole civilization recognizes itself as All That Is within thirty to fifty years"@en, "Vorhersage: die ganze Zivilisation erkennt sich binnen dreißig bis fünfzig Jahren als Alles, was ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "For about twenty-five thousand years humans chose as a group to explore forgetting that they are All That Is; now they are done with separation, hence the new age. Separation created more time, which is why it took so long; within roughly the next thirty to fifty years the whole civilization will recognize itself as the Creator, and integration can be lived out on the planet in only some two or three thousand years, after which no one need reincarnate here."@en ;
    skos:note "A dated prediction and therefore testable in its first part: thirty to fifty years from the late 1980s, about 2017 to 2037, for the whole civilization to recognize itself as All That Is."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a deadline with an outcome that is only loosely observable (a civilization-wide recognition); no one is blamed in advance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section Changing Symbols; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHolySpirit a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Holy Spirit as the collective electromagnetic mentality"@en, "Der Heilige Geist als kollektive elektromagnetische Geistigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Holy Spirit, which Bashar also calls world spirit, is said to be the collective electromagnetic mentality from which individual minds are made, literally an electrical and electromagnetic phenomenon, the light of the world's consciousness, a sea in which all are immersed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section Changing Symbols (question on the Holy Spirit); read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharAligningWithTheSpirit a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Aligning electromagnetically with the spirit by raising one's vibration"@en, "Sich elektromagnetisch mit dem Geist ausrichten, indem man die eigene Schwingung hebt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accelerating one's vibration by the means discussed, excitement, service, positivity and the like, so as to align electromagnetically with the energy sea of the spirit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section Changing Symbols (question on the Holy Spirit); read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTelempathy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Telempathic union with all beings: knowing all thought"@en, "Telempathische Verbindung mit allen Wesen: alle Gedanken kennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being of the spirit: flowing harmoniously with every other being, linking telepathically with them and knowing all thought; telepathy is more exactly telempathy, activated emotionally by love."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section Changing Symbols (question on the Holy Spirit); read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAligningYieldsTelempathy a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Aligning with the spirit yields telempathic union"@en, "Ausrichtung mit dem Geist bringt telempathische Verbindung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Raising one's vibration through excitement, service and positivity is said to align one with the spirit, so that one becomes of the spirit and knows all thought telempathically."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharAligningWithTheSpirit ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharTelempathy ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section Changing Symbols (question on the Holy Spirit); read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharCatholicChurchOrigin a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Catholic Church as an offshoot of Atlantean priesthoods by way of Druidic practice"@en, "Die katholische Kirche als Ableger atlantischer Priesterschaften über druidische Praxis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many Catholic rites are said to derive from ancient Druidic practice, remnants of the priestly hierarchy of Atlantis, reshaped by councils and leaders and handed down as misunderstood notions of hierarchy, with some mingling with Orion incarnations a few thousand years ago. In reaction to the negativity of the sinking of Atlantis came the belief that reconnection to the Infinite is regained by suppressing the will, by order and domination. Not Jesus but those around him, steeped in Druidic knowledge, set up the structure, continuing a lineage with much misinterpretation."@en ;
    skos:note "A dispute with the popular belief, voiced by the questioner, that Jesus instituted the Church."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section Catholic Church; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAfterDeath a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "After death: a thought form among thought forms meeting one's strongest beliefs"@en, "Nach dem Tod: eine Gedankenform unter Gedankenformen, die ihren stärksten Glaubenssätzen begegnet"@de ;
    skos:definition "At death one no longer takes oneself as physical, knows one chose everything in that life, and may create any other reality here or elsewhere, or not reincarnate. One first finds oneself one thought form among others and meets the seeming physical form of one's strongest beliefs, heaven, hell or between. There the mind turns instantly into experience, so pain one cannot bear lessens, and on seeing that a changed thought changes the scene one leaves it; only true masochists could stay long in hell."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section After Death; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharReincarnation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Some two to three thousand lives, each return a new being; this life may be the final one"@en, "Etwa zwei- bis dreitausend Leben, jede Rückkehr ein neues Wesen; dieses Leben kann das letzte sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reincarnating is chosen each time. Each person present has had on average two to three thousand lives in the Earth cycle of the past fifty thousand years or so, having chosen to explore limitation as it is lived here and having been every possible thing. Yet each return is an entirely new being and universe, so in that sense nobody returns. As this is the transformational life and the cycle is ending, one may choose this to be one's final physical life in it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section Further Reincarnation; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 5 The Second Coming, section Changing Symbols (question why people keep returning); read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 6, Life Works!
#

pmc:BasharInfiniteCreatorNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Infinite Creator, out of whose love all things are made"@en, "Der Unendliche Schöpfer, aus dessen Liebe alle Dinge gemacht sind"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar names the Infinite Creator as the one by whom everything has been created out of love, the primary vibration; every being is called a hologram of the Infinite Creation and a reflection of Infinite Creatorhood, and the hearers are told they are already aspects of the Infinite."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "the Infinite Creator; the Infinite Creation; the Infinite" ;
    pm:nameRole "the creator of everything, out of love as the primary vibration, of whom each being is a holographic representation and an aspect" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Being in Love; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Different Frequencies; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLoveAsFabricOfCreation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Love as the primary vibration and fabric of all reality"@en, "Liebe als Grundschwingung und Gewebe aller Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The transformation of consciousness now under way on Earth is said to consist in learning to fall in love with the whole world, the multiverse and all creation. Love is the basic vibration from which the Infinite Creator made everything; every being is made of it, so every act is at bottom an act of love, and every physical or non-physical experience draws from it the energy to become real. Learning to create the reality one wishes is learning to identify with this vibration; it is remembering what one already is, not learning something new, and blending with that flow lets one sculpt reality into the shape of the heart's desire."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Being in Love; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDefinitionsCreatePhysicalReality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Physical reality has no existence apart from one's definitions and beliefs"@en, "Die physische Wirklichkeit existiert nicht getrennt von den eigenen Definitionen und Überzeugungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each person is said to create his physiological reality by a mechanism bound up with his definitions, the belief systems about what reality he has been taught he ought to experience. Bashar says many of Earth's physicists are coming to see that physical reality has no empirical existence apart from the observer and no existence without his definition and imagination of it."@en ;
    skos:note "The appeal to physicists names no one and cites no work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Being in Love; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBeliefSystemsAsBackdrop a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A primary belief gathers similar beliefs into a backdrop taken for the way reality is"@en, "Eine Hauptüberzeugung sammelt ähnliche Überzeugungen zu einer Kulisse, die man für die Wirklichkeit selbst hält"@de ;
    skos:definition "A system is glossed as a pattern, a cycle of observations or ideas giving the sense of continuity and cohesion. Every belief is a vibrational frequency; once manifested it draws to itself slightly out-of-phase beliefs of similar nature, so that the primary belief stands out against a graded background. This happens automatically and very fast; the background becomes ingrained and is then taken for reality as it simply is, existing without oneself, and is a main mechanism behind the illusion of a universe outside. No belief exists alone: each brings its whole entourage of props, stage and an audience receptive to that play."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Systems of Belief; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Changing the Primary Focus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPrimaryFocusDominoEffect a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Changing the primary focus changes the entire background"@en, "Eine Änderung des Hauptfokus ändert den gesamten Hintergrund"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because everything is connected and is one thing, altering the fundamental beliefs that make up a being changes the whole backdrop in a domino effect, sometimes subtly but widely, if one lets oneself recognize it. Cause and effect are one and the same event: one may change the whole system or one particular within it, and in every case both change, so it can be worked from either end."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Changing the Primary Focus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharChangingTheWholeStage a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Changing the primary belief on a new stage: acting as if everything has changed"@en, "Die Hauptüberzeugung auf einer neuen Bühne ändern: handeln, als habe sich alles geändert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whoever wishes to change a primary focus is told not to play it out on the old stage but to know himself in a wholly different place where everything has changed, to look for validation first in the primary signal and not in the background's echo, and, once the change is made, to function as though it had occurred across the whole spectrum rather than in one localized effect."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Changing the Primary Focus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEchoValidationCancelsChange a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeking validation in the unchanged background cancels the change"@en, "Bestätigung im unveränderten Hintergrund zu suchen hebt die Änderung auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many create seeming contradictions: they say they wish to change their primary focus but keep seeing it against the same background. Looking at the background as before cancels at once the change made in the focus, since the two are one thing; whoever waits for the echo to change before validating the change stays in the reality already focused."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: no deadline and no count; the sign is an observable habit, judging the new focus against the old surroundings, and the failure is put on the person who keeps doing so, not on the teaching or the world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Changing the Primary Focus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEchoValidationCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Warning against weighing the change against the old background"@en, "Warnung davor, die Änderung am alten Hintergrund zu messen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The hearer is warned that he will tend to look to the echo for changes before he validates the change he has made, and that while he does so he only continues in his existing reality; validation must come first in the primary signal."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharChangingTheWholeStage ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Changing the Primary Focus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharChangingOnesDefinitions a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Reaching the definitions behind one's reality and changing them"@en, "Mit den Definitionen hinter der eigenen Wirklichkeit in Kontakt kommen und sie ändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "One is said to be able to reach the definitions by which one has created the physical reality experienced for thousands of years, and to change them into whatever pattern one wishes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Changing the Primary Focus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharDesiringThroughJoyAndIntegrity a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Expressing one's desires through joy, love, light, service and integrity, knowing what one does"@en, "Die eigenen Wünsche durch Freude, Liebe, Licht, Dienst und Integrität ausdrücken, im Wissen um das eigene Tun"@de ;
    skos:definition "The manner of desiring set as the condition of unlimited creation: understanding that one is doing what one does, and expressing one's desires through joy, love, light, service and integrity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Changing the Primary Focus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharUnwithheldCreation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating the reality one desires, when and as one wants, with nothing withheld"@en, "Die gewünschte Wirklichkeit erschaffen, wann und wie man will, ohne dass etwas vorenthalten wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "The promised result of the teaching: creating very easily the realities one desires, at the time and in the exact manner one wants, the universe withholding absolutely nothing; at the end of the chapter, creating reality to be as one prefers as soon as one believes oneself capable of it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Changing the Primary Focus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharChangingDefinitionsYieldsCreation a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Changing one's definitions yields the reality desired, with nothing withheld"@en, "Die Änderung der eigenen Definitionen bringt die gewünschte Wirklichkeit, ohne dass etwas vorenthalten wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one can change one's definitions into the pattern one desires, one can quite easily create the realities one desires, when and how one wants; so long as the desires are expressed through joy, love, light, service and integrity the universe will withhold nothing."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharChangingOnesDefinitions ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharUnwithheldCreation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Changing the Primary Focus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharJoyAndIntegrityBeforeCreation a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Desiring through joy, love, light, service and integrity as the condition of nothing being withheld"@en, "Wünschen durch Freude, Liebe, Licht, Dienst und Integrität als Bedingung dafür, dass nichts vorenthalten wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "The promise that the universe withholds nothing is made on condition that one understands what one is doing and expresses one's desires through joy, love, light, service and integrity."@en ;
    skos:note "Given as a condition ('as long as'); the text does not say what follows when it is not met, so it is not entered as a stated necessity."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharDesiringThroughJoyAndIntegrity ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharUnwithheldCreation ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Changing the Primary Focus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFrequencySetByBeliefs a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Everything is one substance differing only in frequency, and beliefs set one's frequency"@en, "Alles ist eine Substanz, die sich nur in der Frequenz unterscheidet, und Überzeugungen bestimmen die eigene Frequenz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Everything is energy vibrating at different rates; things and persons differ only by pitch, the level at which they define themselves, being all of one homogenous substance. Every being is self-aware, self-reflective and endowed with free will, and a hologram of the Infinite Creation, able to operate at any frequency it wishes; its levels are set automatically by the beliefs it holds most strongly. Earth society has long been given to self-invalidation, and so people buy into judgements others put on them and into belief systems that do not reflect who they wish to be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Different Frequencies; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharActingAsThePreferredSelf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Acting as the person one imagines oneself wanting to be"@en, "Als die Person handeln, die man sich zu sein wünscht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The central procedure of the chapter: stop looking outside oneself for what would let one be who one wants to be, and be it; behave as the person one envisions being, the one who no longer needs to batter or invalidate herself, and act physically on the certainty that being able to imagine another way of being already is being that other person. When the dial is turned to the preferred self, leave it there and assume that conceiving it is being born as it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Different Frequencies; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Believing Is Seeing; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Guaranteed to Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBecomingThePreferredSelf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being the preferred person, with a life that reflects only that person"@en, "Die bevorzugte Person sein, mit einem Leben, das nur diese Person spiegelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The promised state: one is the person one has imagined, and one's life contains only what is representative of that kind of person, since nothing not of one's vibration can be experienced in one's reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Believing Is Seeing; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Guaranteed to Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharActingAsPreferredSelfYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Acting as the preferred self yields a reality that reflects it, guaranteed 100%"@en, "Als bevorzugtes Selbst zu handeln bringt eine Wirklichkeit, die es spiegelt, zu 100% garantiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting as what one imagines oneself wanting to be makes one it, and the experiences that seem to come from outside will represent who one is now willing to believe one can be. Bashar says he cannot prove any of this to the hearers but guarantees one hundred percent that they can prove it to themselves: reality will mirror that idea alone."@en ;
    skos:note "The guarantee is the strongest promise of the unit and is put as self-testable; it names no period and no measure by which a hearer would count the test failed, and the conditions of failure elsewhere in the chapter place any shortfall on the hearer's remaining old beliefs."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharActingAsThePreferredSelf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharBecomingThePreferredSelf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Different Frequencies; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Believing Is Seeing; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Guaranteed to Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharReflectingRealityAsProof a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A life that reflects the chosen self as the proof one can give oneself"@en, "Ein Leben, das das gewählte Selbst spiegelt, als Beweis, den man sich selbst geben kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "What the hearer is to look for: the life comes to contain the things representative of the person one has decided one is, mirroring that idea alone; this is the proof Bashar says each can give himself, though he cannot give it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: no deadline and no count; an outcome the hearer is to observe in his own circumstances, judged by himself alone, with no third party and no measure named."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Believing Is Seeing; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Guaranteed to Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharUnpreferredEventsShowOldSelf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Events one no longer prefers show that one is still being the old person"@en, "Ereignisse, die man nicht mehr bevorzugt, zeigen, dass man noch die alte Person ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since the events of a life can only reflect, one hundred percent, the person one has decided to be, experiencing events one no longer prefers means one has not yet taken up the other way of being one can already imagine; urges belonging to the old self show likewise that one is no longer the preferred self but the one who has them."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: no deadline and no count; the sign is observable, the presence in one's life of unpreferred events or urges, and the failure is put entirely on the person, as still choosing the old vibration, never on the procedure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Believing Is Seeing; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBelievingIsSeeing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Believing is seeing: perception follows belief, often unconscious belief"@en, "Glauben ist Sehen: Wahrnehmung folgt der Überzeugung, oft einer unbewussten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Society teaches that seeing is believing; Bashar reverses it. A belief may be unconscious, so that when its manifestation is seen one thinks the sight created the belief; but one sees things only if one already believes one will, and outer reality then forms symbols of that belief. Seeing shows that the belief exists and lets it become conscious."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Believing Is Seeing; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharConceivingIsBeing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "To be able to imagine a way of being is already to be at its vibration"@en, "Eine Weise des Seins vorstellen zu können heißt bereits, auf ihrer Schwingung zu sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to imagine what one would like to be is said to be the ability to be it; at the moment one conceives it one is that person, for if one were not of that vibration one could not picture it, as one must be tuned to a station to hear it. Asking what one must first do or see to become the ideal puts all the steps in one's way. The persona is an artificial construct of consciousness and becomes literally another person when consciousness changes its idea of itself; this is called only mechanics and physics."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Believing Is Seeing; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSelfLimitingStatementsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Warning that saying one has trouble, finds it hard or hopes creates that reality"@en, "Warnung, dass zu sagen, man habe Mühe, finde es schwer oder hoffe, eben diese Wirklichkeit erschafft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hearers are corrected for their own words: hope implies despair and uncertainty; saying one has trouble staying tuned is what creates the trouble and still believes one is the old program, whereas this is day zero and the present is the sole place one ever exists; the statement that a concept is difficult to hold is itself a belief and yields a reality of someone who finds it difficult."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharActingAsThePreferredSelf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Believing Is Seeing; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Tuning In; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharChosenParentsAndAgreements a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Chosen parents and prior agreements do not bind one's present creation"@en, "Gewählte Eltern und frühere Vereinbarungen binden die gegenwärtige Schöpfung nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked about choosing one's parents to learn lessons, Bashar answers that such a choice does not keep one from expressing the lesson positively; many such scenarios and agreements are chosen precisely to bring one to realize that at any moment one is self-contained and can determine one's reality regardless of them. Predestination shows only in the most general terms, as a theme such as self-empowerment, not in specifics such as which food one eats."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Believing Is Seeing; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBasicTrustSuffices a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A basic trust that one has and knows what one needs suffices; total knowledge would hamper"@en, "Ein Grundvertrauen, dass man hat und weiß, was man braucht, genügt; totales Wissen würde behindern"@de ;
    skos:definition "All that is needed is the trust that at every moment one has what one needs and knows what one must know to be who one is being; when one redefines oneself, one will know what that person needs to know. Knowing everything is not needed to function in physical reality and would hinder it. Everyone is said to be as powerful as needed to create anything desired without hurting oneself or others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Guaranteed to Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharLivingAsTheExampleOfThePreferredWorld a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Changing oneself first and living as if the preferred world were already real, as an example to others"@en, "Zuerst sich selbst ändern und leben, als sei die bevorzugte Welt schon wirklich, als Beispiel für andere"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since one cannot change anything out there but only allow others and situations to change, one is to feel love within first, change oneself, and be an unconditionally loving example regardless of what others choose. One forms the image of the world one prefers and lives as one would in that world, becoming a receiving beacon for that program so others can tune to it; trust is to be placed in one's love making the difference."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Guaranteed to Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Tuning In; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharArrivingAtThePeacefulEarth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Arriving at the already existing peaceful and abundant Earth"@en, "Ankunft auf der bereits bestehenden friedlichen und überreichen Erde"@de ;
    skos:definition "All possible Earths are said to exist here and now like programs reaching a radio at once, the one received being the one tuned to. Living as its example takes one to the Earth that already is peaceful, harmonious and abundant everywhere, and lets others pick up the broadcast and tune their dials to it; suffering, war and hatred are called illusions and old programs everyone will tire of sooner or later."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Guaranteed to Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Tuning In; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExampleYieldsPeacefulEarth a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Being the example of the preferred world takes one to that Earth and broadcasts it to others"@en, "Das Beispiel der bevorzugten Welt zu sein führt einen auf diese Erde und sendet sie an andere"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being the unconditionally loving example and living as in the preferred world is said to create the desired changes, take one to the frequency of the Earth that is already peaceful and abundant, and make that program available for others to tune in to."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharLivingAsTheExampleOfThePreferredWorld ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharArrivingAtThePeacefulEarth ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Guaranteed to Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Tuning In; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOwnVibrationBeforeThatEarth a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Making the vibration of the preferred world one's own before one can see it"@en, "Die Schwingung der bevorzugten Welt zur eigenen machen, bevor man sie sehen kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "Love must be felt within first or it will never be seen outside, and the peaceful Earth that exists now will never be seen unless one makes its vibration one's own; others cannot find the program if no one lives it as an example."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharLivingAsTheExampleOfThePreferredWorld ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharArrivingAtThePeacefulEarth ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Love and the peaceful Earth are never seen outside, and others have no example by which to find that program." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Guaranteed to Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Tuning In; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharReinforcingOthersRealityCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Warning that joining others in their frustration only reinforces their reality"@en, "Warnung, dass sich der Frustration anderer anzuschließen nur ihre Wirklichkeit verstärkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Buying into the reality of others and becoming frustrated and hateful because they are, only reinforces the reality they already live and gives them no example of another way; the text adds that it does not ask one to ignore that others choose to suffer."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharLivingAsTheExampleOfThePreferredWorld ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Guaranteed to Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharFollowingTheChangingExcitement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Following the excitement through every change of form, as water down whatever channel it takes"@en, "Der Begeisterung durch jeden Formwechsel folgen, wie Wasser in jedem Lauf, den es nimmt"@de ;
    skos:definition "When something begun with excitement changes course, one is to read it as continuing in another mode, perhaps one needed to attract the people one first wanted, and to go along the channel it leads however it meanders, trusting that the meandering is the quickest route; one is not to try to know analytically all the paths it might take."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Tuning In; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section No Interruptions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharContinuingExcitementSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Excitement that continues is the sign the undertaking still continues"@en, "Fortdauernde Begeisterung ist das Zeichen, dass das Vorhaben weitergeht"@de ;
    skos:definition "However the undertaking changes, even when it seems unrelated to its starting course, the persistence of excitement is said to show that the whole idea is still going, like water still in the river however many tributaries it takes."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: no deadline and no count; an inner sign, felt excitement, observed by the person alone; it licenses continuing even when the outward course seems to have nothing to do with the original aim."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section No Interruptions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAssumedInterruption a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The assumption that a change of form means the process has stopped creates the interruption"@en, "Die Annahme, ein Formwechsel bedeute das Ende des Vorgangs, erzeugt die Unterbrechung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Earth people are said to assume that if something does not manifest as they think it should, the process has stopped; it is only this assumption that creates the interruption they experience. Refusing a new channel because it is not the old one, while still sensing the excitement, is damming the river oneself."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: no deadline and no count; the observable mark is the stall of something begun with excitement, and the cause is put on the person's assumption and refusal, never on the excitement followed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Tuning In; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section No Interruptions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLessSleepMoreTime a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Needing less sleep and having more time"@en, "Weniger Schlaf brauchen und mehr Zeit haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being consciously in touch with the levels of consciousness one otherwise reaches unconsciously in sleep, so that one probably sleeps less and so probably has the experience of more time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section No Interruptions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFollowingPathYieldsLessSleep a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing one follows one's own path brings fuller contact with consciousness and less need of sleep"@en, "Zu wissen, dass man dem eigenen Weg folgt, bringt volleren Kontakt mit dem Bewusstsein und weniger Schlafbedarf"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one lets oneself know that at every moment one follows the path one has created, one comes into stronger touch with all levels of one's consciousness and needs less unconscious time in sleep to connect to them; one will probably sleep less and have more time, though one already has all the time one needs."@en ;
    skos:note "Stated as probable, not certain; the only bodily prediction in the chapter."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharFollowingTheChangingExcitement ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharLessSleepMoreTime ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section No Interruptions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharLivingInTheNow a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Live now: accepting what comes as belonging in one's life and getting excited"@en, "Jetzt leben: annehmen, was kommt, als zum eigenen Leben gehörig, und sich begeistern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against inner blocks there is no mysterious how: laugh and be happy because one wants to; live utterly in the moment, open and vulnerable, which is called strength and not weakness; assume what happens belongs in one's life, accept, acknowledge and integrate it, live through it, explore and examine it, get excited; act as if one knows the blocks are there for one's own reasons, conscious of them or not."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section No Interruptions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMatchingEnergyInstantly a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Matching any energy instantly and using blocks as acceleration"@en, "Jede Energie sofort angleichen und Blockaden als Beschleunigung nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Matching at once the frequency one has chosen and any energy that comes along, and becoming conscious sooner of why a block is there; often the only reason found is that it was there to be accepted as energy for acceleration, after which one moves on to the next thing, always in joy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section No Interruptions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLivingNowYieldsMatching a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Living in the now yields instant matching of energy and quicker insight into blocks"@en, "Im Jetzt leben bringt sofortige Angleichung an Energie und schnellere Einsicht in Blockaden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Laughing because one wants to matches that frequency at once; living fully in the now matches instantly any energy or difference one meets; and the more one acts as if one knows the blocks serve one's own reasons, the sooner one becomes conscious of those reasons. It is called that easy."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharLivingInTheNow ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharMatchingEnergyInstantly ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section No Interruptions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharCreatingTheEffectFirst a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Being happy without waiting for a reason: creating the effect first"@en, "Glücklich sein, ohne auf einen Grund zu warten: zuerst die Wirkung erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since cause and effect are said to be one and the same event, one need not wait for a cause of happiness; one creates the effect of being happy just because one wants to and says so, as creator of one's reality, needing no further why or how."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section No Interruptions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAttractingCausesOfHappiness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Attracting the causes that support a happiness already created"@en, "Die Ursachen anziehen, die ein bereits erschaffenes Glück stützen"@de ;
    skos:definition "That the circumstances supporting one's happiness are drawn into one's life after one has created the happiness itself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section No Interruptions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEffectFirstYieldsCauses a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Creating the effect of happiness attracts its causes"@en, "Die Wirkung des Glücks zu erschaffen zieht seine Ursachen an"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creating the effect of being happy is said to attract into one's life all the causes that support the happiness one has created; what one says goes."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharCreatingTheEffectFirst ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharAttractingCausesOfHappiness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section No Interruptions; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharVictimhoodAsCreation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Victimhood is created by the one who experiences it, and explaining it is not condoning it"@en, "Opferschaft wird von dem erschaffen, der sie erlebt, und sie zu erklären heißt nicht, sie gutzuheißen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar recounts an exchange with a man who thought it a dangerous teaching to tell someone creating himself a victim that he creates the whole scenario, and took it as rationalizing victimhood. Bashar answers that explaining the mechanism is neither rationalization nor condonement: the intention is always to hand back power, the hand being on the lever of control even in creating victimhood, and one can at any moment cease creating it and create unbridled joy instead."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Victimhood; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharOwningEverythingExperienced a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Acknowledging and owning everything one experiences, positive and negative"@en, "Alles Erlebte, Positives und Negatives, anerkennen und als das Eigene annehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Holding within one's belief system an full acknowledgement and owning of everything in one's life, both positive and negative."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Victimhood; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharControlOverOwnLife a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Absolute control over one's own life and an end to victimhood"@en, "Absolute Kontrolle über das eigene Leben und ein Ende der Opferschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "The result Bashar says his civilization's perspective can bring: absolute control over one's own life, the positive creation of what one desires, ceasing to create victimhood and creating joy and ecstasy with no end to it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Victimhood; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOwnershipBeforeChange a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Owning everything one experiences before one can change it"@en, "Alles Erlebte als das Eigene annehmen, bevor man es ändern kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "In Bashar's understanding, which he says has always worked for his people, there must first be an full acknowledgement and owning of everything one experiences, since one cannot change what one does not own."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharOwningEverythingExperienced ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharControlOverOwnLife ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "What one does not own cannot be changed." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Victimhood; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharTakingTeachingsNeutrally a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Taking anything said neutrally and using it only if it works for one"@en, "Alles Gesagte neutral aufnehmen und es nur nutzen, wenn es einem dient"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar asks that whatever he or anyone else says be taken first from a neutral standpoint; one then assigns the meaning that relates most to one's life, uses it if workable and leaves it if not, and may change one's mind later. He says he does not care whether it is workable, since it comes from love."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Victimhood; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDangerousPhilosophyBelief a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No neutral philosophy is dangerous; the danger lies in believing it is"@en, "Keine neutrale Philosophie ist gefährlich; die Gefahr liegt im Glauben, sie sei es"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every philosophy can be applied positively or negatively; any danger comes from believing a philosophy dangerous, and since every belief is a self-fulfilling system, whoever fears one will meet only negativity and danger from it if he applies it."@en ;
    skos:note "Answers the unnamed questioner of the Victimhood section; no author or tradition is named."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Victimhood; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNeutralSituationsMeaning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "All situations are neutral; the meaning given creates the experience"@en, "Alle Situationen sind neutral; die gegebene Bedeutung erschafft die Erfahrung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Circumstances are neutral props with no meaning but what one gives them: positive meaning gives positive effect, and the reverse. Physical reality is a composite of all probable realities existing at once, a holographic background with no one truer reality, from which a chosen reality is called up by beliefs, attitudes and one's vibration through sympathetic synchronization; meaning gives rise to experience rather than the reverse, and giving meaning is the act of creation itself. Before birth the non-physical self gives its coming life a meaning that calls up the circumstances to represent it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Neutral Situations; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharAssigningPositiveMeaning a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Trusting a neutral setback serves a positive purpose instead of reacting in anger"@en, "Darauf vertrauen, dass ein neutraler Rückschlag einen positiven Grund hat, statt zornig zu reagieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Illustrated by a missed train: the old self curses and goes to complain about the railway; the changed person, standing on the same platform, knows everything in life has a positive reason and does not storm off. One is to recognize oneself as the definer of one's life and give each situation the meaning one prefers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Neutral Situations; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPositiveEffectsFromMeaning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Positive effects drawn from neutral circumstances"@en, "Positive Wirkungen, gewonnen aus neutralen Umständen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Extracting from a neutral circumstance the effect one desires; a life that takes on only the colouring and atmosphere of the meaning one has decided it will have."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Neutral Situations; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPositiveMeaningYieldsEffects a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Assigning positive meaning yields positive effects, as meeting a friend at the missed train"@en, "Positive Bedeutung zu geben bringt positive Wirkungen, wie das Treffen einer Freundin am verpassten Zug"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the example, the person who does not react in anger notices that a friend unseen for ten years has just left the train, and later events show the meeting was needed then for positive reasons; whoever stormed off would have missed her. In general, as one gives life meaning, it takes on only that meaning's character."@en ;
    skos:note "The train scene is a constructed example, not a reported case."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharAssigningPositiveMeaning ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharPositiveEffectsFromMeaning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Neutral Situations; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharUrgeAbsentInPreferredSelf a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Having no urge for what does not fit the preferred self, without will power"@en, "Kein Verlangen nach dem haben, was nicht zum bevorzugten Selbst passt, ohne Willenskraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Freedom from an unwanted urge, such as for a snack cake, not through will power or a struggle against oneself but because the preferred self is not of the vibration that contains the urge; the station it is tuned to does not advertise the snack."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPreferredSelfYieldsNoUrge a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Acting as the preferred being removes the unwanted urge"@en, "Als bevorzugtes Wesen zu handeln nimmt das unerwünschte Verlangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A questioner torn between eating too many snack cakes and remorse is told that if he recognizes the food is out of tune with the being he prefers and acts as that being, he will find he has no urge; this is called recognition, the ceasing of self-judgement and of the belief that change is difficult, not will power."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharActingAsThePreferredSelf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharUrgeAbsentInPreferredSelf ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLibraryAnalogy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The library analogy: awareness of all probable selves while checking out only one"@en, "Die Bibliotheksanalogie: Bewusstsein aller wahrscheinlichen Selbste, während man nur eines ausleiht"@de ;
    skos:definition "An integrated being can stay aware of every other probable reality while being the one it is: in a library one may read every book, the positive, the negative, the one about the snack, but only the one consciously checked out becomes one's reality, so there is no fight against an urge. One is never off one's path, since one is the path; the fixedness of the human condition exists only because it is believed real, and everything offers a chance to decide one's preference."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPolarityAsDensityPerspective a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Polarity as a third- and fourth-density view of a wholeness; the soul neither male nor female"@en, "Polarität als Sicht der dritten und vierten Dichte auf eine Ganzheit; die Seele weder männlich noch weiblich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Outside physical reality all polarity is one thing, and one need not see oneself as a dichotomy. Bashar's civilization, being partly physical, has polarity, but one in which each side recognizes the other's validity and works as a balanced unit; going up the scale polarity is lost in a sense, being only a third- and fourth-density perspective. His people experience the whole coin rather than two sides. The soul is neither male nor female but one thing, polarity coming into existence with physical reality; in many universes it differentiates otherwise than by positive and negative."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharCeasingSelfInvalidation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Ceasing to invalidate oneself and loving oneself unconditionally"@en, "Aufhören, sich selbst zu entwerten, und sich bedingungslos lieben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ceasing to invalidate any part of oneself, since one is the only thing one has to work with and a representation of the infinite, and allowing oneself to love oneself unconditionally, so that one knows who one is and has something to stand up for."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSelfValidationFirstStep a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Ceasing self-invalidation as the first step in creating one's reality"@en, "Das Ende der Selbstentwertung als erster Schritt zur Erschaffung der eigenen Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first step in creating reality as one desires is to stop invalidating oneself; invalidating any part keeps one from functioning as a whole being able to use constructively what comes from others, and without unconditional self-love one does not know who one is."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharCeasingSelfInvalidation ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharUnwithheldCreation ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "One cannot function as a whole being able to use what others bring constructively, and does not know who one is or have anything to stand up for." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEveryoneIsAMirror a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Everyone is a mirror, though not a one-to-one reflection of what one must work on"@en, "Jeder ist ein Spiegel, wenn auch keine genaue Abbildung dessen, woran man arbeiten muss"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every being is designed as a mirror, but what is seen in it is not exactly what one needs to work on: someone may attract invalidating people so that, by not accepting their invalidations, he shows them what it is to stand firm in his desire and gives them the chance to stand for their own beliefs, every belief being as true and valid as any other. A neighbour without one's urge likewise reflects a reality one can also choose."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 6 Life Works!, section Dual Nature; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 7, The Orchestration
#

pmc:BasharSynchronicityAsOneEvent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Synchronicity: no accidents, everything one event seen from different points of view"@en, "Synchronizität: keine Zufälle, alles ein Ereignis aus verschiedenen Blickwinkeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Nothing happens by accident; what looks like one is overlapping incidents describing the paths one has chosen to be. Synchronicity is defined as the conscious perception, in a time track of spatial reality, of everything's multidimensional existence manifesting simultaneously: the recognition that every event, object, relation and perception is the same single thing seen from another angle. Every crack in the street and leaf on a tree is there for a reason, drawn in unconsciously, though its relative importance differs from person to person, one's presence enhancing another's experience. In the propeller analogy, observers whose strobe lights flash at different timings see one propeller in different positions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Coincidence?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section The Orchestration; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTwoPointsOfControl a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The two points: everything is synchronicity; act on it with integrity"@en, "Die zwei Punkte: Alles ist Synchronizität; danach mit Integrität handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar reduces all he has taught, ideology, belief, emotion, thought, perception and interaction, to two ideas that are the mechanism of knowing oneself in control: first, that everything is synchronicity and there for a reason; second, to act with integrity on the opportunities that recognition brings. The two are called self-perpetuating, each breeding the other and accelerating into infinity, and the whole of physical reality."@en ;
    skos:note "The full-text layer prints no date and the session is undated, so the date of the compilation is left open."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Bashar through Darryl Anka, in Blueprint for Change" ;
    dcterms:date "undated in the full-text layer, which carries no imprint" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Coincidence?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section The Orchestration; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharRecognizingEverythingAsSynchronicity a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognizing everything as synchronicity and being fascinated by the orchestration"@en, "Alles als Synchronizität erkennen und sich von der Orchestrierung faszinieren lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first point: while driving, walking or doing anything, remember that every object, person, sound and interaction is there for a reason, including the car that cuts one off and the traffic jam one would call negative; marvel at how finely orchestrated everything one takes part in is; take it for granted as a knowingness and act as though what stands out is what one needs to know."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Coincidence?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section The Orchestration; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Analyzing Everything; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharActingOnSynchronicityWithIntegrity a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Acting with integrity on every opportunity synchronicity brings"@en, "Mit Integrität auf jede Gelegenheit handeln, die Synchronizität bringt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The second point: act on all the opportunities synchronicity brings, with integrity, which is glossed as integrated, blended, whole: knowing that, as part of the one thing, one has all one needs to be anything one wants without forcing opinions on others, dominating them, relying on them or making them do it for one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section The Orchestration; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Acting with Integrity; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharRecognitionBeforeAction a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognizing synchronicity as point one before acting on it as point two"@en, "Synchronizität als ersten Punkt erkennen, bevor man als zweiten Punkt danach handelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The two points are numbered, recognition first and action on the opportunities it brings second, after which each feeds the other."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharRecognizingEverythingAsSynchronicity ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:BasharActingOnSynchronicityWithIntegrity ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section The Orchestration; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharConsciousControlAndDesiredLife a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Conscious knowledge of being in control and the life one desires, in resonance with All That Is"@en, "Bewusstes Wissen, die Kontrolle zu haben, und das gewünschte Leben, im Einklang mit Allem Was Ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "The promised result of the two points: understanding consciously that one is and always was in control of one's life, creating the life one desires, being in full harmonic resonance with All That Is, consciously understood as it shows itself in physical reality, with ever more awareness of synchronicity and ever more opportunities."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Coincidence?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section The Orchestration; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Acting with Integrity; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTwoPointsYieldControl a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Recognizing synchronicity and acting on it with integrity yields the desired life and growing awareness"@en, "Synchronizität erkennen und mit Integrität danach handeln bringt das gewünschte Leben und wachsendes Gewahrsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The two points are said to be all one need do to create the desired life; acting with integrity always generates more conscious awareness of synchronicity, which brings more opportunities to act, accelerating without end, and keeps the connection to All That Is conscious, felt as acceleration rather than stagnation."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharActingOnSynchronicityWithIntegrity ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharConsciousControlAndDesiredLife ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section The Orchestration; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Acting with Integrity; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharActingWithoutIntegrityCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Warning that acting outside integrity breaks the loop between the two points"@en, "Warnung, dass Handeln ohne Integrität den Kreislauf zwischen den zwei Punkten bricht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting outside integrity is said to separate one from the whole and stop the process between recognition and action, so that acting no longer generates conscious awareness of synchronicity."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharActingOnSynchronicityWithIntegrity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Acting with Integrity; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNegativeSynchronicity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Negative synchronicity: misfortune as fulfilment of one's negative beliefs, leading to victimhood"@en, "Negative Synchronizität: Unglück als Erfüllung der eigenen negativen Überzeugungen, die zur Opferschaft führt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Everything is synchronicity, the negative too: one attracts what one believes one will act on, in the manner one will act, and negative occurrences fulfil one's negative beliefs. Negative acceleration is perceived as destruction; dissociated from the fact that all is synchronicity, one cannot see its reasons, asks why this is happening to one, and so creates victimhood. Likewise, not acting on one's instincts and what one knows true for oneself creates a reality that forces one to recognize that, often a negative one such as still hating one's job; one always reinforces the choice one makes, and this is called not a setback but a chance to learn and redefine the choice."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: no deadline and no count; the observable signs are destruction, the question why it happens to one, a job still hated; the failure is put on the person's negative beliefs and on not following instinct, and is at once reframed as the procedure working flawlessly on those beliefs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Acting with Integrity; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Planning and Free Will; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNothingHappensAsExpectation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "When one acts on synchronicity and nothing happens: expectation and fixation on mechanism"@en, "Wenn man nach Synchronizität handelt und nichts geschieht: Erwartung und Fixierung auf den Mechanismus"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked about acting on much synchronicity with nothing happening, Bashar calls the question a contradiction that sets a negative view of synchronicity beside a positive one. It always manifests as it must, perhaps not consciously, since awareness of the mechanism could fixate one like someone who analyses how to drive and is late for the appointment; it comes in the appropriate timing, and saying it should not have happened is a judgement that puts expectations on how it ought to occur and does not allow it to be synchronicity."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the case the questioner offers as failure, action without result, is not admitted as one; no deadline and no count are set, the outcome is declared to have come in some form not necessarily visible, and the only failure named is the person's own expectation and judgement of how it should have happened. Nothing observable is left by which the procedure could be found not to work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Analyzing Everything; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOverAnalysisCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Warning against analysing every synchronicity"@en, "Warnung davor, jede Synchronizität zu analysieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognizing everything as synchronicity does not mean one can analyse every aspect consciously, and that is not the aim; becoming analytical may keep one from living the experience and break it back into pieces, and fixation on the mechanism keeps one from moving. Understanding is not only conscious analysis."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharRecognizingEverythingAsSynchronicity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Analyzing Everything; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharRightPlaceRightTimeSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs: the obvious coincidence of what one needed, and sense made in retrospect"@en, "Zeichen: die offensichtliche Fügung dessen, was man brauchte, und nachträglich gewonnener Sinn"@de ;
    skos:definition "The synchronicities of highest importance will be obvious, met as the right thing at the right place and time, everything else not mattering; by moving on whatever excites one and feels correct, all past circumstances settle into place and become meaningful in retrospect, and trusting they serve one's own reason one is bound to find out at some point how they served one positively. Acting as if all is synchronicity makes it ever more obvious."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: an observable coincidence felt as just what was needed, and a sense of meaning found afterwards; the only time given is sooner or later, so no deadline; no count; judged by the person alone and in retrospect, which leaves any circumstance able to qualify."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Analyzing Everything; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharExaminingHesitation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Trusting one's instincts and examining what a hesitation brings up"@en, "Den eigenen Instinkten vertrauen und prüfen, was ein Zögern hervorbringt"@de ;
    skos:definition "One is to trust one's instincts and examine what they raise by questioning oneself: why one hesitates, what one really believes about one's situation and one's part in the shared creation, what the hesitation lets one look at in oneself and the others; learn all one can about it and apply it, then act on the choice that results."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Analyzing Everything; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharObviousChoice a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The obvious choice falling into place"@en, "Die offensichtliche Wahl, die sich von selbst ergibt"@de ;
    skos:definition "A choice that becomes evident without being forced, ready to be acted on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Analyzing Everything; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExaminingHesitationYieldsChoice a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Examining one's hesitation lets the obvious choice fall into place"@en, "Das Prüfen des eigenen Zögerns lässt die offensichtliche Wahl sich ergeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one has learned what one can from the beliefs a hesitation brings up and applied it, the obvious choice is said simply to fall into place, and one then acts on it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharExaminingHesitation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharObviousChoice ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Analyzing Everything; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPlanAndFreeWill a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Plan and free will at once, and a civilization run by synchronicity without government or economy"@en, "Plan und freier Wille zugleich, und eine Zivilisation, die durch Synchronizität ohne Regierung und Wirtschaft lebt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked whether there is a plan with free will inside it, Bashar answers that it is both at once, time and space being illusions and one more manifestation of the one thing, all occurring here and now. His own civilization lives this way and so needs neither government nor economic systems as tools: synchronicity always shows its members that they are dealing with exactly the beings they need and sharing with them the services needed at that moment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Planning and Free Will; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSymbolicReflections a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Physical reality as symbol of inner process; others as one's own versions of them"@en, "Physische Wirklichkeit als Symbol inneren Geschehens; andere als die eigene Version von ihnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Synchronicity brings symbology: everything physical is a symbolic extension of processes going on within, and one is oneself the interaction and the experience. One does interact with other consciousnesses, but what one perceives is one's own self-created version of the other, shaped as needed to reflect back what one must see about oneself, so one is always dealing with aspects of one's own consciousness. One can only attract the vibration one is equal to, so synchronicity, positive or negative, reflects only what one believes reality to be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Symbolic Reflections; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharUnderstandingRelationToMultiverse a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Understanding how one relates to the whole multiverse"@en, "Verstehen, wie man sich zum ganzen Multiversum verhält"@de ;
    skos:definition "The understanding promised to whoever takes every situation as able to be positive: how one stands in relation to the entirety of the multiverse, and how any neutral situation can serve the path one chose."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Symbolic Reflections; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPositiveAttitudeYieldsMultiverseInsight a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Adopting the view that every situation can be positive yields understanding of one's place in the multiverse"@en, "Die Sicht anzunehmen, jede Situation könne positiv sein, bringt Verständnis des eigenen Ortes im Multiversum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Trusting that whatever comes is symbolic of one's chosen path and can serve it, without assuming it negative, lets one use any neutral situation positively; as soon as one takes the attitude that any situation may be seen positively and create positive effects, one will understand how one relates to the multiverse."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharAssigningPositiveMeaning ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharUnderstandingRelationToMultiverse ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Symbolic Reflections; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPredictionAsSensingThePresent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction as sensing the present energy most likely to manifest"@en, "Vorhersage als Wahrnehmen der gegenwärtigen Energie, die sich am wahrscheinlichsten zeigt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The future can be predicted, but not as a fixed future: a prediction senses the energy of the present that has most momentum behind it, like the setting of the strobe at that moment, and the prediction can itself change the setting, every thought changing what it thinks of, as physicists are said now to understand; strong momentum makes change unlikely. Past, present and future are all now, all possible futures existing like radio programs, and the question is only which one is chosen."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section No Future; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLimboStateAsAcceleration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The limbo state: not a slowdown but perception caught up with the speed of creation"@en, "Der Schwebezustand: keine Verlangsamung, sondern eine Wahrnehmung, die das Tempo der Schöpfung eingeholt hat"@de ;
    skos:definition "A standstill with no direction more apparent than another is usually taken as waiting for what one has set up to come out. Bashar explains it with the film strip analogy: each moment is a discrete quantum, its own universe, determined by what one decides one is, and continuity is imposed by oneself; from the projectionist's view, that of the higher self or oversoul, all frames and lives exist at once and can be viewed in any order. The negative reading is that the film has slowed onto one frame; the positive is that one's perception has accelerated to the film's speed, as a strobe freezes a falling drop, so one stands in equilibrium with the pace at which one creates reality, which is a point of power. Limbo states are personal as well as collective."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section The Limbo State; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Film Strip Analogy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section A Long Limbo?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHigherSelfNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The higher self or oversoul, the projectionist of all one's lives"@en, "Das höhere Selbst oder die Überseele, der Vorführer aller eigenen Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the film strip analogy the hypothetical projectionist, for whom all frames of one's life and all one's lives exist at once and can be viewed in any order, is said to be the same as one's higher self or oversoul."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "higher self; oversoul" ;
    pm:nameRole "the projectionist of the film strip analogy, who sees all frames and all lives at once, outside linear time" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Film Strip Analogy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharActingFromThePointOfPower a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Acting in one's preferred direction from the limbo state, seen as the point of power"@en, "Aus dem als Kraftpunkt verstandenen Schwebezustand in die bevorzugte Richtung handeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one finds oneself in a seeming standstill, one is to regard it as the point of power and not wait for something to happen: act in one's direction of preference, as the embodiment of the reality one prefers, moving the events of one's life gently where one wants them; an individual can do this within a collective limbo as well."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Film Strip Analogy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Balanced Inertia; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section A Long Limbo?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBalancedInertia a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Balanced inertia: moving any event in one's life gently in any direction"@en, "Ausgeglichene Trägheit: jedes Ereignis des eigenen Lebens sanft in jede Richtung bewegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In equilibrium with one's rate of creating reality, everything moves at one's own pace, so no inertia need be overcome and events can be pushed gently in any preferred direction; this is called the secret of the martial arts, where a small person moves a larger one by matching his speed at one moment. At infinite speed one is everywhere at once and seems still, and all events can be moved effortlessly as extensions of oneself. Bashar insists he speaks literally and physically, not figuratively."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Balanced Inertia; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Infinite Speed; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPointOfPowerYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Acting from the point of power makes things fall into place at once"@en, "Aus dem Kraftpunkt zu handeln lässt die Dinge sofort an ihren Platz fallen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting in the preferred direction while in the limbo state is said to make things fall into place in one's life immediately and synchronistically; the seeming standstill is when the most magical and fastest things can happen."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharActingFromThePointOfPower ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharBalancedInertia ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Balanced Inertia; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section A Long Limbo?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharImmediateFallingIntoPlace a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Things falling into place at once after acting from the limbo state"@en, "Dinge fallen sofort an ihren Platz, nachdem man aus dem Schwebezustand handelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "What one is to see after acting in the direction of preference from the limbo state: events falling into place in one's life immediately and synchronistically, and in one's personal world things changing even within a collective limbo."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the one sign in the chapter with a time attached, immediately; an observable outcome in the person's own affairs, with no count; the chapter supplies its own explanation should it not come, the person standing and waiting."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Balanced Inertia; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section A Long Limbo?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharWaitingInLimbo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Waiting for something to happen keeps the limbo state a standstill"@en, "Darauf zu warten, dass etwas geschieht, hält den Schwebezustand im Stillstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one reads the limbo state as one's life slowing down, one waits for something to happen and takes no action; the only reason the point of power may seem not to work is that one stands there waiting. A collective limbo may last longer if the individual does not act."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: no deadline and no count; the mark is observable inaction, and the failure is put on the person who reads the standstill negatively and waits."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Film Strip Analogy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Balanced Inertia; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section A Long Limbo?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFearOfOwnPowerCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Warning that one may shrink from the power one finds, and that the last little step is the hardest"@en, "Warnung, dass man vor der gefundenen Macht zurückschrecken kann und der letzte kleine Schritt der schwerste ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says, not to set the hearers up, that the only thing that would make them hesitate at the point of power is fear of the power they finally see they have, and backing off from it; one is said to be a hair's breadth from having everything one wants, and the final small step is the most difficult because one has been taught again and again that it cannot be so easy and one cannot be so powerful. Creating daily reality is so natural that one has forgotten one's responsibility for it; recognizing one's power needs no swollen ego."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharActingFromThePointOfPower ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Balanced Inertia; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Infinite Speed; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharCreationGodNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Creation, God, All That Is: the one thing of which all are aspects"@en, "Schöpfung, Gott, Alles Was Ist: das eine Ding, dessen Aspekte alle sind"@de ;
    skos:definition "The one fundamental thing that everything is, holographically, each part containing the whole as each cell holds the information for a body, is called Creation or God; humans are aspects and mirrors of Creation, made in God's image, meaning they echo God, God's dreams, hands and instruments, the ways Creation expresses itself inside itself. All That Is names the same whole as it expresses itself in physical reality."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Creation; God; All That Is" ;
    pm:nameRole "the single holographic whole of which every being and thing is an aspect, which gives free will and does not control it" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Acting with Integrity; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section The Orchestration; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Infinite Speed; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFreeWillWithoutDivineControl a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Free will as being made in God's image, against those who say Creation also controls one's life"@en, "Freier Wille als Gottebenbildlichkeit, gegen jene, die sagen, die Schöpfung lenke zugleich das eigene Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "As aspects of the Infinite, humans have been charged with creating their immediate reality as they wish, which is why they have free will; Bashar finds it contradictory that some members of Earth society insist Creation gave free will and then sought to control lives with its own will. Having free will and creating any reality one desires is what being made in God's image means."@en ;
    skos:note "The other side is named only as some members of society, from conversations with a few hearers; no author, church or tradition is named, so it is not entered as a dispute with a named party."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Infinite Speed; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharActingAsMadeInGodsImage a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Acting as one made in God's image, creating any reality one desires"@en, "Als nach Gottes Bild Geschaffener handeln und jede gewünschte Wirklichkeit erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting as a being with free will who can create any reality desired, balanced with all things and knowing everything is an extension of oneself that moves in the direction one allows because one says so."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Infinite Speed; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHeavenOnEarth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heaven on Earth"@en, "Der Himmel auf Erden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state promised, with a guarantee, to those who act as beings bearing the image of God."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Infinite Speed; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharGodsImageYieldsHeaven a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Acting as made in God's image yields heaven on Earth, guaranteed"@en, "Als nach Gottes Bild Geschaffener zu handeln bringt den Himmel auf Erden, garantiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar tells the hearers to act as beings with free will who can create any reality, which is being made in God's image, and they will have heaven on their Earth, which he guarantees."@en ;
    skos:note "Guaranteed without date, count or sign by which it would be recognized."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharActingAsMadeInGodsImage ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharHeavenOnEarth ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section Infinite Speed; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharIndividualExampleSpeedsCollective a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Creating one's desired reality now speeds the collective change"@en, "Die gewünschte Wirklichkeit jetzt zu erschaffen beschleunigt den kollektiven Wandel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even in a collective limbo one can have all one desires in one's personal reality now; the more one creates it, the faster one becomes a living example of the reality others can create together, speeding up the whole process, since one individual can affect the whole planet, as hearers are said to have seen many times."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharLivingAsTheExampleOfThePreferredWorld ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharArrivingAtThePeacefulEarth ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section A Long Limbo?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharServingEachOtherInJoy a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Serving one another, creating a reality of joy and being fully who one is"@en, "Einander dienen, eine Wirklichkeit der Freude erschaffen und ganz der sein, der man ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognizing that one can serve others and make a joyful reality, and being willing to be wholly what one truly is: creative, spontaneous and loving, rather than one's idea of what one ought to be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section A Long Limbo?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharInteractionWithBasharsRace a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Open interaction with Bashar's people and the blending of the two races"@en, "Offene Begegnung mit Bashars Volk und das Verschmelzen der beiden Rassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The prospect held out: Bashar's people interacting with humanity and the two races blending into a larger civilization that goes on exploring creation ecstatically without end; Bashar says no end has been found in thousands of years and thousands of civilizations. His people will be with humans whatever reality they choose, but the reality chosen determines how they can interact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section A Long Limbo?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharJoyBeforeInteraction a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "A reality of mutual service and joy, and being one's genuine self, before interaction with Bashar's people"@en, "Eine Wirklichkeit gegenseitigen Dienstes und der Freude, und das echte Selbst, vor der Begegnung mit Bashars Volk"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recognizing that humans can serve one another and make a joyful reality opens the invitation Bashar's people need in order to interact and blend; they welcome sharing creation only if humans are willing to be fully what they are, otherwise they would be dealing only with an idea of what one ought to be."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharServingEachOtherInJoy ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharInteractionWithBasharsRace ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without the invitation Bashar's people cannot interact with humans, and if humans are not fully themselves the interaction is only with their illusions and delusions of self." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 7 The Orchestration, section A Long Limbo?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 8, Welcome to Fourth Density
#

pmc:BasharFoundationAndSeedIdea a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Two years of teaching as soil for a single crystalline seed idea"@en, "Zwei Jahre Lehre als Boden für eine einzige kristalline Saatidee"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says the ideas shared over the past two years, that one creates reality, creates past and future from the present, that moments are unconnected, that time and memory are present creations, that imagination and dreams are real, that what is called sanity is merely an insanity the mass has agreed on, and that prophecies, rituals and tools stay valid, have laid a foundation co-created by the hearers' allowance. Into it a single idea is now to be planted, so far given only subconsciously, which works not against anyone's will but at each one's own timing and willingness, and on which the coming revelation hinges; no one need have heard the earlier ideas, since being present shows one is where one should be, and one never hears what one is not ready to hear."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section opening section, before the first heading; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharThoughtRewiresTheBrain a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Every thought rewires the brain, and no brain can study another objectively"@en, "Jeder Gedanke verdrahtet das Gehirn neu, und kein Gehirn kann ein Gehirn objektiv erforschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says he told the hearers, and their scientists have since found, that every thought physically changes the brain's pathways, creating new ones and removing old ones; revelation is the conscious recognition of many levels aligning at once, a near total rewiring from which one emerges a new person, as in truth one is in every moment. Brains are wired by beliefs and see only what they are wired to see, so a brain studying a brain cannot be objective; only changing one's idea of oneself rewires it to perceive the reality one is blind to. Physicality is the product of consciousness, not the other way round; neurophysiologists will understand only when they include consciousness, since nothing is ever found analytically, analysis only retracing what consciousness already knows."@en ;
    skos:note "The scientists and neurophysiologists are not named and no study is cited."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section opening section, before the first heading; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Being the Dimension; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharPresentNotResultOfPastExercise a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The seed phrase exercise: one's present does not stem from one's past"@en, "Die Übung des Saatsatzes: ‚deine Gegenwart ist nicht das Ergebnis deiner Vergangenheit‘"@de ;
    skos:definition "A guided exercise given to the audience: all shut their eyes, relax and breathe in deeply; feel whatever feelings are there, fear included, live, love and enjoy them; take two more deep breaths; relax into the imagination and attend while the phrase denying that one's present stems from one's past is spoken four times, the last time loudly; take a deep breath and two more, then open the eyes and emerge into one's natural state. Bashar says the phrase is not hypnosis and is not implanted against anyone's will; it is let into conscious recognition, to be used as and when each wishes."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section opening section, before the first heading; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBreakingWithThirdDensity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cutting the tie to the third density: a rewired brain and a changed physical reality"@en, "Den Bruch mit der dritten Dichte vollziehen: ein neu verdrahtetes Gehirn und eine veränderte physische Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The promised result of the seed idea: a revelation that lets one finally perceive physically one's own transition into fourth density, physical reality changing as it has not for thousands of years, possibly in an instant; an energy explosion that rewires the brain from the inside out so that perceived reality reflects it, fourth density complete; the tie to the third density cut once and for all."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section opening section, before the first heading; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSeedPhraseYieldsFourthDensity a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Understanding emotionally that one's present does not stem from one's past breaks with the third density"@en, "Emotional zu verstehen, dass die Gegenwart nicht das Ergebnis der Vergangenheit ist, bricht mit der dritten Dichte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once one lets the understanding that one's present does not stem from one's past explode emotionally and experientially, one is said to cut the tie to the third density for good; when this recognition is fully allowed, physical reality will change, at one's own timing and willingness, perhaps in an instant. The seed is called the key and the fulcrum: if one understands it, one's reality will change."@en ;
    skos:note "The text sets the result on the hearer's allowance and timing, and says different people will understand at different times without reason for judgement; no date or measure is given."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharPresentNotResultOfPastExercise ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharBreakingWithThirdDensity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section opening section, before the first heading; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharUnderstoodButNotFelt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Understanding the phrase intellectually but feeling no different is not a failure"@en, "Den Satz verstandesmäßig zu verstehen, aber sich nicht anders zu fühlen, ist kein Scheitern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar foresees that many will say they understand the words but feel no different, and calls this all right: it is how their imagination accepts the idea for now, and the seed will be there and will explode later."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the obvious sign that the exercise did not work, feeling no different, is named in advance and declared not to be one; no deadline is set for the later explosion, no count, and no observable by which its absence could ever be established."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section opening section, before the first heading; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNoNeedForMemorySign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs of the break: no need for memory, and learning by process giving way to knowing in the moment"@en, "Zeichen des Bruchs: kein Bedarf an Erinnerung, und das Lernen im Prozess weicht dem Wissen im Augenblick"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the break one will have experiences in physical reality reflecting that one no longer needs memory, since one will know what one needs in any present situation; one will begin to lose the methods one calls learning, understanding that one need not learn by process what one can know by living it in the moment. One will not exactly forget anything but will relate to a past event differently, disconnected emotionally, as one more way to experience the present."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: no deadline and no count; an inner and behavioural change observed by the person, the loss of reliance on memory and on learning; the closing note of the chapter repeats it as forgetting one's past and tells the hearer not to fear it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section opening section, before the first heading; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Being the Dimension; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPresentNotResultOfPast a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The present does not stem from the past; the past is created from the present"@en, "Die Gegenwart ist nicht das Ergebnis der Vergangenheit; die Vergangenheit wird aus der Gegenwart erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One keeps recreating oneself as a person with habitual patterns from the past, moment after moment, but need not keep that definition. The present results from what one now thinks it results from; believing it results from the past creates that effect now, together with all the linear continuity that supports one's theory of who one is. Change the theory and one experiences only what supports the new one. Past and future are both created from now, the only time one ever exists, and have as many probable versions as each other; who one is now decides which past one perceives as real. In fourth density one will still relate to linear time, perhaps no longer at its end."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section opening section, before the first heading; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Only Now; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Being the Dimension; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBeliefInPastKeepsThirdDensity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Whoever believes his past produced him remains in the third density"@en, "Wer glaubt, das Ergebnis seiner Vergangenheit zu sein, bleibt in der dritten Dichte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked whether someone who thinks his past produced him is right, Bashar agrees and says such a person will mirror that idea by staying in the third density; whoever is creative enough to define a reality in which he may believe anything and still be where he wants will be there, and will probably simplify his definitions bit by bit."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: no deadline and no count; the mark is a belief the person holds, and the failure, staying in the third density, is placed on that belief and so on the person."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Only Now; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAcclimationSymptoms a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bodily symptoms read as acclimation to the fourth-density energy"@en, "Körperliche Symptome, gedeutet als Gewöhnung an die Energie der vierten Dichte"@de ;
    skos:definition "The fourth-density experience is called more rarefied, a higher degree of energy. Many acclimating to it while still thinking they live in the third density, and comparing it with what they think their bodies can bear, feel it as fevers, flushing, rushes of adrenaline or anxiety, pain in the spine, shoulder blades or base of the neck, migraines, sinus pressure, palpitations, anxiety in the solar plexus, disorientation, tiredness. There is not more energy than before, only more awareness of it. Disorientation is the time taken to grow used to the new level, literally a dis-illusionment as old definitions dissolve; these are fourth-density symptoms couched in old terms, one way to know one is changing, and seem slow only through remnants of reliance on process."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: observable bodily symptoms, a list of them, taken in advance as signs that transformation is under way; no deadline and no count; the text tells the hearer not to fear and says they will work themselves through, and gives no criterion for telling such symptoms from illness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Acclimating; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharReorientingThroughClearIntention a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Reorienting through clear intention, definition, desire, deservability and action"@en, "Neuorientierung durch klare Absicht, Definition, Begierde, Würdigkeit und Handlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Against disorientation one is to have clarity of intention, definition, desire, deservability and action; to use the energy and the limbo state for defining one's preference, and then to act accordingly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Acclimating; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharQuickReorientation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Quick reorientation and alignment in the new energy"@en, "Rasche Neuorientierung und Ausrichtung in der neuen Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being aligned and reoriented quickly into the new reality after the disorientation of acclimation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Acclimating; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharClearIntentionYieldsReorientation a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Clear intention and action reorient one quickly"@en, "Klare Absicht und Handlung orientieren einen rasch neu"@de ;
    skos:definition "Clarity of intention, definition, desire, deservability and action is said to reorient one very quickly; defining one's preference and acting on it aligns and reorients one."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharReorientingThroughClearIntention ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharQuickReorientation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Acclimating; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDensitiesScale a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The scale of densities: third, fourth as last physical, fifth to seventh non-physical, then another octave"@en, "Die Skala der Dichten: dritte, vierte als letzte physische, fünfte bis siebte nichtphysisch, dann eine andere Oktave"@de ;
    skos:definition "Density is called a colloquial term for dimensions of experience, meaning frequencies of existence, a higher density being faster and less material, as some light is visible and some not by its vibration. Earth is passing from third to fourth density, the last level at which one can be accelerated and still physical; Bashar's civilization is passing from fourth to fifth, which is non-physical; above it non-physical states rise to the seventh, after which comes a different octave of dimensional experience his people are only beginning to explore. Fourth density is synchronous congruence with the higher self while still somewhat separate, fifth is becoming the higher self. Passing from level to level is realizing that one is the dimension one thought one lived in; since one exists on every level at once, the twelfth included, the linear order is a third-density view. The progression is said never to end."@en ;
    skos:note "The full-text layer prints no date and the session is undated, so the date of the compilation is left open."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Bashar through Darryl Anka, in Blueprint for Change" ;
    dcterms:date "undated in the full-text layer, which carries no imprint" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Acclimating; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Being the Dimension; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section All Together; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Enjoy the Third; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBeingTheDimension a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fourth density as realizing one is the creator and is physical reality itself"@en, "Die vierte Dichte als Erkenntnis, dass man Schöpfer und selbst die physische Wirklichkeit ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "The fourth-density change is where one begins to realize one creates one's reality: physical reality is one's projection, made of oneself, and one is it. Paradoxically each individual will experience becoming the whole dimension and absorbing all others, all sharing that experience since the universe is holographic and every point of view holds everywhere. Every being is a God-thought, a way God thinks, expresses and experiences itself; humans are God manifest as individuals. Fourth density is summed up as knowing there is no objectivity, taking responsibility for creating one's reality and acting as if one does, recognizing all as synchronicity and acting on it; the unconscious dissolves, one knows what one needs when one needs it, fears nothing and sees nothing hidden or occult."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Being the Dimension; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section All Together; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharShiftingToAParallelDimension a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "A questioner's method: closing the eyes and deciding one is in a different dimension"@en, "Die Methode eines Fragenden: die Augen schließen und entscheiden, man sei in einer anderen Dimension"@de ;
    skos:definition "A questioner reports that, applying what he heard about parallel dimensions, whenever he met a situation he did not prefer he shut his eyes and decided he had entered another dimension, then opened them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Being the Dimension; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPreferenceManifestInAnotherDimension a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Finding one's preference manifest on opening the eyes, even a cleared traffic jam"@en, "Beim Öffnen der Augen die eigene Vorliebe verwirklicht finden, sogar einen aufgelösten Stau"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being, on opening one's eyes, in a dimension where one's preference is manifest, reported to extend even to altering a freeway traffic jam."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Being the Dimension; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDimensionShiftYieldsPreference a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Deciding one is in another dimension brings one's preference about, as a questioner reports"@en, "Zu entscheiden, man sei in einer anderen Dimension, bringt die eigene Vorliebe hervor, wie ein Fragender berichtet"@de ;
    skos:definition "The questioner says that on opening his eyes he found himself in another dimension with his preference manifested, quite outstandingly, even in a jam on the freeway. Bashar affirms that all possibilities exist, physical reality's ebb and flow being illusion, and agrees that it works because the mass consciousness, which once allowed only processes, now allows instantaneousness."@en ;
    skos:note "A questioner's report of a result, affirmed by Bashar; the report gives no number of trials and no failures."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharShiftingToAParallelDimension ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharPreferenceManifestInAnotherDimension ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Being the Dimension; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharLivingEachMomentAsTheFirst a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Living each moment as new, for the first time, and letting time be joyful"@en, "Jeden Augenblick als neu, zum ersten Mal, leben und die Zeit freudvoll sein lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One is to understand that every moment is literally new, continuity being an illusion, and act like a child who notices an opportunity and acts on it regardless of where or when, as Bashar says his people meet each session as if for the first time; to let whatever time one creates be experienced in full joy, not waiting for something else, and to drop worry about past and future."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Being in the Moment; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Creating Less Time; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Fourth Density Life; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLessTimeLongerLifespan a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Experiencing less time and spanning the ages: longer lifespans"@en, "Weniger Zeit erleben und die Zeitalter überspannen: längere Lebensspannen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Losing track of when it is, being where one needs to be when one needs to be there, years and centuries passing like a day; lifespans increasing, which is said to be not having more time but creating less of it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Creating Less Time; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Fourth Density Life; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLivingInMomentYieldsLessTime a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Living in the moment creates less time and lengthens life"@en, "Im Augenblick zu leben erschafft weniger Zeit und verlängert das Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one lets the time one creates be experienced in full joy, one paradoxically experiences less of it, since only waiting creates the time in between; the more one lives in the now, the less one experiences time itself, so that lifespans increase and one spans the ages."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharLivingEachMomentAsTheFirst ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharLessTimeLongerLifespan ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Creating Less Time; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Fourth Density Life; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLinearPlanningCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Warning that planning to do something for a set period makes it wind down"@en, "Warnung, dass die Planung, etwas für eine bestimmte Dauer zu tun, es auslaufen lässt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Saying one will do something for two or three months sets one up to experience it linearly, which makes it run down; Bashar's people do not plan how many sessions the channelling will take, but follow the flow and act when it changes direction."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharLivingEachMomentAsTheFirst ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Being in the Moment; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharSeeingHesitationAsSpontaneous a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing everything, hesitation and planning included, as spontaneous creation"@en, "Alles, auch Zögern und Planen, als spontane Schöpfung sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "From one chosen point of view everyone is always spontaneous, even in hesitating; one is to regard everything in life, planning and hesitation included, as a spontaneous creation of the moment, if that is what one desires."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Creating Less Time; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSpontaneousUnfolding a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A life that unfolds spontaneously, with opportunities met spontaneously"@en, "Ein Leben, das sich spontan entfaltet, mit spontan ergriffenen Gelegenheiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Manifesting physically in a more spontaneous way: opportunities coming and being acted on spontaneously, everything seen to be redefined so."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Creating Less Time; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSpontaneityAttitudeYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing hesitation as spontaneity makes life unfold spontaneously"@en, "Zögern als Spontaneität zu sehen lässt das Leben sich spontan entfalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking even hesitation as one more form of spontaneity is said to let one manifest physically in a more spontaneous way, the attitude deciding how life unfolds, how opportunities come and how one acts on them; one will see the result in one's actions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharSeeingHesitationAsSpontaneous ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharSpontaneousUnfolding ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Creating Less Time; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharDivingIntoTheBlock a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Diving into a block: asking what one must believe to experience it so, and absorbing its information"@en, "In eine Blockade eintauchen: fragen, was man glauben muss, um sie so zu erleben, und ihre Information aufnehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one feels stuck, one is not to read it as stasis but as part of the process, dive into it to learn which part, and simply do the next thing; a block is one only if treated as something to go around rather than through. When something seems a block, find out what one would have to believe to experience it that way and what information it brings, as a present in unexpected wrapping, and absorb it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Creating Less Time; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBlockUnfoldsAsPath a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A block passing quickly and unfolding as a clear direction"@en, "Eine Blockade, die rasch vorübergeht und sich als klare Richtung entfaltet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Passing through the feeling of being stuck very quickly, and seeing what was called a block unfold as a direction or path, obviously and clearly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Creating Less Time; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDivingInYieldsPath a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Diving into a block lets it pass and unfold as a path"@en, "In eine Blockade einzutauchen lässt sie vorübergehen und sich als Weg entfalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Once one dives in one is experiencing it, so it goes right through one and is soon over; absorbing the information a block brings makes it unfold as a direction and path, in a very obvious way."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharDivingIntoTheBlock ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharBlockUnfoldsAsPath ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Creating Less Time; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFrictionPain a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pain from the friction of two vibrations, born of judging the third density as less"@en, "Schmerz aus der Reibung zweier Schwingungen, entstanden aus dem Urteil, die dritte Dichte sei geringer"@de ;
    skos:definition "The symptoms of the move into fourth density come from retaining connections to the third. Approaching the fourth density with a third-density outlook, society has created the belief that third-density beings vibrate slower, a remnant of judging the third as less; holding the fourth as higher while thinking oneself still slower sets two vibrations in one body, and their friction causes pain."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the sign is observable, bodily pain during the transition; no deadline and no count; the cause is put on the person's comparison and self-judgement."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Third Density Pain; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharDroppingDensityComparison a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing one is what one needs to be at each moment, without comparing less and more"@en, "Wissen, dass man in jedem Augenblick ist, was man sein muss, ohne Vergleich von weniger und mehr"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing that at any moment one is what one is, and that this is what one needs to be, and so making no comparison between something one thinks is less and something one thinks is more."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Third Density Pain; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPainlessAcceleration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Accelerating as one smooth vibration, without friction or pain"@en, "Als eine gleichmäßige Schwingung beschleunigen, ohne Reibung und Schmerz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Becoming a single vibration that accelerates smoothly, the friction erased and no pain left."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Third Density Pain; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNoComparisonYieldsNoPain a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping the comparison of densities ends the friction and the pain"@en, "Den Vergleich der Dichten aufzugeben beendet die Reibung und den Schmerz"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one knows one is what one needs to be at every moment and makes no comparison between less and more, one accelerates as one smooth vibration, erases the friction and has no pain."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharDroppingDensityComparison ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharPainlessAcceleration ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Third Density Pain; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTransformationSickness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transformation sickness: a questioner's attacks diagnosed as fourth-density disease"@en, "Transformationskrankheit: die Anfälle einer Fragenden als Krankheit der vierten Dichte gedeutet"@de ;
    skos:definition "A questioner reports some three months in which every moment felt like a fascinating leap from a cliff, then morbid thoughts, the news turning ugly and malevolent, a night when every dichotomy returned, racing heart, near fainting, parts of the body seeming to vanish, paramedics who did nothing, a hospital visit finding no heart attack, shrinking from sun and moon, and later racing heart and faintness while driving. Asked whether she is ill, Bashar says yes: symptoms of transformation sickness, fourth-density disease, arising because acceleration to infinite speeds can, through belief systems, make one lose sight of what one came to exemplify, so one meets the polarity of the ecstasy."@en ;
    skos:note "A third-party report of symptoms within the session. The text attributes them to transformation and names as the remedy only living and ceasing to judge; it does not say whether medical care should be sought, though the questioner reports she was examined at a hospital."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section A Strange Disease; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharBefriendingFear a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Living, ceasing to judge, and making a friend of one's fear"@en, "Leben, aufhören zu urteilen und sich mit der eigenen Angst anfreunden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The remedy given for transformation sickness: to live and stop judging what happens as negative; to make a friend of one's fear, which is there to show something, accept the message it brings and integrate it as part of oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section A Strange Disease; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharGroundedEcstasy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A balanced state: ecstasy together with groundedness enough to help others"@en, "Ein ausgeglichener Zustand: Ekstase zusammen mit genug Erdung, um anderen zu helfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Blending the two poles into a balanced being equally at ease in the fourth-density state, remaining grounded enough in ecstasy to assist others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section A Strange Disease; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBefriendingFearYieldsBalance a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Befriending fear and integrating its message yields grounded ecstasy"@en, "Sich mit der Angst anzufreunden und ihre Botschaft zu integrieren bringt geerdete Ekstase"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accepting and integrating the message of fear lets one know that in ecstasy one will stay grounded enough to help others, blending the dichotomies into a balanced state at ease in fourth density."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharBefriendingFear ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharGroundedEcstasy ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section A Strange Disease; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFourthDensityFaculties a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fourth-density faculties: lighter bodies, auras seen, no disease, leaving the body at will"@en, "Fähigkeiten der vierten Dichte: leichtere Körper, gesehene Auren, keine Krankheit, den Körper nach Belieben verlassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "What the transformation is said to bring: bodies held less by gravity, which one may choose to symbolize on the bathroom scale; things brighter and colours clearer; sight of energies now invisible, of auric fields, of an ethereal magnetic field and of the fields linking the planet's consciousness; no disease, less sleep and food; seeing physical reality as one's own projection; going in and out of the body at will; no further need to reincarnate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Fourth Density Life; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFourthDensityForecast a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Forecasts for fourth-density Earth, with dated figures for embodiment and population"@en, "Vorhersagen für die Erde der vierten Dichte, mit datierten Zahlen zu Verkörperung und Bevölkerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar perceives that human civilization need stay physically embodied only some further two or three thousand years before going on to other realms. Humans will create their dreams on Earth, interact with many other civilizations, reshape parts of the world into pleasing forms and stop building on many, build in space and explore space, time and other levels, and share a very few bodies when they wish a brief physical experience. Within a thousand years the population will likely, not absolutely, be down to fifty million; in sixty years the trend from about six billion may start turning downward. The planet is not overpopulated, land being only unequally apportioned; numbers fall as reincarnation ends and lives lengthen, many staying as non-physical support for those still physical. Night dreams, daydreams and waking will become one experience, as for his people, who never sleep since they live in the dream."@en ;
    skos:note "Testable predictions with dates, counted from the unstated date of the session: a falling population trend from about six billion within sixty years, about fifty million within a thousand years (called likely, not absolute), and physical embodiment ending within two to three thousand years. The sixty-year figure is hedged ('may be beginning')."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Fourth Density Life; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNoBlamingSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No longer blaming or pointing fingers as the beginning of fourth density"@en, "Nicht mehr beschuldigen und mit Fingern zeigen als Beginn der vierten Dichte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked whether someone who has stopped blaming and pointing fingers has more or less reached fourth density, Bashar says this will be its beginning, the start of the willingness to know consciously that one is in it, to be followed by physiological, energetic and social changes one can witness along the way."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: an observable change of conduct in the person, judged by himself or others; no deadline and no count."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section All Together; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPercentagesCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Warning that asking what proportion will pass into fourth density causes separation"@en, "Warnung, dass die Frage, welcher Anteil in die vierte Dichte übergeht, Trennung erzeugt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asking what percentage of people will go into fourth density is said to cause separation and to be meaningless: everyone who chooses fourth density will be in it, and all who choose third will be in third; choices erase any percentage the moment they are made, so it changes constantly. Humanity moves within a bubble of acceptability and enters fourth density together, though some are personally ahead. One can share the idea with anyone one meets, since the meeting shows one can."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharLivingEachMomentAsTheFirst ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Fourth Density Life; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section All Together; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharInvalidatingThirdDensity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not enjoying the third density keeps one in it"@en, "Die dritte Dichte nicht zu genießen hält einen in ihr"@de ;
    skos:definition "To a questioner who has not enjoyed the third density, Bashar says she is likely to stay in it until she realizes it can be enjoyed: invalidating an experience one has chosen means one does not get from it what one can, and usually keeps one there until one understands why one chose it. Only the taught belief that it is unpleasant makes it so; no limitation is inherently negative, even the twelfth density being a focus and so a limit."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: no deadline and no count; the mark is the person's own displeasure with physical life, and the failure, staying in the third density, is put on that displeasure as a taught belief."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Enjoy the Third; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharEnjoyingTheThirdDensity a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Enjoying the third density and knowing oneself to be it"@en, "Die dritte Dichte genießen und sich selbst als sie erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Realizing one can enjoy the third density absolutely and in every way, even soar with exuberance in it; giving neutral circumstances the meaning one prefers; thinking of oneself as the third density and the physical universe, from the standpoint of the level one already is; and remembering that the body exists in consciousness and not consciousness in the body, so one can widen and disperse one's point of view."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Enjoy the Third; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharCognitionOfAllLevels a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Cognition of existing on all levels at once: twelfth density and heaven on Earth"@en, "Erkenntnis, auf allen Ebenen zugleich zu existieren: zwölfte Dichte und Himmel auf Erden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing that one already exists on every other level, drawing on the totality of spirit and soul one is so that no level overwhelms, having the future and all levels accelerate into present experience, and, being in control of what one experiences the physical universe to be, heaven on Earth, the twelfth density on Earth; also greater mobility through a dispersed point of view."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Enjoy the Third; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEnjoyingThirdYieldsAllLevels a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Enjoying the third density is the quickest way to the twelfth"@en, "Die dritte Dichte zu genießen ist der schnellste Weg zur zwölften"@de ;
    skos:definition "The quickest way to the twelfth level is said to be realizing one can wholly enjoy the third; becoming ecstatic in it is when one will recognize that one already exists on all the other levels, a shift of perspective and not a climb out of a mire; enjoying where one is, living in the present, is what lets all levels accelerate most quickly into the present."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharEnjoyingTheThirdDensity ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharCognitionOfAllLevels ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section Enjoy the Third; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharIncreasingSynchronicitySign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "From now on: increasing synchronicity and perhaps forgetting the past"@en, "Von nun an: zunehmende Synchronizität und vielleicht das Vergessen der Vergangenheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the chapter's closing note Bashar tells the hearers that from this point on, at their own rate and timing, they will begin to notice synchronicity increasing in their lives, an ecstatic burst of coincidence, and perhaps begin to forget their past, which they are not to fear, since it lets them live in the moment knowing what they need when they need it; he welcomes them to fourth density."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: a starting point is fixed, from this point forward, but the pace is left to each hearer, so no deadline; no count; the increase in coincidence is to be noticed by the hearer himself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 8 Welcome to Fourth Density, section closing note after the last section; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 9, Follow Your Excitement
#

pmc:BasharFundamentalPurpose a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The fundamental purpose: to be fully the self one designed oneself to be"@en, "Der grundlegende Zweck: ganz das Selbst zu sein, als das man sich entworfen hat"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked for the purpose of a questioner's life, Bashar answers that projects and services are only chosen ways of expressing a purpose, not the purpose itself. Everything without exception is chosen, birth included; the basic purpose of each person is to be the person they designed, which means doing what excites them most and serving by doing it. Since a soul has many lifetimes but each is a unique expression, the self of this life has one chance at being itself and will not be it again; everything beyond that, the method and the point of view, is left to the person in the body."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section opening, before Only One Life; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Only One Life; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHigherSelfPredestination a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Predestination limited to being here: the higher self chooses the hallway, the person chooses how to walk it"@en, "Vorherbestimmung beschränkt auf das Hiersein: das höhere Selbst wählt den Flur, der Mensch wie er ihn geht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being in physical reality was the higher self's decision, and that single fact is nearly all of what is usually meant by predestination. Some broad themes may have been set before birth in a non-physical state, but they show only as general themes; how the life is lived is decided by the physical person, an emissary sent into physical reality as into a foreign country. Bashar's image is a hallway chosen by the whole self, down which one may run, crawl, walk backwards or look into every door."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Only One Life; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExcitementAsSignal a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Excitement as the physical translation of the vibration of one's chosen path"@en, "Begeisterung als körperliche Übersetzung der Schwingung des gewählten Weges"@de ;
    skos:definition "Excitement, the sensation or knowing a person feels, is said mechanically to be the bodily rendering of the vibration that represents the path that person chose for this life. It is the sign people ask the universe for while they are too busy searching to notice it; a thing excites because it is aligned with who one is. Excitement need not mean jumping about: a calm knowing, a steady conviction or certainty can stand for the same vibration of alignment with the chosen path. Bashar insists this is mechanics and not an airy philosophy."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Give Me a Sign; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Finding A Career; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section No Excitement; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharThreeMessagesOfExcitement a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The three things excitement tells: it is you, it is effortless, it brings abundance"@en, "Die drei Botschaften der Begeisterung: das bist du, es ist mühelos, es bringt Fülle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar numbers what the most exciting thing in a situation tells a person. One: it shows what and who one is, and to act on it. Two: because it is you, if acted on with conviction and trust it becomes the most effortless thing you ever do; struggle and pain come only from trying to be someone else. Three: because it is you and effortless, it will support you most abundantly so that you can keep doing it in an ever expanding spiral, attracting the opportunities for it."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Bashar through Darryl Anka, in Blueprint for Change" ;
    dcterms:date "undated in the full-text layer, which carries no imprint" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Give Me a Sign; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Abundance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharFollowYourExcitement a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Following one's excitement: acting at each moment on what excites most, with integrity"@en, "Der eigenen Begeisterung folgen: in jedem Augenblick mit Integrität tun, was am meisten begeistert"@de ;
    skos:definition "The book's central procedure. At any moment one acts, with all available integrity, on whatever is then the most exciting thing one can imagine doing, without needing to know the most exciting career of one's whole life; it is kept in the present. Where several things excite equally, one acts on whichever, and the choice will show which was the stronger. One does something about those one can do something about, and when one can do no more there, looks round to see whether the point reached has made others possible, so that step by step all are brought up to the same level. Integrity here means acting as one whole and not as a set of compartments. A questioner who loves to dance is told that if she keeps acting as a dancer from now on she will have the life of one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Give Me a Sign; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Finding A Career; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEffortlessness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Effortless creation"@en, "Mühelose Schöpfung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state promised for doing what one is: action without struggle or pain, because one is being oneself and not fighting the flow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Give Me a Sign; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Abundance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAbundance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Abundance: being able to do what one needs and wants, when one wants"@en, "Fülle: die Fähigkeit, zu tun, was man braucht und will, wann man es will"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar defines abundance as nothing more than the ability to do what one needs and wants when one wants; money is one valid tool for it but neither the only one nor always the quickest. Abundance takes the path of least resistance, like electricity, and a broader definition lets more of its forms arrive: trading, making, winning, receiving a gift, borrowing, renting. Two people with unequal money who can each do what they need when they need it are equally abundant. Everyone is said to deserve unlimited amounts of what they want."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Abundance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Struggle or Ease; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExcitementYieldsAbundance a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Following one's excitement yields abundance and the opportunities to go on"@en, "Der Begeisterung folgen bringt Fülle und die Gelegenheiten weiterzumachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting on what excites most is said always to lead where one needs to go to receive the skills, abilities and abundance needed for the next most exciting step; one will automatically attract the opportunities to keep doing it, and the other exciting things fall into perfect timing. To the dancer: behaving as a dancer from now on brings, synchronistically and without effort, all the circumstances and relationships of a dancer's life."@en ;
    skos:note "No deadline, count or observable mark is given by which a failure to receive the abundance could be told; the timing is called perfect whatever it turns out to be."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharFollowYourExcitement ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharAbundance ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Give Me a Sign; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Finding A Career; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExcitementYieldsEffortlessness a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Acting on excitement with trust and conviction yields effortlessness"@en, "Handeln aus Begeisterung mit Vertrauen und Überzeugung bringt Mühelosigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acted on with trust and conviction, the thing that excites most is said to be the most effortless thing one will ever do, since one is only being oneself."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharFollowYourExcitement ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharEffortlessness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Give Me a Sign; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharDisassemblingABeliefStructure a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Examining a belief, taking its components apart and attaching preferred ones"@en, "Einen Glauben prüfen, seine Bestandteile zerlegen und bevorzugte anknüpfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar's worked example: one examines one's beliefs about abundance and may find that, from seeing rich people one takes for morally bankrupt, one has quietly linked being abundant with being a scum and so keeps oneself from abundance. One names that structure, declares one no longer wants it, takes its components apart and asks which ideas one would rather attach, for instance that abundance would let one stay loving, share exciting ideas and change the world for the better. The old version is let go without judgment, as one choice one no longer prefers; preference is said not to be judgment. The example is offered to be rearranged for one's own case."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Abundance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharJudgmentChangesVibration a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not judge what you no longer prefer: judging puts you on its level"@en, "Nicht urteilen über das, was man nicht mehr bevorzugt: Urteilen versetzt einen auf dessen Ebene"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even what is very negative is not to be judged or invalidated, for judging it shifts one's own vibration to the same level, so that one cannot be where one wants. Bashar reads the biblical saying against judging, lest one be judged, in this sense: not a judgment from outside but becoming the vibration one judges."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharDisassemblingABeliefStructure ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Abundance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharOwningTheBelief a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Owning a belief one has difficulty with: honest acknowledgement, then an honest inquiry into why one chose it"@en, "Einen hinderlichen Glauben als eigenen annehmen: ehrlich anerkennen, dann ehrlich fragen, warum man ihn wählt"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one finds one only sometimes believes one can have what one wants, one is to be honest with oneself and acknowledge the difficulty, the doubt, fear or self-invalidation, saying in effect that one does it sometimes because one sometimes feels incapable. Owning the right to think so makes plain that the negative reality was one's own choice, which puts it back under one's control. One then holds a frank discussion with oneself about why one would choose that belief and which definitions one would have to accept to feel unable to do what most represents oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Abundance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOwnBeforeTransform a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "What one does not own one cannot transform"@en, "Was man nicht als eigen annimmt, kann man nicht verwandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acknowledging a belief as one's own is said to come before changing it: feelings not acknowledged and not dealt with cannot be changed."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharOwningTheBelief ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:BasharDisassemblingABeliefStructure ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "If the feelings and beliefs are not acknowledged and dealt with, they cannot be changed." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Abundance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDenialCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not deny anything about yourself, not even your denial"@en, "Nichts an sich leugnen, nicht einmal das eigene Leugnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Denial is called the first step toward forgetting everything about who one is; one is to deny nothing about oneself, including the fact that one denies."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharOwningTheBelief ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Abundance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharUniverseSupportsBelief a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The universe supports whatever one believes oneself to be, one hundred per cent"@en, "Das Universum unterstützt hundertprozentig, was man von sich glaubt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The universe is said always to supply automatically the opportunities that let a person go on being what they most believe themselves to be. Who believes that life must be a struggle receives situations that confirm it; these are not proof of being stuck or of having failed but a display of one's beliefs, with the message to change them if one does not prefer the result. Changing the belief to deserving ease brings ease with the same impartiality. A mediocre life is the universe supporting a belief in mediocrity; believing in ecstasy is said to cost no more effort."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Struggle or Ease; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDoubtAsTrust a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Doubt as one hundred per cent trust in a negative reality"@en, "Zweifel als hundertprozentiges Vertrauen in eine negative Wirklichkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Doubt, as society names it, is no absence of trust but a total, unshakable conviction in a reality one does not prefer. Everyone always trusts at one hundred per cent; the only question is whether the trust is placed in what one prefers or in what one does not. Nothing new is therefore asked of anyone, only a change of direction."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Struggle or Ease; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section 100% Trust; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharPlacingTrustInPreference a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Placing one's whole trust in the direction one prefers"@en, "Das ganze Vertrauen in die bevorzugte Richtung legen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since one already trusts fully, one moves that full trust to the direction one prefers, for instance from doing what one likes to doing what one loves, without changing the mechanics of how one acts. One then acts as if the preferred thing is true for one, reasoning that what excites more must represent who one really is and so must be something one can handle, or one could not have conceived it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Struggle or Ease; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section 100% Trust; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPreferredReality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Living the reality one prefers"@en, "Die bevorzugte Wirklichkeit leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The outcome promised for full trust in a preferred direction: circumstances and opportunities that reflect the self one now believes oneself to be, including the life one desires."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Struggle or Ease; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section 100% Trust; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Threshold of Believability; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTrustYieldsPreferredReality a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Full trust in what one prefers yields a full reflection of it, guaranteed"@en, "Volles Vertrauen in das Bevorzugte bringt dessen volle Spiegelung, garantiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar guarantees and promises that full trust always returns a complete reflection of the reality so trusted: once one decides to do one's preference wholly, the universe has no reason to withhold any part of the result, and offers every opportunity matching the new self-image. Going from what one likes to what one loves is supported just as strongly as the liked thing was."@en ;
    skos:note "Stated as a guarantee, without deadline; the clause that a remaining one per cent can block the rest (see pmc:BasharOnePercentFailure) means any shortfall is read as incomplete trust."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharPlacingTrustInPreference ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharPreferredReality ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Struggle or Ease; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section 100% Trust; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOnePercentFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The one per cent not done can keep one from the other ninety-nine"@en, "Das eine nicht getane Prozent kann einen von den übrigen neunundneunzig abhalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Depending on how a person has arranged their self-definition, doing something ninety-nine per cent while one per cent is held back may be enough to prevent experiencing the ninety-nine; the result comes in full only when the action is in full."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a reason, not a deadline or a count one could measure; the outcome (not experiencing the result) is observable but the one per cent is not, and the failure is put on the practitioner's own definitions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section 100% Trust; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharReadinessLimitsWhatIsGiven a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The universe gives only what one says one is ready to handle"@en, "Das Universum gibt nur, wofür man sich bereit erklärt"@de ;
    skos:definition "One always receives an exact reflection of the reality one defines as the most likely one one can handle, no more and no less. Who holds that success must be a struggle or a striving thereby tells the universe that they are not ready for more and asks it to hold things back until they believe they deserve a positive reality; so the universe gives only so much. Everyone deserves whatever they can conceive, simply by existing, and need not earn it."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a reason given for a limited result, with no deadline or count; the limit is put on the believer, who is said to be asking for it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section 100% Trust; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section One Consciousness; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDoNotBerateYourself a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Self-reproach for the time one takes only lengthens it"@en, "Sich nicht für die Zeit tadeln, die man braucht: das verlängert sie nur"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one keeps for now what one does not prefer, believing that is the pace one needs, one should at least not reproach oneself for the time it takes, since that only lengthens it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharPlacingTrustInPreference ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section 100% Trust; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharLettingWhereYouAreBeAllRight a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting where one is be all right"@en, "Den Ort, an dem man steht, in Ordnung sein lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "One relaxes, breathes easily and says that one goes about things this way because one chooses to believe one needs to; one lets wherever one is be where one wants to be, and so lives in the present, the only time there is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section 100% Trust; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLivingInTheNow a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Living in the present, where everything can find one, and changing faster"@en, "Im Jetzt leben, wo einen alles finden kann, und schneller sich wandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state of being at home in the present: everything one needs can find one there, and one reaches where one wants to be far sooner. Living in the past or future means nothing one needs can reach one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section 100% Trust; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAcceptanceYieldsChange a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Letting where one is be all right yields change and presence"@en, "Den jetzigen Ort gelten lassen bringt Wandel und Gegenwart"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar calls it the paradoxical mechanism: as soon as the way one is doing it is allowed to be all right, one will probably change, and gets where one wants much faster; letting where one is be where one wants means living in the moment, where everything can find one."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharLettingWhereYouAreBeAllRight ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharLivingInTheNow ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section 100% Trust; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOneConsciousness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One consciousness: there is no subconscious or unconscious mind"@en, "Ein Bewusstsein: es gibt keinen unterbewussten oder unbewussten Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar tells a questioner that none of them really has an unconscious or subconscious mind; each is one homogeneous, unbroken consciousness. Soul, spirit, higher and lower consciousness, mind and subconscious are convenient compartments made to avoid looking at what one has been taught is dangerous. Nothing one discovers about oneself cannot be put to positive use, and a positive application cannot yield a negative result."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section One Consciousness; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSegregatingTheSelfCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Splitting oneself into mind, conscious and subconscious spins a game lasting years"@en, "Sich in Verstand, Bewusstes und Unbewusstes aufzuteilen, spinnt ein Spiel von Jahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar interrupts a questioner who begins with what her mind says: dividing oneself into a mind, a conscious and a subconscious and then trying to reconcile the fragments is a game many keep up for years."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:BasharOneConsciousness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section One Consciousness; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharYouGetWhatYouPutOut a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One cannot experience a reality of which one is not the vibration"@en, "Man kann keine Wirklichkeit erleben, deren Schwingung man nicht ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any unpreferred reality comes from accepting a belief system that supports it. What goes out returns as an equal, corresponding reaction and never as its opposite: positive preferential trust can only bring a positive reality back, and the negative trust called doubt brings hesitation, guilt and frustration. Bashar names this the one law of Creation that applies to his people as to humans, and says it works for them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section One Consciousness; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Follow your Excitement!; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharThresholdOfBelievability a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The threshold of believability: what a person truly accepts as possible for themselves"@en, "Die Schwelle der Glaubwürdigkeit: was man wirklich für sich für möglich zu halten bereit ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "The line up to which a person truly accepts that something is possible for them. The wording a person uses shows where it lies. Its position in time decides experience: placed in the present, inside the person, the desired life is lived."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the desired life is experienced once the threshold sits in the present; no deadline or count, the threshold is located only by the person's own feeling and wording."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Threshold of Believability; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharThresholdInFutureFailure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "While the threshold of believability lies in the future, the life is not experienced"@en, "Solange die Schwelle der Glaubwürdigkeit in der Zukunft liegt, wird das Leben nicht erlebt"@de ;
    skos:definition "As long as the threshold remains somewhere ahead in time, however near, and not within the person, the preferred life will not be experienced."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: no deadline and no count; the failure is the absence of the preferred life, put on where the person places their belief."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Threshold of Believability; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharThresholdExercise a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The exercise of locating the threshold of believability by time questions"@en, "Die Übung, die Schwelle der Glaubwürdigkeit durch Zeitfragen zu finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "One forms, in whatever simple way is comfortable, a picture or feeling of the ideal way one would like to live, doing something enjoyable and fully supported, held as the essence of how living feels rather than a rigid picture. One then answers honestly whether one could create that life within ten years, within a month, a year, three years, and whether one can really feel it. The answers show where the threshold lies; asked why one would attend to anything one does not want, the questioner in the session is shown the belief that many other details must be handled first."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Threshold of Believability; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharRecognizingTheThreshold a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognizing where one's threshold of believability lies"@en, "Erkennen, wo die eigene Schwelle der Glaubwürdigkeit liegt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowledge of how far off in time one actually places the preferred life, and of the beliefs that hold it there."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Threshold of Believability; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharThresholdExerciseYieldsRecognition a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The time-question exercise yields recognition of the threshold"@en, "Die Zeitfragen-Übung bringt das Erkennen der Schwelle"@de ;
    skos:definition "The exercise is introduced as one that helps the person recognize where their threshold of believability is."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharThresholdExercise ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharRecognizingTheThreshold ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Threshold of Believability; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDetailsTakeCareOfThemselves a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "When one lives one's vibration, the details settle by themselves"@en, "Wer seine Schwingung lebt, dessen Einzelheiten erledigen sich von selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "Life is one homogeneous event, not a series of separate matters: when one lives in harmony with the chosen path, the tools for the details are attracted automatically and by coincidence. Whatever is left undone, if one is truly being oneself, did not need doing."@en ;
    skos:note "The second sentence turns any undone detail into evidence that it was unnecessary; no detail left undone can therefore count against the claim."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Threshold of Believability; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOuterReflectsInner a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Outer reality as no more than a mirror of inner knowing"@en, "Die äußere Wirklichkeit ist nur ein Spiegel des inneren Wissens"@de ;
    skos:definition "One does not get the outer reality before forming the inner belief: one receives in physical reality only what one already believes most likely. When one generates with the whole heart the feeling and energy of being the person one prefers, the outer world has no choice but to show it. Bashar's image is a radio dial: tuned to and kept on one's own station, one can receive only what belongs to it. The inner and the outer are said to be one; as one sows, so one reaps, and changing the seed one plants within changes the garden one sees."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section The Outer Reflection; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Out of Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Plant Something Different; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTuneFirst a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Tune to the frequency first; the outer reality follows"@en, "Zuerst auf die Frequenz einstimmen; die äußere Wirklichkeit folgt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deciding to tune to the frequency of the self one chose comes before the outer reality can reflect it; inner belief precedes outer form."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharPlacingTrustInPreference ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharPreferredReality ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Otherwise one keeps listening to a programme one does not enjoy." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section The Outer Reflection; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharChildlikeFascination a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Facing the world with childlike fascination and breaking through society's conventions"@en, "Der Welt mit kindlicher Faszination begegnen und die Konventionen der Gesellschaft durchbrechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To someone who is never really excited, Bashar says what one is doing now is by definition what matters most at that moment, and one is to look at it so. One meets the world with a child's fascination and breaks through the conventions of society, which thins the thick skin many have grown so that excitement can get through."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section No Excitement; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharRecognizingOnesExcitement a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognizing one's excitement and its direction"@en, "Die eigene Begeisterung und ihre Richtung erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being able to perceive what excites one, finding the mundane more exciting than supposed, and seeing in which direction one's path lies."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section No Excitement; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFascinationYieldsRecognition a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Childlike fascination yields the recognition of one's excitement"@en, "Kindliche Faszination bringt das Erkennen der eigenen Begeisterung"@de ;
    skos:definition "With a changed attitude one starts to see that one is where one is for a reason and to draw from the moment what one needs; things taken for granted turn out more exciting, and with a thinner skin the direction of one's excitement and path becomes obvious."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharChildlikeFascination ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharRecognizingOnesExcitement ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section No Excitement; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharImaginationTemplate a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Handing a situation to the imagined preferred self and copying how it handles it"@en, "Eine Situation dem vorgestellten bevorzugten Selbst übergeben und nachahmen, wie es sie handhabt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Described as a very simple mechanism that works for anything. One conjures in imagination a vision of the excited self one would prefer to be, hands it any situation now under way in one's life, watches how that imagined self deals with it, and then copies it. Imagination is the template or blueprint and exists to be copied; Bashar likens it to a child, who sees and becomes without questioning the validity of what it sees."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section No Excitement; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPreferredSelfAndLifeStyle a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being the imagined person and having that life style"@en, "Die vorgestellte Person sein und deren Lebensweise haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The result promised for copying the imagined self: one gets the effect it gets in its excited way of handling things, becomes that person and has that way of life automatically."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section No Excitement; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharImaginationYieldsPreferredSelf a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Copying the imagined self yields being that self"@en, "Das vorgestellte Selbst nachahmen bringt, dieses Selbst zu sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Creating an image and mimicking it is said to make one that person, with that life style, automatically."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharImaginationTemplate ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharPreferredSelfAndLifeStyle ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section No Excitement; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharCreatingOnesOwnJob a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Creating what excites one as one's job when no such job exists"@en, "Das Begeisternde zum eigenen Beruf machen, wenn es diesen Beruf nicht gibt"@de ;
    skos:definition "To a questioner growing depressed from unemployment: instead of looking only among existing jobs, if none excites and no opportunity arrives, one examines honestly what would excite and makes that one's job, as whoever started each existing kind of work once did. The ability to conceive the exciting thing is taken to be the ability to create it as a supporting job; the structure is inherent in the one who thought of it and has only to be let out for reality to build on that template."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Out of Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFeelingsAreSecondary a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feelings are secondary to beliefs"@en, "Gefühle sind den Glaubenssätzen nachgeordnet"@de ;
    skos:definition "No feeling arises from nothing; every feeling reacts to a belief already held. Beliefs are the primary interface with reality: first one believes, then feels, then has thoughts that reinforce the belief, and so regenerates the same feelings. A feeling of incompetence therefore means one chooses to believe one is incompetent, which one need not."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Out of Work; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Feelings Are Secondary; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharUsingTheOldVoices a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting the old inner voices come and using them as a measure of change"@en, "Die alten inneren Stimmen kommen lassen und als Maß der Veränderung nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When inner voices recall past failures, one does not try to shut them off: they will always be heard, the more so the more one integrates. One answers them that this was then, one has learned since, and thanks them for the chance to see how differently one will act now. If an event recurs nearly as before, a positive person fixes on the nearly: a little different means it can be very different, and each reminder becomes a chance to see how much further things are changing. Every part of life, the same old voices included, can be used as a tool."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Feelings Are Secondary; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharVoicesAsMeasure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A changed relation to the old voices, and a slightly different outcome, as the measure of change"@en, "Ein veränderter Umgang mit den alten Stimmen und ein leicht anderer Ausgang als Maß der Veränderung"@de ;
    skos:definition "The recurring voices give a measure of one's evolution: one notices that one no longer relates to them as before, and that something which happened before has happened again almost but not quite the same."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: observable by the practitioner alone (a different reaction, an outcome slightly different from last time); no deadline or count, and any difference however small qualifies."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Feelings Are Secondary; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharVoicesNotFailureCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The recurrence of the old voices does not mean one has failed"@en, "Die Wiederkehr der alten Stimmen bedeutet nicht, dass man gescheitert ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Taking the return of the old voices as proof of having failed, or of doing it wrong, keeps the old relationship to them. They come not to show failure or being stuck but to give the chance to see change; to read their presence as failure is the old belief."@en ;
    skos:note "A caution that removes an obvious sign of failure: the persistence of the symptom is declared not to count against the practice."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharUsingTheOldVoices ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Feelings Are Secondary; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOuterVoicesChange a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "When the inner voices are used positively, the outer voices change too"@en, "Werden die inneren Stimmen positiv genutzt, ändern sich auch die äußeren"@de ;
    skos:definition "To a questioner whose acquaintances echo the inner voices: no one can give reinforcement, it must be accepted; since inner and outer are one, once the inner voices are used in the described way the voices of others will also change."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: announced in advance and observable in other people's speech; no deadline."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Feelings Are Secondary; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPhrasingRevealsBelief a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Wording that tries to convince oneself shows the belief is not held"@en, "Formulierungen, die sich selbst überzeugen wollen, zeigen, dass der Glaube nicht gehalten wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "To someone who repeated that she could handle the job and found the old belief still there: the way one phrases a thing shows what one really believes. Saying one can handle it implies one finds it overwhelming; who knew it beyond doubt would not need to persuade themselves. Words that attempt to convince mean the belief is not held naturally. One already controls everything, so an unpreferred event was shaped so for a positive reason."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: an observable sign (one's own phrasing) that the belief change has not taken; no deadline; the failure rests with the speaker. Bashar adds that nothing can be got rid of."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Plant Something Different; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharHowDoesThisServeMe a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Asking how the situation, exactly as it is, serves one"@en, "Fragen, wie die Lage, genau so wie sie ist, einem dient"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar's suggested phrasing: how does this serve me just as it is, what lesson it holds, and how something positive may be drawn from it. Letting it be as it is gives it the greatest chance to change. Only by acknowledging one's own way of delivering messages to oneself exactly as it comes does one gain the freedom to change that delivery into a preferred form. Even in the worst circumstances one tells oneself that everything is fine and that one must have great power to have created so wild a scenario."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Something Positive; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMalfunctionCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Treating one's delivery system as malfunctioning reinforces that something is wrong"@en, "Das eigene Übermittlungssystem als gestört zu behandeln, bestärkt, dass etwas falsch ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Denying the form in which a situation arrives hides what is in it; who constantly treats their inner delivery system as faulty does not listen to it, reinforces the belief that something is wrong, and sees reality reflect that back."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharHowDoesThisServeMe ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Something Positive; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharPositiveHabits a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Using belief in habits to create positive habits"@en, "Den Glauben an Gewohnheiten nutzen, um positive Gewohnheiten zu schaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one believes old habits are hard to break, one uses that very idea of habit positively and creates positive habits, telling oneself that one controls everything even when it looks out of control, and getting used to knowing that every scenario, without exception, can produce a positive manifestation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Something Positive; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharLookingAtThePositiveSide a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Deciding to seek the positive side in every circumstance"@en, "Sich entscheiden, die positive Seite jedes Umstandes zu sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To a questioner who sank after losing a job: losing it is only assumed to be negative. If one knows one is doing one's best and such things still happen, one assumes a good reason, perhaps room for something delightful, and lets oneself see it. One insists as strongly that the loss must lead to a broader positive experience as one used to insist it was bad."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Something Positive; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPositiveSideNecessity a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Without the conscious decision to look at the positive side, positive manifestation cannot be seen"@en, "Ohne den bewussten Entschluss zur positiven Seite ist positive Manifestation nicht zu sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Seeing a positive manifestation in a circumstance is said to depend on a prior conscious decision to seek the positive side in every circumstance."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharLookingAtThePositiveSide ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharPreferredReality ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Insisting that the event is inherently negative keeps away the reason that would show why it happened for the good, and no positive manifestation can be seen." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Something Positive; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharJobInterviewReport a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A questioner's report: stating the positive view brought an interview for a better-paid job, which she then lost"@en, "Bericht einer Fragenden: die positive Sicht brachte ein Vorstellungsgespräch für eine besser bezahlte Stelle, das sie dann verlor"@de ;
    skos:definition "A questioner says that she had stated exactly the positive view Bashar recommends and then got an interview for a job paying more; she went into it expecting that not getting it would mean failing, did badly, did not get the job and fell back into her old state. Bashar attributes the setback to the expectation."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered as a reported result of the practice: partial success (the interview) followed by a failure the text puts on the questioner's expectation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Something Positive; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExpectationCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Remove the expectations: it need not manifest as ego or habit thinks it should"@en, "Die Erwartungen entfernen: es muss sich nicht so zeigen, wie Ego oder Gewohnheit meinen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Expecting that a particular outcome must arrive, and that its absence is failure, fights oneself; the result is to be allowed to come by the easiest route, in any form. One need not force oneself into a mould or match an idea of success; one is successful as one is."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the expectation that one particular outcome must happen is given as the reason for the questioner's relapse; no deadline; the failure is put on the practitioner."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharLookingAtThePositiveSide ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Something Positive; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAnxietyIsExcitement a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Anxiety as excitement's own energy with a judgment laid on it"@en, "Angst ist dieselbe Energie wie Begeisterung, mit einem Urteil belegt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Anxiety and excitement are one energy; the energy does not go away, it is felt according to how one regards it. Its presence signals that one is on the threshold of new information and awareness. Since one never goes faster than one is ready for, there is a built-in governor, and the universe does nothing pointless, so one need not worry."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Anxiety; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharRelaxingTheJudgment a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Relaxing the judgment on anxiety and acting as if it is excitement"@en, "Das Urteil über die Angst lockern und handeln, als sei sie Begeisterung"@de ;
    skos:definition "One takes anxiety and excitement to be a single energy and begins to act as though one believes it; one relaxes the judgment, laughs a little more about what one is going through, and pays attention to it, since it may later be passed on to others."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Anxiety; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFeelingTheEnergyAsExcitement a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling the energy as excitement and laughter instead of anxiety"@en, "Die Energie als Begeisterung und Lachen statt als Angst fühlen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state in which the same energy is felt as excitement; Bashar says one will giggle through life."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Anxiety; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharRelaxingJudgmentYieldsExcitement a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Relaxing the judgment turns anxiety into excitement"@en, "Das Lockern des Urteils verwandelt Angst in Begeisterung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting as if anxiety and excitement are one energy makes the energy felt as excitement; relaxing the judgment lets the anxiety go and turns it into excitement and laughter."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharRelaxingTheJudgment ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharFeelingTheEnergyAsExcitement ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Anxiety; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharWillingToHaveIt a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Saying one is at least willing to have it, then acting as far as one can"@en, "Sagen, man sei wenigstens bereit, es zu haben, dann so weit handeln, wie man kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "A suggestion Bashar credits to a spiritual friend of all: when one feels one lacks what one needs, one says that one may believe one does not have it now but is at least willing to have it, then acts as well as one can on what is possible, uses imagination and leaves the rest to take care of itself. Tools and props are to be acquired and applied in the world, doing what one loves; doing, more than thinking, believing or feeling, creates the reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Follow your Excitement!; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDoNotSitWithTheProp a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A prop is not to be built and then left idle"@en, "Kein Hilfsmittel bauen und dann nur damit sitzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A tool or prop that is made and then not used leaves one wondering what is happening; it must be applied and acted on."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharFollowYourExcitement ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Follow your Excitement!; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAudienceForEveryActor a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "There is always an audience for what one truly needs to say; results guaranteed"@en, "Es gibt immer ein Publikum für das, was man wirklich sagen muss; Ergebnisse garantiert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar urges boldness: there is always a fitting audience for what one truly needs to say, and no actor is ever born without an audience born with them; the world shapes itself to what each needs, with enough for everyone, so no one loses by another's winning. If one believes this and acts as if one does, the results will be seen; he says he cannot and would not prove it, but it works for his people."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: results visible to the practitioner, guaranteed without deadline or count; the test is put to the reader (see for yourself)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Follow your Excitement!; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBarbaraSherWishcraft a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Barbara Sher, author of Wishcraft"@en, "Barbara Sher, Verfasserin von Wishcraft"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Barbara Sher" ;
    pm:nameRole "author of a human book, Wishcraft, which Bashar recommends as an aid in finding one's excitement and joy and for its many ways of having abundance other than money" ;
    skos:definition "Bashar refers to a book of his hearers called Wishcraft as helpful for finding what brings joy and for listing non-monetary ways to have abundance; a footnote names Barbara Sher as its author, published by Ballantine in New York in 1979."@en ;
    skos:note "The footnote spells the title Witshcraft, a misprint or a fault of the full-text layer."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 9 Follow Your Excitement, section Abundance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 10, The Agenda
#

pmc:BasharOctober15Threshold a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The threshold of October 15, 1989: after it, choosing against one's preference falls apart sooner"@en, "Die Schwelle des 15. Oktober 1989: danach zerfällt rascher, was man gegen die eigene Vorliebe wählt"@de ;
    skos:definition "At a session dated November 1989 at the Whole Life Expo, Bashar explains a date he had given before in that area, October 15 of that year, after which much acceleration was to follow. Choosing paths and habits that better express peace and creativity crystallizes one's life so that only matching opportunities occur, and makes it ever harder to choose what one does not prefer. The date marked a threshold: enough people in society now aim at what they want that whoever, from doubt, fear, hesitation or habit, chooses otherwise will see it fall apart faster, through mounting unhappy and stressful situations, and tire sooner of what is not theirs. From that date, the longer one hesitates to do what really excites, the worse things go and the more confusion there is."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it sets a date (after October 15, 1989) and an observable mark (things going worse, stress, confusion) for hesitation to follow one's excitement; the failure is put on the hesitating person. Also a dated statement about the world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section opening, November, 1989: Whole Life Expo; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Crossing the Threshold; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:Bashar1997Deadline a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "If by 1997 one does only what represents one's preference, one keeps pace; otherwise one may not catch up"@en, "Wer bis 1997 nur tut, was seiner Vorliebe entspricht, hält Schritt; sonst holt man vielleicht nicht mehr auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar's agenda: roughly from 1990 to 1994 or 1995 more of this energy crystallizes. He calls the next statement bold and only a reading of the energy as he now perceives it: if by 1997 people have not let themselves do in life only what represents what they prefer to be, they may be unable to catch up afterwards. The acceleration will then be so great that turning back without alignment will be almost impossible short of a complete breakdown of everything one knows, and the only way may be to cut oneself off from everything and begin again from nothing. For the next three years the change can still be made somewhat smoothly, with buffers and pacing. He adds that some may find the fresh start more exciting and that he tells no one what to do."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: it sets a deadline (1997) and a consequence (being unable to catch up, breakdown, starting from scratch), observable in principle; the failure is put on those who have not aligned. Qualified twice (may, almost impossible) and offered as a reading, not a command. A dated prediction about the world, testable against the years named."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Crossing the Threshold; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharChangingGracefully a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Changing, gracefully and with love, the jobs, situations and relationships that do not represent one"@en, "Arbeitsstellen, Lagen und Beziehungen, die einen nicht darstellen, anmutig und mit Liebe ändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Since nothing justifies postponing what one loves, one does not cling to jobs, situations or relationships that fail to represent oneself; one lets them change with integrity and love, but changes them. Against the usual fears of quitting a job, of food, rent and eviction, one trusts that the most exciting thing in life arrives with every tool needed to support doing it, and simply acts on the opportunities it brings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Crossing the Threshold; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTypicalFearsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not fear the typical fears of quitting a job"@en, "Die üblichen Ängste vor dem Kündigen nicht fürchten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The familiar worries, what one will eat, where one will live, whether one can pay the rent or will be thrown out, are not to be feared; the support is said to be built into the exciting thing itself."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharChangingGracefully ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Crossing the Threshold; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharSeeFeelBe a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing, feeling, being: the three steps into which all of Bashar's teaching folds"@en, "Sieh es, fühle es, sei es: die drei Schritte, in die sich Bashars ganze Lehre faltet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says everything his people have taught folds into three steps. First see what you want. Then feel, know and desire it. Then be and act it, doing only that, in the manner of the self you wish to be. He calls it easy and fun."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Crossing the Threshold; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Time Gates; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSeeFeelBeSystem a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The reduction of the teaching to three steps: see, feel, be"@en, "Die Rückführung der Lehre auf drei Schritte: sehen, fühlen, sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The summary Bashar himself gives of the whole message as a numbered sequence of three: seeing, feeling and being."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Bashar through Darryl Anka, in Blueprint for Change" ;
    dcterms:date "November 1989" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Crossing the Threshold; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharManifestingTheWish a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Manifesting every true wish in the present reality"@en, "Jeden wahren Wunsch in der gegenwärtigen Wirklichkeit verwirklichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "For every desire that truly represents a person, a self wish or soul wish, there is said always to be a time and place, and an opportunity in the present reality, to make it manifest; otherwise the person would not exist."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Time Gates; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSeeFeelBeYieldsManifestation a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "See, feel, be yields the manifestation of one's true wishes"@en, "Sehen, fühlen, sein bringt die Verwirklichung der wahren Wünsche"@de ;
    skos:definition "The three steps are presented as the way to use the ever present opportunity to manifest any true wish in the current reality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharSeeFeelBe ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharManifestingTheWish ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Time Gates; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExtraterrestrialDisclosureYears a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Major releases of data on human involvement with extraterrestrial societies in the odd years 1993 to 1999"@en, "Große Veröffentlichungen über die Verbindung der Menschen mit außerirdischen Gesellschaften 1993, 1995, 1997 und 1999"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar outlines his people's agenda for more open interaction, while saying humans do not need them to decide for them and that they have not come to save anyone. In each odd year from 1993 through 1999 (1993, 1995, 1997, 1999) people are to look for a major release of data about their involvement with extraterrestrial societies; these are critical points, and what humans do at them regarding his people will decide what happens after 2000, which he cannot yet say."@en ;
    skos:note "A dated prediction about the world, testable against the four years named; its sequel is made conditional on human choices."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section The E.T. Agenda; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:Bashar1990sUnifiedPhilosophy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The 1990s: all disciplines brought together, and by 2000 the foundation of a global philosophy for a thousand years"@en, "Die 1990er: alle Disziplinen zusammengeführt, und bis 2000 die Grundlage einer Weltphilosophie für tausend Jahre"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the 1990s the peripheral issues that obscure the kernel of every discipline are to be set aside, and the roots of one interdisciplinary understanding joining the political, economic, religious, metaphysical, scientific and philosophical are to be laid; the shared seeds of the issues will be seen. By 2000 humans will have begun the basis of a global philosophy to carry them through the next thousand years. Individually, the decade's agenda is to strip from oneself what does not belong in the preferred reality and shine as one's own core; people will grow more sensitive to one another, see certain social patterns as creations of fear and doubt, and understand that their core cannot be destroyed. Questions of consciousness, dreaming and reality will in the 1990s be understood as manifestations of one's own perspective."@en ;
    skos:note "A dated prediction about the world (the 1990s, the year 2000), testable in part."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section The E.T. Agenda; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Constant Change; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExistenceCannotCease a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Whatever exists always has and always will: non-existence is already full"@en, "Was existiert, hat immer existiert und wird immer existieren: das Nichtsein ist schon voll"@de ;
    skos:definition "The name of creation is said to be I Am, absolutely true. What exists can only go on existing, since non-existence is a realm of its own already holding everything that will never exist and has no room for anything else; it is the polar opposite of creation, without beginning or end. Hence each person, existing, has always existed and always will, can neither be destroyed nor consigned to oblivion, is infinite and yet changes from each second to the next."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Constant Change; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharConstantChange a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Constant change as the stable foundation of existence: God ever creating Itself anew"@en, "Ständiger Wandel als feste Grundlage des Daseins: Gott, der sich immer neu erschafft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Change is called the true constant of creation and the stable ground of existence, so that it never stagnates. Creation is not finished, as if God had made everything and sent it off to play; all beings together are God continually creating Itself anew. Paradox signals nearness to the central seed, where apparent contradictions are one; they only seem mutually exclusive in realms of polar vibration. The power of creation is shown in its ability to fool itself into forgetting that it is I Am; humanity has played that game through and is now waking up to play as whole, integrated beings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Constant Change; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTimeGates a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Time gates around the fifteenth of each month, strongest at March 15 from 1990"@en, "Zeittore um den Fünfzehnten jedes Monats, am stärksten am 15. März ab 1990"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acceleration has currents, eddies and loops which mostly reinforce forward motion; at times the overlapping vibration opens doorways or dimensional gates in which people briefly reflect past and future ideas and perceive their collective self. These are strongest around the fifteenth of every month, and very strong at March 15, the Ides of March, increasingly from 1990: people will find confusion in their consciousness and events in the world that hardly seem to belong to one world. At that date gates in consciousness also open to probes or visits from humanity's own past civilizations, to be seen in discoveries and a resurgence of awareness of those civilizations."@en ;
    skos:note "A dated prediction about the world (monthly, and March 15 from 1990), observable only in loose terms (confusion, discoveries about past civilizations)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Time Gates; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharGroundedConnectionToHeaven a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Hands in rich earth, eyes on the sky: making a grounded connection to heaven"@en, "Hände in reiche Erde, Blick zum Himmel: eine geerdete Verbindung zum Himmel herstellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar suggests going to a natural place with rich soil and plunging one's hands deep into the dark earth, breathing in the smell of nature, then looking up at the sky; one sees where one has come from in physical reality, where one is and where one is going, and so joins heaven and Earth. The surrounding image takes the turmoil of the time as tilled soil and past negativity as compost from which new growth comes, drawn upward by the light of one's future selves."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Time Gates; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharVitalityOfTheSoul a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Experiencing the richness and vitality of one's soul"@en, "Den Reichtum und die Lebenskraft der eigenen Seele erfahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "The experience offered at the end of the earth-and-sky suggestion: feeling the richness and liveliness of the soul."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Time Gates; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharGroundingYieldsVitality a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The grounded connection to heaven yields an experience of the soul's vitality"@en, "Die geerdete Verbindung zum Himmel bringt die Erfahrung der Lebenskraft der Seele"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hands in the soil and eyes on the sky are offered as the way to bring heaven to Earth and experience the soul's richness and vitality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharGroundedConnectionToHeaven ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharVitalityOfTheSoul ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 10 The Agenda, section Time Gates; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 11, Life on Essassani
#

pmc:BasharSassaniNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Sassani of Essassani, the place of living light"@en, "Die Sassani von Essassani, dem Ort lebendigen Lichts"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Sassani" ;
    pm:nameForm "Essassani" ;
    pm:nameForm "Essassanians" ;
    pm:nameRole "Bashar's people and his world: a civilization said to be of the questioners' future, passing out of physicality into a wholly non-physical state, which contacts new civilizations such as Earth's" ;
    skos:definition "In their old language, unused now that they are telepathic, the planet is called Essassani: the people being Sassani and es meaning place, the name renders as place of living light, all beings being taken for living light. Bashar describes them as about five feet tall, pale white-grey, with wide upturned eyes whose large pupils look almost black though mostly grey; men usually hairless, women with some whitish hair; slender and frail as they leave physicality, comparable roughly to a Mongolian type. The planet is said to be a little smaller than Earth, with about 85 per cent of its gravity, days of about 25 hours, a year of about 454 days at some 120 million miles from a hotter, yellow-green star, a tilt of three or four degrees and a steady temperature around 72 degrees Fahrenheit; park-like and green, without major structures, its 200 to 250 million inhabitants living mostly in city ships one to ten miles long. In a different dimensional plane, its star would lie about 500 light years away toward Orion if the two dimensions overlapped. They leave the body consciously around the age of 300, know no pain, reincarnate by choice and are passing from a transitional fourth density into the fifth; Bashar gives his own age as about 145 of his years, 167 of Earth's."@en ;
    skos:note "What the text holds them to be is entered here once; the figures are given as the speaker's own and have no external check in the work."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section opening, before Physical Aspects; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Physical Aspects; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section The Galaxy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Body Death; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAssociationOfWorlds a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Association of Worlds"@en, "Die Vereinigung der Welten"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Association of Worlds" ;
    pm:nameForm "the Association" ;
    pm:nameRole "a networking and serving body of some 360 worlds, not a government or federation, which puts intelligences in touch with matching intelligences, need for need and service for service" ;
    skos:definition "Many of the societies in the Association, Bashar says, have observed Earth's culture for thousands of years. Its members number several billion by a fluctuating count; it has explored five galaxies minutely and has some members from each, though most come from star systems of this galaxy. The Association has directly interacted with some 359 or 360 worlds; it knows of 60 to 70 million inhabited planets in the galaxy near human density, most never contacted. Each Association planet and each large city ship has one place from which images and information can be accessed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section opening, before Physical Aspects; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Physical Aspects; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section The Galaxy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Social Organization; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Entertainment; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSiriusTriad a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The triad of Sirius, Essassani and Earth"@en, "Die Triade aus Sirius, Essassani und Erde"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Sirius" ;
    pm:nameRole "the civilization of Sirius, which with Bashar's and the human civilization forms a triad consciousness in which two always support the one" ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says the triangle is the primary geometry that always arises in second and third density, and the tetrahedron the most basic manifest form in the third density. His civilization works in networks of threes on the principle of two supporting one, which is why Sirius consciousness, his own and the human form a triad, and why his scout craft is an equilateral triangle, hexagonal inside, with machinery in the three points and control in the centre."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section The Galaxy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharContactWithinEightToTenYears a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Essassani's opportunity to interact visibly with humans within eight to ten years"@en, "Die Gelegenheit Essassanis, binnen acht bis zehn Jahren sichtbar mit den Menschen zu verkehren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked whether his craft would be visible, Bashar says many beings interact with human civilization now, that his people will not be the first to do so physically because they assist others who will be, and that their own chance to interact will come roughly eight to ten years on. The landing place is unknown to him."@en ;
    skos:note "A dated prediction about the world, but the chapter gives no date for the session, so the window of eight to ten years cannot be fixed from the work itself; see pmc:BasharExpectationPreventsContact for the condition attached."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExpectationPreventsContact a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Expecting the visitors to come keeps them from coming"@en, "Wer die Besucher erwartet, hält sie vom Kommen ab"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar repeats that one must not expect his people to come, for then they cannot: expectation says that humans need them and place them above themselves, which puts them out of reach. They can meet a person only when the excitement is present now; the sooner people act as the beings they know they are, the sooner his people will be there."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a reason given in advance why the promised contact may not happen (the hearers' expectation), no deadline; the failure is put on the human side. Bashar adds that contact is in no way critical and that the hearers' own world matters more to them than his people do."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Essassani's Transformation; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMeetUsHalfway a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Humans must meet Essassani halfway: open contact follows a society living its full potential"@en, "Die Menschen müssen Essassani auf halbem Weg begegnen: offener Kontakt folgt einer Gesellschaft, die ihr volles Vermögen lebt"@de ;
    skos:definition "When human society lets itself live up to its potential, it co-creates with Bashar's people a shared frequency, a meeting ground where both can come together; until certain changes make it more conducive, contact goes through consciousness, since materializing requires his people to lower and solidify their vibration a great deal and the mind is where humans are nearest their frequency. What is solid for them is, for humans, the stuff of dreams."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharFollowYourExcitement ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharOpenContactChapter11 ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Essassani's Transformation; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOpenContactChapter11 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Open and blatant interaction between Essassani and Earth"@en, "Offener und unverhohlener Verkehr zwischen Essassani und der Erde"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state promised once the conditions on Earth allow it: nothing will hold Bashar's people back from interacting openly, in a compatible meeting frequency."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Essassani's Transformation; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharAstralVisitToEssassani a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Visiting Essassani in astral form by thinking of Bashar's vibration or a blue-white tetrahedron"@en, "Essassani in Astralgestalt besuchen, indem man an Bashars Schwingung oder ein blauweißes Tetraeder denkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "A human can visit Bashar's planet only in astral form. Lying down in a meditative state with eyes closed, one thinks of the vibration one feels as representing Bashar; thinking of his identity keys one automatically into his civilization's frequency. An abstract aid is to picture a tetrahedron with three sides, outlined in blue-white electromagnetic light. Then one simply lets oneself flow toward their dimensional vibration. Most of their population are said to be such visitors, projecting their mind and instantly forming a body there for as long as they like."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAstralPresenceOnEssassani a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A representational body and interaction on Essassani"@en, "Ein Abbildkörper und Verkehr auf Essassani"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being present on Bashar's world in one of their bodies and interacting with its members; Bashar says that the moment one identifies with being there one has such a form, whether or not one is aware of it, and that while he speaks to people here he speaks to them there as well."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAstralVisitYieldsPresence a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Thinking of Bashar's frequency yields presence on Essassani"@en, "An Bashars Frequenz denken bringt Gegenwart auf Essassani"@de ;
    skos:definition "Thinking of Bashar or of the blue-white tetrahedron aligns one like a radio dial with his people's frequency and lets one flow into their dimension; it is called as simple as that."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharAstralVisitToEssassani ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharAstralPresenceOnEssassani ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSymbolicDreamMemory a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Returning from Essassani with a dream remnant in symbols, if not a literal memory"@en, "Von Essassani mit einem Traumrest in Symbolen heimkehren, wenn nicht mit wörtlicher Erinnerung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many people are said to visit their dimension astrally already; on waking the physical mind, which cannot or need not relate to everything done out of the body, brings back a dream that may make no sense, giving convenient symbols for the experience. One may carry no literal memory but will carry at least a symbolic one, holding what one needs to apply what was learned or shared there."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: a dream fragment, observable by the dreamer, no deadline. The same passage pre-empts the obvious failure: the absence of any literal memory is not to count against the visit, and Bashar adds that awareness of being there is not needed for being there."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSynchronicityEconomy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A society run by synchronicity, without government, economy or medium of exchange"@en, "Eine Gesellschaft, die von Synchronizität getragen wird, ohne Regierung, Wirtschaft oder Tauschmittel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar's people call themselves a spontaneous civilization that has raised trust to an art: they need no government, political or economic system, but interact directly as a network. Each one with a service automatically draws each one who needs it, and the latter brings a service the former needs; so there is no medium of exchange, all running by coincidence, because life is a holographic matrix in which everything is linked. Knowing and focusing on that, one needs no reference structure, things organize themselves, and government serves instead of ruling. Bashar perceives that human governments will in time also become networks linking those who serve with those in need."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Social Organization; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOneMindOfStrongIndividuals a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "One mind through strongest individuals: unconditional love as the key"@en, "Ein Geist durch stärkste Einzelne: bedingungslose Liebe als Schlüssel"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is called a human misunderstanding that one mind means bland individuality. As a person functions as a whole when each of their parts is as strong as any other, so a society has unity when each individual is as strong as possible and equally validated; everyone is a non-conformist. Unconditional love lets them be one mind and at once distinct individuals. Different views never block progress: if three people propose three approaches, all three are done, and the two will likely join the third when they see it is more efficient. Their unity came when each became the strongest individual conceivable, and being in love with all creation, Earth included, was the way to expand their reality."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Social Organization; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Essassani's Transformation; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAkashicRecords a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Akashic records: access to all knowledge according to one's frequency"@en, "Die Akasha-Chronik: Zugang zu allem Wissen nach der eigenen Frequenz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says all individuals, humans included, can reach all knowledge, especially that most pertinent to their own world, a storehouse of the Infinite generally called the Akashic records. His people have mechanical versions of it, read into the mind from mnemonic devices rather than screens; it is an overlapping holographic network in which each person, made into a particular frequency, receives only what fits that frequency without hindering anyone else."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Entertainment; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPainNeedNotRemain a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pain can always be transformed and need not end in death"@en, "Schmerz lässt sich stets verwandeln und muss nicht im Tod enden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Arising pain need in no way end in physical death; it is always transformable, especially now that humans are becoming aware that pain need not stay. Bashar's people no longer feel pain at all, and leave their bodies consciously and without disease, the body turning instantly back into the energy of their world."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Body Death; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharChosenReincarnation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reincarnation is always by choice, for humans as for Essassani"@en, "Wiedergeburt geschieht stets aus Wahl, bei Menschen wie in Essassani"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked whether his people reincarnate by choice, Bashar says they do, and so do humans, always. His people no longer plan incarnations on Earth, being in another cycle."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Body Death; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharContactWithTheUnborn a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Contact with those who are to be born to one"@en, "Mit den Wesen in Verbindung sein, die einem geboren werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar's people are telepathically and consciously in touch with each consciousness that chooses birth among them, agree its timing and purpose, and do not conceive before that time; conception needs only an exchange of energy blending the masculine and feminine, gestation lasts seven months and by three a child is fully independent. Humans too can be in touch with those who will be born to them, who are not children now but non-physical individuals radiating the wish to accomplish certain things, and can recognize services they may wish to perform for them. Such an individual draws only those who can serve it; humans make negative as well as positive synchronicity, his people only the positive kind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Procreation and Children; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTelepathyThroughLove a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "When everyone on Earth is in love with everyone else, humans will be of one mind and telepathic"@en, "Wenn jeder auf der Erde in jeden verliebt ist, werden die Menschen eines Sinnes und telepathisch sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar likens his telepathic link with the channel to sharing a common daydream, a form of love-making. When every person on the planet loves every other, they will be of one mind and telepathic: identifying as one another, they read what Infinite Creation vibrates in the same way. Lovers who share thoughts are not reading minds but on one wavelength; the physical channel and Bashar are said to be displaying what being in love is."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Love-Making; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharRelationshipWithoutExpectation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting a relationship be what it is for, without expectation of its course"@en, "Eine Beziehung sein lassen, wofür sie da ist, ohne Erwartung an ihren Verlauf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any relationship one is drawn into is taken as an obvious reflection of what one needs to learn then, and allowed to serve its own purpose rather than what one thinks it should be. One follows emotions and instincts within integrity, puts no labels or expectations on how it should go or end, and takes for granted that however it transforms naturally is how it is supposed to transform. Bashar's people regard everyone as married to everyone, so courtship is unnecessary and whether a bond was monogamous is known only at the end of a lifespan."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Love and Courtship; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Marriage; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharCommitmentAndWholeness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why humans cling to committed relationships, and the commitment that always exists"@en, "Warum Menschen an verbindlichen Beziehungen festhalten, und die Bindung, die immer besteht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Humans hold to committed relationships because they think them the only guarantee of support and seek someone to make them whole; instead they attract someone who reflects their own sense of not being whole. Knowing that one attracts exactly what one needs, one is committed as much and as long as needed and changes with the relationship. One is always committed, even when exploring the lack of commitment, to the idea one is co-creating; structure changes nothing, as the human creation of divorce beside marriage shows. A relationship, once made, lasts forever in changing forms, and every change serves, change being the only constant."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Marriage; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharThirdYearRitual a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The ritual of the third year: three adults flow body, mind and spirit to the child"@en, "Das Ritual des dritten Jahres: drei Erwachsene lassen Körper, Geist und Seele zum Kind fließen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The one ritual Bashar says remains among his people, a recognition of adulthood or naming ritual at about three years, though no names are taken. Three individuals, one for each year, surround the child seated in the middle; each attends to one of body, mind or spirit and sends energy to the child, who takes from the three a blend and balance of its own. Through it the child, until then fluid and able to leave or become non-physical at will, crystallizes its identity, and if it stays, synchronizes with the mental tempo of the society to grow along its path of least resistance. Other rituals and myths arise spontaneously and dissolve when no longer needed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Rituals; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharChildCrystallizedIdentity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A crystallized identity attuned to the society"@en, "Eine kristallisierte, auf die Gesellschaft abgestimmte Identität"@de ;
    skos:definition "The result ascribed to the third-year ritual: the child forms its own blend and frequency of the three, body, mind, spirit, and fits into the flow of the society."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Rituals; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharThirdYearRitualYieldsIdentity a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The third-year ritual yields the child's crystallized identity"@en, "Das Ritual des dritten Jahres bringt die kristallisierte Identität des Kindes"@de ;
    skos:definition "By drawing its own balance from the energies of body, mind and spirit sent by the three, the child is said to solidify its identity in the society."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharThirdYearRitual ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharChildCrystallizedIdentity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Rituals; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharChristConsciousness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Christ consciousness as the combined consciousness of all individuals on a planet"@en, "Das Christusbewusstsein als vereintes Bewusstsein aller Einzelnen eines Planeten"@de ;
    skos:definition "From Bashar's standpoint what humans call the Christ consciousness is the collective consciousness of every individual on the planet, knowing itself as one identity and as made of all. Every planet, society and dimension has its own version, a collective soul or world spirit. His world's abrupt transformation some 300 to 500 years ago came when theirs manifested, an event like the human Christ scenario."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Essassani's Transformation; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharShakanaNamingChapter11 a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Shakana, the world spirit of Essassani"@en, "Shakana, der Weltgeist Essassanis"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Shakana" ;
    pm:nameRole "the collective soul or Christ consciousness of Bashar's world, which took physical birth for about three days and woke the whole world into mental linkup" ;
    skos:definition "In their ancient language the world spirit of Essassani was called Shakana. It manifested as a physical birth lasting about three days without a full lifespan; already inclined to mental linkup, the people went into a collective waking dream and the whole world awoke three days later understanding it could expand beyond its former limits. Bashar says the difference from humans was only that, presented with the reflection of their world spirit, they listened, and from then on functioned as a unit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Essassani's Transformation; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFutureSelfOfTheChannel a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bashar as the future self of the channel, who is Bashar's one past life on Earth"@en, "Bashar als zukünftiges Selbst des Kanals, der Bashars einziges früheres Leben auf der Erde ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "An organization for special training among Bashar's people is said to be responsible for his ability to communicate with humans: since contacted civilizations think in many modes, training and other tools are needed, without which each side would be too alien to the other. They also prepare by having at least one life in the society to be contacted, building a framework in their own incarnational history. Bashar says he is the channel's future self and that the physical channel is the one past life he has had on Earth, giving him a frame of reference instead of coming in raw. He speaks not from beside the hearers but by telepathic link from his scout craft above his own world."@en ;
    skos:note "A statement about the reception of the work's own wording; the work's main pm:Receiving for Bashar is entered in another part of this harvest."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Education; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section The Dawning; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAnimaNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Anima, Bashar's female counterpart"@en, "Anima, Bashars weibliches Gegenstück"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Anima" ;
    pm:nameRole "Bashar's female counterpart, whom a questioner says many have heard speaking through Darryl" ;
    skos:definition "A questioner mentions Anima as Bashar's female counterpart, heard speaking through Darryl by many, and asks whether Bashar knows all counterpart selves of the same oversoul. Bashar answers that all beings of his society are by now part of one oversoul, experienced through unconditional love for every one of them; everyone met is taken as a reflection from a different aspect of that oversoul."@en ;
    skos:note "The claim that Anima spoke through Anka is the questioner's; no words of Anima stand in this unit, so no pm:Receiving is entered for her here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 11 Life on Essassani, section Male/Female Energy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 12, Message from Orion
#

pmc:BasharNeamonReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "The work's claim that the opening of chapter 12 is the speech of Neamon of Orion, through Darryl Anka with Bashar's facilitation"@en, "Die Behauptung des Werkes, der Anfang von Kapitel 12 sei die Rede Neamons aus dem Orion, durch Darryl Anka unter Bashars Vermittlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A bracketed note states that a further entity named Neamon speaks through Darryl, Bashar facilitating. The speaker says he has been told to send greetings, that he is unsure anyone hears him and must trust the one he has just met, who calls himself the Commander; he assumes his words, spoken in his own present, reach hearers some 175,000 years ahead, who were once his colleagues in what they call Orion and who no longer remember themselves. Afterwards Bashar asks whether the message was received, and answers questions on how the link was made."@en ;
    skos:note "This node records the claim, not its truth. The speech is the only passage of the unit given to a speaker other than Bashar; the words after Bashar asks whether the message was received are Bashar's again. Neamon's uncertainty whether he is heard is part of the text; a questioner calls it the reverse of her own uncertainty when she transmits through imagination."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Darryl Anka, the physical channel, in the session; Bashar, called by Neamon the Commander, facilitating" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Neamon, of the Orion systems, a figure he says is best understood as something like a priest, speaking from about 175,000 years in the hearers' past" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "Bashar says he communicated with Neamon much as with the hearers but that it took more: he physically manifested before him, to Neamon's great surprise, and stayed with him. Neamon was helped into a trance-like daydream state yet was conscious and aware. In his systems communication outside what the mass consciousness recognizes was forbidden on pain of death, and Neamon says discovery would put his life at risk; Bashar says he was not. Neamon is connected to Bashar by a different and more general route than Anka is, not as an earlier self. Bashar says the hearers are now due to receive a message many of them sent themselves long ago, and that the questioner who felt no conscious recognition has recognized it as much as she needs." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section opening, before A Message to Yourselves; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section A Message to Yourselves; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNeamonNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Neamon, a priest-like figure of the Orion systems"@en, "Neamon, eine priesterähnliche Gestalt der Orion-Systeme"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Neamon" ;
    pm:nameRole "the speaker of the chapter's message: a third-density being of the Orion systems some 175,000 years ago, akin to a priest, who stayed behind as an anchor for those who left and holds a paternal role toward them" ;
    skos:definition "Neamon gives his name as one by which he may be reckoned and says his role is best rendered by a priesthood, though not literally. He is told to hold a paternal image for the hearers and has out of love made himself their anchor in the home system; he hopes he may send such messages from time to time. Bashar says he stayed, through many lives paralleling the hearers', so that someone would be there to receive what they send back, and that in his present life he lives within the light now present in those systems; contacting him now would not endanger him."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section opening, before A Message to Yourselves; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section A Message to Yourselves; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOrionSystemsNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Orion systems and the Orions"@en, "Die Orion-Systeme und die Orioner"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Orion" ;
    pm:nameForm "the Orion systems" ;
    pm:nameForm "Orions" ;
    pm:nameForm "Hoova" ;
    pm:nameRole "a group of star systems whose old way was domination, control, servitude and slavery, from which many of the hearers are said to have come, and which now has light in it" ;
    skos:definition "Bashar describes the Orion systems of 175,000 years ago as third-density governments of suppression: all interaction is domination, only a ruling hierarchy has any say, the many work for the gratification of the few without believing it benefits them, and communication outside what the mass consciousness recognizes is punished by death. Neamon spoke from no single planet, there being travel among them; his origin point translates as Hoova. Those systems are now, like Earth, in third and transitional fourth density, with light in them, partly because of what the hearers have done. Many humans are said to be reincarnated Orions who came to Earth to bring the old negativity to the surface and balance it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section A Message to Yourselves; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section Orion Involvement; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section The Dark Side; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOrionResistanceNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The resistance near Mintaka and its dark crystal moon"@en, "Der Widerstand bei Mintaka und sein dunkler Kristallmond"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Mintaka" ;
    pm:nameForm "the resistance" ;
    pm:nameRole "the resistance to the Orion suppression, which used a dark crystal moon near the star Mintaka, and to which many of the hearers are said to have belonged" ;
    skos:definition "Asked how Hoova relates to Mintaka, Bashar says Mintaka is the star near which lay the dark crystal moon used by those resisting the suppression; many of the hearers come from the resistance. Neamon says their leaving the Orion systems stood for their will to reach beyond the suppression there."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section opening, before A Message to Yourselves; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section A Message to Yourselves; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharThreePrimesNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The three primes, rendered as Shadrach, Meshach and Abednego"@en, "Die drei Primen, wiedergegeben als Schadrach, Meschach und Abed-Nego"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Shadrach, Meshach, and Abednego" ;
    pm:nameForm "three primes" ;
    pm:nameRole "the three primes that act in the basic triad consciousness of the Orion systems, recognized there as sorcery and as the heritage of what humans would call religion" ;
    skos:definition "Neamon is instructed to remind the hearers of their heritage: within the Orion systems there is the creation of three primes, which he is told translates into the hearers' speech as Shadrach, Meshach and Abednego, standing for what is called sorcery, which is how the primes of the basic triad consciousness act. In a later answer Bashar takes a gospel phrase naming these three, heard by a questioner, as an unconscious remembrance of Orion connections in the Middle East, very ancient."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section opening, before A Message to Yourselves; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section The Religious Connection; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMagicAsMassConsciousness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Magic as mass consciousness personified in one individual"@en, "Magie als Verkörperung des Massenbewusstseins durch einen Einzelnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Neamon says the hearers took the Orion heritage with them but applied it to their new system without understanding it as the action of their mind and personality on the primal energy, which the Commander calls an archetypal flow of the subconscious stream. Positive and negative polarities, merged in a third persona, both and neither, together form a mental interaction that produces an effect in the planet's electromagnetic field, called magic in human history. It is the individual mind interacting with the primal field of the whole civilization's mentality; he is told to repeat that magic is the mass consciousness personified through one person. By leaving a universal time track the hearers can use these abilities without the burden of domination and suppression."@en ;
    skos:note "Wording ascribed to Neamon; see pmc:BasharNeamonReceiving. Neamon says the terms are outside his experience and he may be simplifying."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section opening, before A Message to Yourselves; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharThirdIdentity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The third identity: blended polarities, a reservoir of all that is possible"@en, "Die dritte Identität: verschmolzene Polaritäten, ein Speicher alles Möglichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Merging the polarities into the third identity, each individual is said to become a reservoir and wealth of everything possible within the system or universal tangent they inhabit; the triad of two poles and a balancing third point is what allows transformation and change."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section opening, before A Message to Yourselves; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section Finding the Balance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExcitementYieldsBlending a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Doing with integrity what excites most yields the fullest merging of the polarities"@en, "Mit Integrität tun, was am meisten begeistert, bringt die stärkste Verschmelzung der Polaritäten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says that the moment one does with integrity what excites one most, one allows the polarities in oneself to merge most fully, the balance his service is meant to help the old Orion energy find."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharFollowYourExcitement ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharThirdIdentity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section Finding the Balance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOrionInfluenceOnReligionAndScience a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Orion influence in the Commandments, in religious organizations and in analytical science"@en, "Orion-Einfluss in den Geboten, in religiösen Organisationen und in der analytischen Wissenschaft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says there is Orion influence even in the Commandments: what humans call God has no thou shalt not in its vocabulary, and what higher consciousness communicated was grasped but read through an Orion frame. Early human society served to absorb Orion energy afresh, to be balanced now, and all would know power lies within, not in another. Orions founded some religious organizations for their own kind, to go on experiencing and finally integrate the polarities of Earth and of their former home. Much of human analysis, and the way many see science, especially the strong focus on analytical methods, trickles down from the way Orion first filtered ideas."@en ;
    skos:note "An explicit dispute with the biblical tradition of the Commandments, whose side is not read here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section The Religious Connection; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharReincarnatedOrionsBalance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reincarnated Orions on Earth bringing the old negativity to the surface to balance it: the road is clear"@en, "Wiedergeborene Orioner auf der Erde, die die alte Negativität hervorholen, um sie auszugleichen: der Weg ist frei"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many Orions incarnated on Earth to set up real scenarios in which to meet the old momentum of exploring negativity and blend it; being born on Earth is meant to bring all of it up and balance it with the knowledge that it need no longer apply, since the Orion systems have changed. Through their incarnations here they have sent that energy back and can receive what the Orions have become. Those connected to it can know they hold every opportunity for balance and acceleration from now on; the energy is fully reconnected to its origin to make a positive reality there. Bashar ends by saying that the light humans now make is mirrored as far as Orion, and that struggle and conflict are no longer needed to create the desired harmony."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section Orion Involvement; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section Finding the Balance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFearGivesNegativeBeingsPower a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Only fear of negative beings gives them the power to link with anyone"@en, "Nur die Furcht vor negativen Wesen gibt ihnen die Macht, sich mit jemandem zu verbinden"@de ;
    skos:definition "To a questioner who has heard that beings of Orion's dark side bear hostility to Earth, Bashar replies that a negatively oriented consciousness can connect only with people who believe it has power to force such a link on them; that fear and concern alone give it the power. Negative beings exist on many worlds, as on Earth, and negativity is not confined to Orion but spread through the local galaxy; because time and space are simultaneous, the old negative Orion consciousnesses can still be picked up telepathically by those who keep to the same old frequency."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the reason given why a person might be reached by negative beings despite the promised protection; no deadline or count; the failure is put on the person's own fear and frequency."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section The Dark Side; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharFocusingOnTheChosenReality a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Not focusing on negative beings, but on the reality one chooses to be"@en, "Sich nicht auf negative Wesen richten, sondern auf die Wirklichkeit, die man sein will"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar's advice and suggestion: one does not dwell on the idea that negative beings elsewhere in the universe might interact with one against one's will, and instead takes on the vibration, frequency and attitude of the reality one chooses to be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section The Dark Side; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBeyondReachOfNegativity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being beyond the reach of all who lack one's loving frequency"@en, "Außer Reichweite aller sein, die nicht auf derselben liebenden Frequenz sind"@de ;
    skos:definition "The protection promised: on a different frequency, negative consciousnesses cannot intercept one's reality, and one is wholly out of reach of all who do not share that loving frequency."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section The Dark Side; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFocusYieldsProtection a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Focusing on the chosen reality yields being out of reach of negative beings"@en, "Die Ausrichtung auf die gewählte Wirklichkeit bringt, außer Reichweite negativer Wesen zu sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being the frequency of the reality one chooses is said to put one, by that very difference of frequency, completely beyond the reach of negative consciousnesses; reincarnated Orions can likewise switch themselves to a frequency out of reach of the old negativity of their parent systems."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharFocusingOnTheChosenReality ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharBeyondReachOfNegativity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section The Dark Side; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFearOfNegativeBeingsCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not dwell on negative beings who might act against your will"@en, "Nicht bei negativen Wesen verweilen, die gegen den eigenen Willen handeln könnten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Focusing on the notion that negative beings from other worlds could interact with one against one's will is warned against, since that very fear is what lends them a link."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharFocusingOnTheChosenReality ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section The Dark Side; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEssassaniAsMarker a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being drawn to Bashar's people as a marker that one is keeping one's agreements"@en, "Die Anziehung zu Bashars Volk als Zeichen, dass man seine Vereinbarungen einhält"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says his people's agreement to serve Earth includes reflecting choices first made in the Orion system, helping that energy find its fulcrum in the triad of all creation. Their service draws those with that connection and reflects back that control is always within them; the drawing together serves as a marker by which they may know their agreements are being kept, and can speed them by doing what excites them."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: attraction to Bashar's reflection is announced as a marker that one keeps one's agreements; observable only to the person, no deadline or count."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 12 Message from Orion, section Finding the Balance; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 13, Friends and Neighbors
#

pmc:BasharHumansAsAliens a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "From another vantage the humans are the aliens"@en, "Aus anderem Blickwinkel sind die Menschen die Außerirdischen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar opens with a description of a strange people of mixed colours and greater height than his own folk, which turns out to be humanity, to show that seen from elsewhere Earth is the unknown and unusual world. No other civilization need be rated above oneself; every form life takes, physical or not, is equally valid, and the diversity of societies arises from how one shared sameness, drawn from a single source of Infinite Creation and one kind of soul, is expressed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Who is the Alien?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEssassani a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Essassani, Bashar's civilization"@en, "Essassani, Bashars Zivilisation"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Essassani; Essassani-ish" ;
    pm:nameRole "Bashar's own fourth-density civilization, the middle of the triad with Earth and Sirius" ;
    skos:definition "Bashar's own people, on average about five feet tall with white to whitish-grey skin, living on the third planet from their sun in the final phase of physical fourth-density life and headed for the fifth; they stand halfway between Earth and Sirius and are to move to the triad's peak once Sirius goes on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Who is the Alien?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Three Levels; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Let's Get Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFrequencyAttractsLikeForms a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "First contacts come from beings closest in frequency, hence humanoid"@en, "Erste Kontakte kommen von frequenznahen, daher menschenähnlichen Wesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Earlier images of extraterrestrials were monstrous because people invested them with malevolence; now that attitudes change, most reported contacts involve humanoid beings. The reason given is that all matter is a product of rates of frequency, so a civilization starting out into space first attracts the forms whose frequency lies nearest its own, and these usually share its bodily build. Meeting the familiar first lets a people get used to contact without fright; quite unlike forms exist and will be met later, some so foreign they may not be recognized as life."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Who is the Alien?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharHeartAsSensor a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Staying open to interaction and using the heart as a sensor"@en, "Offen für Begegnung bleiben und das Herz als Sensor gebrauchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Remaining open to interaction with other kinds of life, opening further, letting the heart serve as the organ that senses, and exploring the range of frequencies at which life can exist."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Who is the Alien?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEncounteringUnlikeLife a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognizing and meeting life in forms unlike one's own"@en, "Leben in fremden Formen erkennen und ihm begegnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The realization that consciousness can take very different bodily forms and still radiate love and integrity, and the eventual encounter with many such variations, including forms built on nothing a human knows."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Who is the Alien?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHeartSensorYieldsEncounter a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Openness and the heart as sensor yield recognition of and encounter with unlike life"@en, "Offenheit und das Herz als Sensor führen zur Begegnung mit fremdem Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The more one opens and senses with the heart, the more one realizes how many forms loving consciousness can take, and the more of these variations one will come to meet as one's sphere of understanding widens; Bashar says the encounter will come eventually."@en ;
    skos:note "No time or count is given by which the promised encounter would be overdue."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharHeartAsSensor ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharEncounteringUnlikeLife ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Who is the Alien?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHumansAsOthersUfos a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Humanity may become the UFOs of later-arriving civilizations"@en, "Die Menschheit kann zu den UFOs später ankommender Zivilisationen werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Other civilizations are expanding as Earth is, some thousands of years behind; if humans are willing they may become the visitors who bring such peoples the understanding that, as parts of Infinite Creation, they can create whatever realities they like. The first such people is said to be a civilization of the Barnard star cluster, which humans may in time assist as Bashar's people assist humans."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Who is the Alien?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Barnard; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBarnardCivilization a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The civilization of the Barnard star cluster"@en, "Die Zivilisation des Barnard-Sternhaufens"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Barnard star cluster" ;
    pm:nameRole "a civilization roughly at the technological stage of the human Renaissance, already in dream contact with humans" ;
    skos:definition "A people on one world of what Bashar calls the Barnard star cluster, similar to humans and technologically about where they stood in the Renaissance. It already knows of humanity through dream-level contact, and some human channels at times speak through its members; it does not divide channelled sources into separate entities but treats all of it as one phenomenon. Bashar names it the most likely civilization to take humanity's place in his triad."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Barnard; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Three Levels; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharIrax a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Irax (name garbled in the layer)"@en, "Die Irax (Name im Textlayer verderbt)"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "/rax, lrax" ;
    pm:nameRole "a civilization with bony, expressionless faces" ;
    skos:definition "A civilization that has given itself the limitation of almost wholly bony faces able to show no feeling, so that emotion must be expressed by other means; its people have waxy skin of a creamy whitish-yellow."@en ;
    skos:note "The layer prints the name first as /rax and then as lrax; the first letter is an OCR misreading, most likely of a capital I. Neither form is corrected here."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Brief Encounters; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDilla a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Dilla"@en, "Die Dilla"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Dilla" ;
    pm:nameRole "non-physical beings of another dimensional plane whose chief export is humour" ;
    skos:definition "Beings of a very different dimensional plane, non-physical though perceived as having a body, without fixed features and able to take nearly any form, seen as plastic-like in primary colours and at rest roughly a flattened oblate spheroid, though they never really rest. Their world is a featureless sphere from whose molten surface things are drawn when needed and with which they can merge. Their main export is said to be a sense of humour."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Brief Encounters; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPleiadians a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Pleiadians"@en, "Die Plejadier"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Pleiadians" ;
    pm:nameRole "humanlike relatives of humanity, the positive pole of the split from Lyra" ;
    skos:definition "A civilization recently in contact with Earth, humanlike because many humans come from the same offshoots, and so literally family whom humans are now rejoining. With the Orions they split from Lyra long ago and formed a polarity system in which the Pleiadians explored the positive side. A questioner calls them headstrong."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Brief Encounters; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Dal Universe; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOrions a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Orions"@en, "Die Orioner"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Orions" ;
    pm:nameRole "the negative pole of the split from Lyra" ;
    skos:definition "An offshoot of the earlier Lyran system which, after the split, explored negative existence while the Pleiadians explored the positive."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Brief Encounters; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLyra a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Lyra"@en, "Lyra"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Lyra" ;
    pm:nameRole "the earlier system from which Pleiadians and Orions split" ;
    skos:definition "An earlier system from which both the Pleiadians and the Orions branched off long ago in physical time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Brief Encounters; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharZetaReticuli a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Reticuli of Zeta Reticulum"@en, "Die Reticuli von Zeta Reticulum"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Zeta Reticulum; Reticuli" ;
    pm:nameRole "short, pale, large-eyed beings behind the abduction phenomena" ;
    skos:definition "Beings of the star system called Zeta Reticulum, of very small stature, pale-skinned, with big black eyes and enlarged heads, most representative of what humans label abductions; the chapter defers them to later."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Brief Encounters; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDals a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Dals of the Dal Universe"@en, "Die Dals des Dal-Universums"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Dal Universe; Dals" ;
    pm:nameRole "etheric energy beings of a vector universe that monitor energy exchange" ;
    skos:definition "Asked by a questioner who reports energy exchanges with them, Bashar says the Dals act like an automatic switch regulating some exchanges of energy in the physical universe, a monitoring energy. They are energy beings, better called etheric than gaseous, from another dimensional plane at ninety degrees to ours, a vector universe; they come by phase shifting and project only a portion of themselves, a finger as it were, and have no ships, though their cohesive electromagnetic consciousness may be seen as ships or spheres of light. Bashar rejects the questioner's reading that the Pleiadians fall silent before them as melodrama."@en ;
    skos:note "Bashar declines for now to say much about other universal realities."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Dal Universe; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharArcturus a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Arcturus, the regulating gate"@en, "Arcturus, das regulierende Tor"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Arcturus; Arcturus energy; Arcturus consciousness" ;
    pm:nameRole "a collective energy consciousness that translates energy from other dimensions; the emotional side of the overall triad" ;
    skos:definition "The consciousness associated with the star Arcturus is described as the gate through which other dimensions' communication is funnelled and translated into symbols humans understand; much of the regulating of the rate of transformation on Earth and other planets of the galaxy falls under it. It has connections to the angelic realm and is partly Pleiadian, partly extra-dimensional energy. It cannot be described as individuals; people who meet Arcturians personally meet an identification projection of that energy rather than its literal embodiment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Arcturus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Arcturean Symbol; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharArcturusAlignmentOfChildren a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Children born now pass through an Arcturian energy alignment and forget less"@en, "Heute geborene Kinder durchlaufen eine arcturische Energieausrichtung und vergessen weniger"@de ;
    skos:definition "Arcturus is said to set up an energy alignment through which many children now being born pass before birth, so that they keep more memory of who they are; the children arriving now are called not merely a new generation but another culture."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Arcturus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharArcturusChannelingReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "A questioner's claim to have channelled an energy relayed through Arcturus"@en, "Die Behauptung eines Fragenden, eine über Arcturus vermittelte Energie gechannelt zu haben"@de ;
    skos:definition "A questioner reports having channelled an energy that seemed to come through Bootes and Arcturus, spoke of the children with great emotion, and seemed to be the planet's own consciousness; Bashar confirms it as a collective and explains the relay through Arcturus as a familiar symbol through which overwhelming energy can be taken in comfortably."@en ;
    skos:note "This node records the claim of a member of the audience, not the claim of the book about itself; the book's own claim for Bashar is pmc:BasharBlueprintReceiving."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "an unnamed questioner in a session audience, who says he will be a bridge for that energy" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "an energy seeming to be the planet's own consciousness, relayed through the constellation Bootes and Arcturus; behind it the questioner saw a brilliant star and a being he took for a teacher" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "Reported in a question to Bashar; the questioner felt more emotion than he could handle for long and saw the star in a vision, or in his mind. No date or place is given." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Arcturus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEmotionalCoreVibrationSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The emotional core vibration as the mark of linking with Arcturus energy"@en, "Die emotionale Kernschwingung als Zeichen der Verbindung mit Arcturus-Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Strong emotion is the core vibration by which one knows one is linking with Arcturus energy at this time: an opening and crystallization of inner doorways tied to the heart and to the solar plexus chakra of intention, felt as heaving and releasing together with assimilation and blending of energy."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: announced as the way to know that contact with Arcturus energy is made; it sets no deadline and no count; it is observable only as the person's own feeling, and since any strong emotion qualifies it can hardly fail; no failure is put on anyone."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Arcturus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEnergyThroughFamiliarSymbol a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Energy from beyond comes through a familiar symbol so it can be assimilated"@en, "Energie von jenseits kommt durch ein vertrautes Symbol, damit sie aufgenommen werden kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "To be taken in comfortably, energy from beyond the physical universe must pass through a physical valve or representational symbol the receiver already relates to, so that it arrives with some familiarity; the relay through Arcturus is explained in this way."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Arcturus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharArctureanSymbol a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Using the Arcturean symbol as a focal point and link"@en, "Das arcturische Symbol als Brennpunkt und Verbindung gebrauchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar gives a symbol for the Arcturus energy, a white star of twelve points set on an orange circle against black, to be used as a focal point and as a communicative or identifying link to that vibration on whatever level one needs to identify with it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Arcturean Symbol; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLinkToArcturusEnergy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A communicative link to the Arcturus energy"@en, "Eine Verbindung zur Arcturus-Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identification with and communication with the vibration of the Arcturus collective, on whatever level the person needs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Arcturean Symbol; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharArctureanSymbolYieldsLink a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The Arcturean symbol serves as a link to the Arcturus energy"@en, "Das arcturische Symbol dient als Verbindung zur Arcturus-Energie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The twelve-pointed star symbol is said to be able to represent the Arcturus energy and act as a link to its vibration."@en ;
    skos:note "Hedged in the text: the symbol may serve as a point of focus; no sign is given by which a working link is told from none."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharArctureanSymbol ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharLinkToArcturusEnergy ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Arcturean Symbol; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharArctureanSymbolCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The symbol is only a symbol: do not get attached to it"@en, "Das Symbol ist nur ein Symbol: nicht daran haften"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar says of the symbol he gives that it is merely a symbol and should not become an object of attachment, though it may serve as a focus."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharArctureanSymbol ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Arcturean Symbol; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTriadOfTriads a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The triads: Earth, Essassani and Sirius in one triad, with Arcturus and Polaris in a higher one"@en, "Die Triaden: Erde, Essassani und Sirius in einer Triade, mit Arcturus und Polaris in einer höheren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Earth, Essassani and Sirius form one triangle whose combined consciousness is one third of a larger triad, the other thirds being Arcturus and Polaris; each of these is itself threefold, Spica being one of the parts that make Arcturus whole, and the larger triad is in turn part of another, without end. Within it the Earth–Essassani–Sirius triad stands for mentality, Arcturus for the emotional side and Polaris for the polarities of positive and negative now being blended; Sirius stands at the peak of the lower triad, Essassani and then Earth to follow, with the Barnard civilization expected to take Earth's place. The combined consciousness is called Siskeen for Sirius, Shakana for Essassani and the Christ consciousness for Earth."@en ;
    dcterms:date "undated in the full-text layer, which carries no imprint" ;
    pm:compiledBy "Bashar through Darryl Anka, in Blueprint for Change" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Arcturus; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section More Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Three Levels; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharShakana a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Shakana"@en, "Shakana"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Shakana" ;
    pm:nameRole "the name of the overall collective consciousness of Essassani" ;
    skos:definition "The name Bashar gives for his own civilization's collective consciousness, one of the names under which the combined consciousness of the triad can be addressed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section More Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharChristConsciousnessAsEarthName a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Christ consciousness as Earth's collective name"@en, "Das Christusbewusstsein als kollektiver Name der Erde"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "the Christ consciousness" ;
    pm:nameRole "the name of the overall collective consciousness of Earth" ;
    skos:definition "Asked what the combined triad is called, Bashar says it may be called by the name of the collective consciousness within each member, and for humans that name is the Christ consciousness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section More Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPolaris a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Polaris"@en, "Polaris"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Polaris" ;
    pm:nameRole "one third of the overall consciousness triad, standing for the polarities" ;
    skos:definition "One of the major parts of the overall triad besides Arcturus and the Earth triad, standing for the polarities now being blended; humans drift towards Polaris in physical affinity because it indicates the theme of their integration."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section More Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSpica a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Spica"@en, "Spica"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Spica" ;
    pm:nameRole "one of the fragments that make up the collective whole of Arcturus" ;
    skos:definition "Asked why Spica is missing from the triad, Bashar says Spica is one of the parts which together with other consciousnesses make Arcturus a whole, as Sirius, Essassani and Earth make one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section More Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDensityThreshold a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The threshold between the third and the fourth density and its astrological symbols"@en, "Die Schwelle von der dritten zur vierten Dichte und ihre astrologischen Symbole"@de ;
    skos:definition "Any alignment with Arcturus marks another threshold being crossed, and the overall threshold is the planet's passage from the third density into the fourth; every symbol of transformation belongs to it. A move in the questioner's chart stands for sub- and unconscious matter surfacing; Pluto stands for the crossing itself, of what was once taken for death and now becomes a new kind of life. The crossing of the Styx expresses the same: entering the blend of one's positive and negative poles and drawing only a positive effect from it, which is why Pluto's moon was named Charon after the ferryman."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section More Triads; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPlutoCharonPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction: Pluto's thin atmosphere envelops Charon and electrical arcs pass between them"@en, "Vorhersage: Plutos dünne Atmosphäre umhüllt Charon, und elektrische Bögen springen zwischen beiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Charon counts as a moon, being smaller than Pluto. Science is beginning to find a very thin atmosphere on Pluto, not breathable, that can reach out far enough to envelop Charon; it will also find an electrical potential between the two bodies, with much arcing at certain alignments in the solar system when ionic charge builds up. Apart from Charon there is only lesser debris around Pluto."@en ;
    skos:note "A testable prediction about the world, without a date; the arcing claim is put as something not yet seen. Only debris is said to orbit Pluto besides Charon."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Moons and Planets; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSolarSystemLifePrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction: primordial organic compounds on Mars and the gas giants; no third-density life elsewhere in the solar system"@en, "Vorhersage: urtümliche organische Verbindungen auf dem Mars und den Gasriesen; kein Leben dritter Dichte sonst im Sonnensystem"@de ;
    skos:definition "No further third-dimensional life will be found in the solar system. In time remnants of compounds will be found on parts of Mars and molecular conglomerates in Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune, primordial organic forms that will give clues to how humanity as a mass consciousness made Earth's life forms. Every planet is inhabited, loosely speaking, though never third-dimensionally; Mars carries fourth-density life, and the moon has life in an altogether alternate reality while being barren in ours."@en ;
    skos:note "A prediction without a date; the finding of compounds is put as certain in time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Moons and Planets; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section More Cover-Up; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMoonBasesCoverUp a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Artificial bases on the moon, seen by the astronauts and suppressed"@en, "Künstliche Basen auf dem Mond, von den Astronauten gesehen und unterdrückt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Under questioning Bashar affirms that the moon carries artificial bases, in human density,, built by civilizations not of Earth, some still inhabited though fewer than before; the astronauts found and photographed them, knew what they saw and reported it, and authorities suppressed the information. Face-to-face meetings with aliens have taken place on Earth with the military and government, and occasionally with private people. Governments keep it secret because they hold power to mean control, and information to be power; open contact on equal terms would end the need to hand one's responsibility to institutions."@en ;
    skos:note "Testable in principle against the record of the lunar missions; no date beyond the past missions is given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section More Cover-Up; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharTakingBackResponsibility a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognizing oneself as one's government and taking back responsibility by loving them"@en, "Erkennen, dass man selbst die Regierung ist, und Verantwortung zurücknehmen, indem man sie liebt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Accepting that the people are their governments and reclaiming responsibility, not through opposition but by loving those in office and dealing with them as equals, so that all run the world together and any organizational service done by government serves rather than controls."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section More Cover-Up; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharContactWithOrdinaryPeople a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Contact with extraterrestrials for people outside government"@en, "Kontakt mit Außerirdischen für Menschen außerhalb der Regierung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Interaction between other civilizations and members of the public who are not part of the governmental structure, which already happens from time to time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section More Cover-Up; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharResponsibilityYieldsContact a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The frequency of contact depends on taking back responsibility"@en, "Die Häufigkeit des Kontakts hängt von der Rücknahme der Verantwortung ab"@de ;
    skos:definition "How often extraterrestrials interact with people outside government is said to depend entirely on two things: recognizing that one is one's government, and reclaiming responsibility by loving rather than opposing it."@en ;
    skos:note "Contact was granted to governments first because enough people entrusted them with power; Bashar says his people do not differentiate between those who did and those who did not."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharTakingBackResponsibility ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharContactWithOrdinaryPeople ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section More Cover-Up; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDefenseProgramAndNonInterference a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The defence programme as a means of staying in power; other civilizations will not interfere"@en, "Das Verteidigungsprogramm als Mittel des Machterhalts; andere Zivilisationen greifen nicht ein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked about the Star Wars programme, Bashar says much of the defence effort exists to make people think they need protection so the authorities stay in power. Governments know beyond doubt that his and other civilizations will not interfere; they scramble for a foothold so as to remain the representatives once contact opens, and do not grasp that empowerment belongs to everyone, reading self-created reality as anarchy rather than as synchronicity and trust in one's higher and future self."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Our Defense; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSirius a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The civilization of Sirius"@en, "Die Zivilisation des Sirius"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Sirius" ;
    pm:nameRole "a civilization of semi-physical and non-physical beings at the peak of Bashar's triad" ;
    skos:definition "A civilization orbiting Sirius, some ten light years away, made of semi-physical and wholly non-physical beings and existing at three levels of density. It stands at the triad's peak and represents the step that Essassani and Earth will both take; it lives as forms of energy within a sea of energy, pictured as a ball of clear light turning white, then electric blue towards its centre, where a black hole gate links all dimensions and through which Sirius projects itself and communicates by telepathy, singly or as a single consciousness, with an instantaneous link to Earth. It constantly sends unconditional love and thought patterns for humans to tap."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Three Levels; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Let's Get Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSiriusThreeLevels a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The three density levels of the Sirius civilization"@en, "Die drei Dichtestufen der Sirius-Zivilisation"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Sirius world is third not in space but in dimension: its civilization has a fourth-density level, once partly amphibious and in physical contact with ancient Earth cultures; a quasi-physical fifth-density level; and the wholly non-physical sixth-density level Siskeen. Its course ran from the fourth through the fifth to the sixth, yet because all realities coexist, interactions on all levels still occur. The parallel is drawn to Earth and Essassani each being the third planet from its sun."@en ;
    dcterms:date "undated in the full-text layer, which carries no imprint" ;
    pm:compiledBy "Bashar through Darryl Anka, in Blueprint for Change" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Three Levels; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSiskeen a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Siskeen"@en, "Siskeen"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Siskeen" ;
    pm:nameRole "the sixth-density, non-physical level of the Sirius consciousness" ;
    skos:definition "The level of Sirius most in contact with Earth: non-physical beings of the sixth density in an energy sea, long in telepathic touch with humans and responsible for some myths of amphibious gods among Sumerian, African and American Indian peoples. Their ancient fourth-density selves were partly amphibious but not half fish as those cultures depicted them; contacts with them shaped some ideas of culture, religion, politics and economy, though extraterrestrials are not wholly responsible for human culture."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Three Levels; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharCetaceans a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Dolphins and whales as Earth's second civilization"@en, "Delfine und Wale als zweite Zivilisation der Erde"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "water cetaceans; dolphins and whales" ;
    pm:nameRole "souls who think, incarnate themselves and know themselves; not animals" ;
    skos:definition "Scanning Earth, Bashar finds two alien civilizations, humans on land and cetaceans in the water. Dolphins and whales are souls aware of themselves, long in telepathic contact with other civilizations and closest to Sirius; whales embody physically the dolphin's higher consciousness, which the buoyancy of the sea allows and Earth's gravity denies to humans, who must be both the individual and the higher consciousness. They already enter human dreams to teach spontaneous ecstatic play, and they love humans."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Three Levels; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharCommunicatingWithCetaceans a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Going to the dolphins and whales, sharing with them and learning to communicate"@en, "Zu Delfinen und Walen gehen, mit ihnen teilen und Verständigung lernen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar urges people to seek out the cetaceans, share with them and learn to communicate with them, the alien civilization already present in the oceans."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharInterCivilizationCommunication a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing how to communicate with other civilizations"@en, "Wissen, wie man mit anderen Zivilisationen kommuniziert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Understanding of the manner in which humans will communicate with every civilization they meet, and an easier interaction with other whole societies once humans and cetaceans blend as one society."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharCetaceansTeachCommunication a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Communicating with cetaceans teaches how to communicate with all civilizations"@en, "Verständigung mit Walen und Delfinen lehrt die Verständigung mit allen Zivilisationen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If people learn to communicate with dolphins and whales, these will teach them much about how humans will communicate with all other civilizations; blending as one society with them will also ease interaction with other whole societies."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharCommunicatingWithCetaceans ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharInterCivilizationCommunication ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharOpeningToOwnFrequency a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Opening oneself to fuller expression of the consciousness and frequency one is"@en, "Sich der volleren Ausdruckskraft des eigenen Bewusstseins und der eigenen Frequenz öffnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each in his own way and time deciding to let more of the consciousness and frequency one is be recognized and expressed; biological life is said to transmit and receive more efficiently than anything else."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Three Levels; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSensitivityToSirius a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensitivity to the frequency Sirius sends"@en, "Empfänglichkeit für die Frequenz, die Sirius sendet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Becoming sensitive to the frequency Sirius bathes in and from which it beams love, energy and thought patterns to Earth, so that one can tap them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Three Levels; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOpeningYieldsSiriusSensitivity a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Opening to one's own frequency yields sensitivity to Sirius"@en, "Öffnung für die eigene Frequenz bringt Empfänglichkeit für Sirius"@de ;
    skos:definition "As people open to expressing the consciousness and frequency they are, they become more sensitive to the frequency of Sirius and can draw on the love and thought forms it sends."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharOpeningToOwnFrequency ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharSensitivityToSirius ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Three Levels; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharEnergizedBalancedEcstaticState a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Being energized, balanced, relaxed and ecstatic"@en, "In einem energiegeladenen, ausgeglichenen, entspannten und ekstatischen Zustand sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping oneself energized, balanced, relaxed and ecstatic, the state in which the central gate within each being is said to be open."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Let's Get Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharCentralGateAwareness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness of all frequencies through one's central black hole gate"@en, "Gewahrsein aller Frequenzen durch das eigene zentrale Schwarze-Loch-Tor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every being has the same central black hole gate as Sirius, through which any idea or information can be received and sent and any desired interaction created; through it one can be aware of the whole spectrum of energy and information always available and ride its wave."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Let's Get Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEcstaticStateYieldsGateAwareness a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The energized, balanced, relaxed, ecstatic state yields awareness of all frequencies"@en, "Der energiegeladene, ausgeglichene, entspannte, ekstatische Zustand bringt Gewahrsein aller Frequenzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In that state one is said always to be able to be aware of all frequencies and information available, through the central gate every being has."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharEnergizedBalancedEcstaticState ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharCentralGateAwareness ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
