pmp:BasharIdentificationWithSiriusAndEssassani a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Identifying with the high energy of Sirius and with Essassani as the halfway vibration"@en, "Sich mit der hohen Energie des Sirius und mit Essassani als halbem Weg identifizieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allowing identification with the very high energy of Sirius, and with Bashar's civilization as the band of consciousness halfway between, which mirrors the future humans have chosen, while meeting them half way oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Let's Get Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAcceleration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Acceleration of one's own evolution"@en, "Beschleunigung der eigenen Entwicklung"@de ;
    skos:definition "A quickening of the movement towards what humanity is becoming, assisted from outside but not done for one."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Let's Get Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharIdentificationYieldsAcceleration a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Identification with Sirius energy assists acceleration, if one meets them half way"@en, "Identifikation mit Sirius-Energie hilft der Beschleunigung, wenn man ihr auf halbem Weg entgegenkommt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Identifying with the high energy of Sirius can assist one's acceleration, though they do not do it for anyone; one must meet them half way, and Essassani is the halfway vibration whose identification reflects humanity's own chosen future."@en ;
    skos:note "The condition 'you must meet them half way' is stated without a consequence beyond the implicit absence of help, so it is kept here rather than as a stated necessity."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharIdentificationWithSiriusAndEssassani ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharAcceleration ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Let's Get Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharShiningAsAStar a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Opening the light by shining brightly as a star; lightening up"@en, "Das Licht öffnen, indem man als heller Stern leuchtet; leichter werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Opening to the stars and opening the light by shining brilliantly oneself; with a pun on the name, people who lighten up and stop being so serious are said to reflect the Sirius nature."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Let's Get Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharKnowingThroughLight a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Using light for all one needs and knowing everything one needs to know"@en, "Licht für alles Nötige nutzen und alles Nötige wissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Gliding on starlight and drawing all power and understanding from light, the matrix in which all needed information is interwoven; attuning to the frequency of every life in Creation and knowing all one needs to know now, just as one is; reflecting one's higher and fuller selves."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Let's Get Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharShiningYieldsKnowing a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Shining as a star yields matching the frequency of all Creation and knowing what one needs"@en, "Als Stern leuchten bringt die Frequenz aller Schöpfung und das nötige Wissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When people open the light by shining as brilliant stars, they will match the frequency of all life in Creation and know everything they need to know right away."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharShiningAsAStar ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharKnowingThroughLight ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Let's Get Sirius; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharStarChildren a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Everyone a star child; nobody original to Earth"@en, "Jeder ein Sternenkind; niemand stammt ursprünglich von der Erde"@de ;
    skos:definition "None of the humans is original to Earth; all have connections to other worlds, and the label star child marks a conscious recognition of a connection that stands out in a particular life. As spirit one has no point of origin, coming from everywhere and nowhere. All are representatives of many civilizations who chose to be born here to help transform Earth's energy into the harmonious energy known elsewhere, so Earth is equally home. The feeling of not belonging and homesickness comes from a fresh recognition read through the habit of separation in space."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Three Levels; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Star Child; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharUnmatchedVibrationUnseen a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "What is not one's vibration cannot be seen"@en, "Was nicht der eigenen Schwingung entspricht, kann nicht gesehen werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked why she feels invisible to others, Bashar says that anything not of one's vibration, and anything whose vibration one is not, literally cannot be perceived."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Star Child; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharBeingFullestSelf a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Being the fullest self one can be, with integrity"@en, "Das vollste Selbst sein, das man sein kann, mit Integrität"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar's suggestion to one who feels alone: simply be as fully oneself as possible, with integrity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Star Child; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAttractingKindredOthers a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Attracting others who wish to interact on one's level"@en, "Andere anziehen, die auf der eigenen Ebene begegnen wollen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Radiating at the pitch that draws all who wish to interact with one, and being drawn into circumstances where such people are found because they already stand there."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Star Child; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFullestSelfYieldsKindred a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Being one's fullest self attracts the others who are like one"@en, "Das vollste Selbst sein zieht die Gleichgesinnten an"@de ;
    skos:definition "By being as fully oneself as possible with integrity one will radiate at the needed pitch to attract those who wish to interact and to reach the circumstances where they are; Bashar adds that one is not alone, and points the questioner to the two hundred people in the room."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharBeingFullestSelf ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharAttractingKindredOthers ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Star Child; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharMeditativeConnectionExploration a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Exploring in meditation which extraterrestrial connection feels strongest"@en, "In der Meditation erkunden, welche außerirdische Verbindung sich am stärksten anfühlt"@de ;
    skos:definition "An optional suggestion: in the meditative state, roam with the imagination and notice which feelings of association or connection to some extraterrestrial idea arise most strongly."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Star Child; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNativeFocusCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Remember that your present focus is that of an Earth native; do not run away to rejoin another home"@en, "Bedenke, dass du als Bewohner der Erde fokussiert bist; nicht fliehen, um eine andere Heimat wiederzufinden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whatever connections the exploration turns up, one is now focused as a native of one's own world and that focus must come first, else one would be elsewhere; the point is not to flee one's chosen place to rejoin another energy but to bring that energy into being here."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharMeditativeConnectionExploration ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section Star Child; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAssociationOfWorldsUnstructured a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Association of Worlds"@en, "Die Vereinigung der Welten"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "The Association of Worlds; The Association" ;
    pm:nameRole "an unstructured association of many civilizations and dimensions that Earth is now joining" ;
    skos:definition "Many civilizations of different levels and dimensions agreeing to interact in mutually reinforcing ways, knowing that serving all lets all serve them. It is not a government but highly unstructured, functioning through spontaneity and the trust that each world, being fully itself, will synchronistically fit the others. Its members meet by telepathic projection in a chamber every mother ship has, where hundreds of civilizations confer to feel the pulse and direction of their agreements; trust and unconditional love tell them when to gather and when to go about helping other worlds recognize their power, which enlarges their numbers."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section The Association; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharHarmonizingWithAssociation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Choosing to harmonize one's pulse with the Association and taking back one's power"@en, "Wählen, den eigenen Puls mit der Vereinigung abzustimmen, und die eigene Macht zurücknehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Making the agreement with the Association: choosing to bring one's pulse, dream and reality into synchronistic harmony with theirs, taking back one's power and functioning as whole beings and as a whole civilization."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section The Association; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLessStruggleMoreSynchronicity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "More synchronicity, less struggle, suffering, doubt, fear and guilt"@en, "Mehr Synchronizität, weniger Kampf, Leiden, Zweifel, Angst und Schuld"@de ;
    skos:definition "The results said to be felt physically by those who choose to harmonize with the Association: more synchronicity, less struggle and suffering, greater recognition of one's existing abundance, fewer rigid definitions, invalidations and self-judgments, less doubt, fear and guilt; and an easier dealing with other whole civilizations."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the text says those who have made the choice are beginning to experience these results; no deadline or count is set; the outcomes are observable to the person only as comparatives of his own experience; no failure is assigned to anyone."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section The Association; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHarmonizingYieldsSynchronicity a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Harmonizing with the Association yields more synchronicity and less struggle"@en, "Abstimmung mit der Vereinigung bringt mehr Synchronizität und weniger Kampf"@de ;
    skos:definition "Those choosing to make the agreement with the Association are said to begin to experience its result physically, as more synchronicity and less struggle and fear, all of which come from taking back one's power."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharHarmonizingWithAssociation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharLessStruggleMoreSynchronicity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section The Association; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharBeingTheAssociations a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Letting oneself be recognized as all the associations one makes"@en, "Sich als alle Verbindungen erkennen lassen, die man eingeht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Allowing oneself to be all the associations one makes in life and to recognize oneself as the relationships one has and the life one lives, oneself being the association."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section The Association; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharParadoxResolved a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The resolution of all paradox, dichotomy and conflict"@en, "Die Auflösung aller Paradoxa, Gegensätze und Konflikte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Every paradox and conflict is a projection of polarity from one's centre; since one perceives both ends, both come from within, where they are blended and one, so no paradox remains."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section The Association; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAssociationResolvesParadox a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Associating resolves all paradox"@en, "Verbinden löst alle Paradoxa auf"@de ;
    skos:definition "By connecting and associating, and by being the associations one makes, all paradox, dichotomy and conflict is said to be resolved; association is called the key."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharBeingTheAssociations ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharParadoxResolved ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 13 Friends and Neighbors, section The Association; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 14, UFOs Identified
#

pmc:BasharForgottenSightings a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Everyone has seen the craft and blanked it out"@en, "Jeder hat die Raumschiffe gesehen und es ausgeblendet"@de ;
    skos:definition "To a questioner who has never seen a ship, Bashar says all have seen them but erased the memory, because it would not serve what they need to be just then and would often hinder them from being themselves naturally; it is not important to see the craft, and the point is to attend to one's own feelings now. The matter is partly one of vibratory rate; in dreams people are on a plane where the visitors are plainly perceivable in their own surroundings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Sightings; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSeeingWhenNeeded a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Whoever truly needs to see the ships will, and you remember when it serves you"@en, "Wer die Schiffe wirklich sehen muss, sieht sie, und erinnert sich, wenn es dient"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar promises that once a person truly needs to see spacecraft, nothing at all will prevent it, and that the memory of a sighting is kept wherever keeping it is of use."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: not seeing, or not remembering, a craft is explained in advance by the absence of real need or by the memory being of no use; there is no deadline and no count; the outcome, a sighting, would be observable, but its absence is put on the person's present needs and so can never count against the claim."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Sightings; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharSofteningFocus a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Softening one's focus into the semi-conscious and blending unconscious with conscious"@en, "Den Blick ins Halbbewusste weich werden lassen und Unbewusstes mit Bewusstem verbinden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Letting attention soften into a half-conscious state, and increasingly letting unconscious and conscious mind merge, so as to meet the visitors half way at the frequency they keep, which is set to make humans stretch."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Sightings; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSeeingCraftAlways a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeing the visitors' craft at will"@en, "Die Raumschiffe der Besucher jederzeit sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being able to see the visitors' craft all the time rather than only on rare occasions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Sightings; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSofteningYieldsSightings a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Blending unconscious and conscious yields seeing the craft all the time"@en, "Die Verbindung von Unbewusstem und Bewusstem lässt die Schiffe ständig sehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Many people see craft only in a softened, semi-conscious focus; once they blend more of the unconscious into the conscious they will be able to see the craft constantly."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharSofteningFocus ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharSeeingCraftAlways ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Sightings; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharDoingWhatExcitesMost a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Doing what excites you most, as the way to raise one's vibration and reach contact"@en, "Tun, was einen am meisten begeistert, als Weg, die eigene Schwingung zu heben und Kontakt zu finden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar's answer to how one raises one's vibratory level and how one comes to go aboard a ship: act on whatever excites one most, keep doing what represents who one is and be the person one needs to be, not waiting for the contact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Sightings; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharRaisedVibration a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A raised vibratory level"@en, "Eine erhöhte Schwingungsebene"@de ;
    skos:definition "A higher vibratory frequency of the person, the condition under which the visitors and their craft become perceivable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Sightings; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExcitementYieldsVibration a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Doing what excites you most raises one's vibration"@en, "Tun, was am meisten begeistert, hebt die Schwingung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked how one raises one's vibratory level, Bashar answers in a single line: by doing what excites one the most."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharDoingWhatExcitesMost ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharRaisedVibration ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Sightings; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEncounterPurpose a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Encounters with extraterrestrials as a reunion that awakens one's own godhood"@en, "Begegnungen mit Außerirdischen als Wiedervereinigung, die die eigene Göttlichkeit weckt"@de ;
    skos:definition "To a questioner reporting three encounters of the third kind at close range, Bashar says the general reason for any encounter is a reunion that wakes people to their own power and godhood and the creative energy within, to be used to change the world and open it to further exchange with other worlds. Specific meanings lie with the person, in agreements and contracts made with those beings to be reminded of who one is at set times."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Why the Encounters?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSelectiveSightingFrequency a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Craft are seen by those attuned to their frequency; sightings as identification"@en, "Schiffe sehen die auf ihre Frequenz Abgestimmten; Sichtungen als Identifikation"@de ;
    skos:definition "A man and his wife report nineteen UFOs nobody else saw. Bashar says craft exist in another dimensional frame and are seen only by those attuned to it, so one person may see them and the next not. The craft were engaged in identification: matching vibration with vibration and taking stock of what share of humanity aligns with the frequency that would allow more contact; the witnesses were noticed and shown symbols that pass straight into the unconscious to awaken whatever they will allow, and to give momentum to what is strongest in them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Why the Encounters?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSightingsMirrorEnergy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sightings mirror the level of energy one is operating on"@en, "Sichtungen spiegeln die Energieebene, auf der man arbeitet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Sightings come from the vibratory frequency a person has put himself on and indicate the level of energy at which he operates; they are a mirror showing how much energy he has and that he can do whatever he wants with it now, without waiting."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: a sighting is announced as the mark of a raised energy level; no deadline or count; the sighting is observable to the witness; the text sets no corresponding mark of failure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Why the Encounters?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharColouredStarLights a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Colour-changing star-like lights: mostly atmospheric aberration, some dimensional doorways"@en, "Farbwechselnde sternartige Lichter: meist atmosphärische Brechung, manche Dimensionstore"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lights that rotate through red, green and blue are mostly stars refracted by the atmosphere acting as a prism and lens, since stars do not twinkle above it; some are dimensional doorways or tunnels, out of which many spacecraft come. The energies around when people cannot sleep do not always show as craft; a questioner who points out stars as craft is told this is rarely so."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Why the Encounters?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharObviousCraftRule a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The rule of thumb: unless it is obviously a craft, treat it as none and go about your business"@en, "Die Faustregel: Wenn es nicht offensichtlich ein Schiff ist, gilt es als keines; geh deinen Geschäften nach"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked how one would know a spaceship, Bashar says one would not necessarily know and offers a practical rule many have found convenient: what is not plainly a craft is not to be counted as one, even should it be one, since guessing serves no purpose; if unsure, one carries on with one's affairs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Why the Encounters?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharUnmistakableSighting a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "When you are sure, you cannot be mistaken"@en, "Wenn du sicher bist, gibt es keinen Irrtum"@de ;
    skos:definition "A real sighting is promised to bring a certainty that leaves no room for error."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: unmistakable certainty is announced as the mark of a real sighting; no deadline or count; observable only as the witness's own conviction; any doubtful sighting is by the rule of thumb set aside, so doubt is never counted as a failure of the claim."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Why the Encounters?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharExtendingSensesToSkyObject a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Extending imagination and senses to the point in the sky where something is seen"@en, "Vorstellung und Sinne zu dem Punkt am Himmel ausdehnen, an dem etwas gesehen wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "When something is seen in the sky, reach out with imagination and senses to that place in space and notice what is picked up; much of what is seen, Bashar says, is not physical sight at all, and the witness of a star-like object leaving what felt like a mother ship saw a motion outside our dimension."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Why the Encounters?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPerceivingConsciousnessInSky a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Picking up a consciousness at the point extended to"@en, "An dem erreichten Punkt ein Bewusstsein wahrnehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Perceiving some form of consciousness at the place in the sky to which one has extended one's senses, and in time co-creating the shape of further interaction."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Why the Encounters?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharExtendingYieldsConsciousness a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Extending the senses to a sky object always picks up a consciousness"@en, "Das Ausdehnen der Sinne zu einem Himmelsobjekt nimmt stets ein Bewusstsein wahr"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some consciousness or other is always perceived, since everything is conscious; what one specifically finds Bashar will not discuss until the person has begun to take up the invitation, after which the interaction will be co-created."@en ;
    skos:note "Since everything is said to be conscious, the yield cannot fail; what is found is left undefined."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharExtendingSensesToSkyObject ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharPerceivingConsciousnessInSky ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Why the Encounters?; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharGoingWhereAttracted a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Going to the places that attract you, away from large cities, and being alone"@en, "An die Orte gehen, die einen anziehen, fern großer Städte, und allein sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "For one who wants to board a ship: act on the impulse and go to the places on Earth that draw one, those most conductive to such blendings, which the visitors have frequented; one need not go far, but ships are more readily seen outside large cities, and being somewhere alone greatly raises the chances of contact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharPhysicalContactAboard a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Going aboard a ship and meeting the visitors physically"@en, "An Bord eines Schiffes gehen und den Besuchern leiblich begegnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being taken aboard a spacecraft in the physical body and spending time with extraterrestrials, which the text says all have already done in dreams."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharContactPlacesYieldBoarding a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Doing what excites you, in attracting places and alone, brings the timed agreement for contact"@en, "Begeisterndes tun, an anziehenden Orten und allein, führt zur verabredeten Zeit des Kontakts"@de ;
    skos:definition "The agreement to go aboard is already made and will be met; persisting in what expresses who one is leads most quickly into it, and going to attracting places and being alone greatly increases the chance. Bashar guarantees nothing, as the timing always depends on the individual."@en ;
    skos:note "No deadline is given; the outcome, a physical boarding, would be observable."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharDoingWhatExcitesMost ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharGoingWhereAttracted ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharPhysicalContactAboard ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTimingMismatch a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The visitors' own timing may not match even when you are ready"@en, "Das Timing der Besucher passt manchmal nicht, auch wenn man bereit ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "People credit the visitors with powers they lack, such as appearing anywhere at any moment; the visitors follow the natural flow lines of timing and the universe's electromagnetic field, so even a ready person may find that the timing on their side does not fulfil the agreement."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a contact that does not come may be due to the visitors' timing and the field lines they follow; no deadline or count; the absence of contact is observable; the failure is put on cosmic timing, not on the person."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharSeekingTimingInMeditation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Seeking the timing of contact in meditation and in pursuing what matters most"@en, "Den Zeitpunkt des Kontakts in Meditation und im Verfolgen des Wichtigsten suchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To learn when the timing of contact will be, one may sometimes receive it in meditation, but always by exploring what means most to one in physical life, and in acting on those pursuits."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharRecognitionOfTiming a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognition of the timing of contact"@en, "Erkennen des Zeitpunkts des Kontakts"@de ;
    skos:definition "Whatever kind of awareness of the timing of contact one needs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMeditationYieldsTiming a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Acting on what matters most yields recognition of the timing"@en, "Handeln nach dem Wichtigsten bringt Erkennen des Zeitpunkts"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the action of the things that mean most to one, one will have whatever recognition of the timing one needs; it may also come in meditation."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharSeekingTimingInMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharRecognitionOfTiming ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFalseReadiness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "You usually think you are ready when you are not, and run"@en, "Man hält sich meist für bereit, wenn man es nicht ist, und läuft davon"@de ;
    skos:definition "People eager to meet the visitors in the flesh often declare themselves fully ready; yet when, in a remote place, they feel the energy change and the visitors draw close in vibration and are about to appear, they flee and ask for more time. Exposure to a higher vibration raises what one is not ready to face, so the running is from oneself; the visitors will know when one is ready."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a contact that does not happen is explained by the person's unreadiness, which he himself cannot judge; no deadline or count; the flight is observable to the person; the failure is put on the person, who is told in advance that his own sense of readiness is not to be trusted."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNeedingContactPreventsIt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Contact will not come to one who feels incomplete without it"@en, "Kontakt kommt nicht zu dem, der sich ohne ihn unvollständig fühlt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Abduction or detention aboard can happen, but often will not when it is asked for in the sense that the asker will not feel whole until it occurs; the visitors will not come and reinforce that sense of being incomplete."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: wanting contact out of need or desperation is named as the reason it does not occur; no deadline or count; the failure is put on the person's need."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharNotNeedingContact a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Not giving contact a second thought: living fully without needing it"@en, "Dem Kontakt keinen zweiten Gedanken schenken: voll leben, ohne ihn zu brauchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar's advice to one who would like to be abducted: do not think about it twice, go about one's business, live as fully as possible as the person one wants to be, do not need it or crave it in desperation, relax, and trust that all happens in perfect timing by agreements serving everyone."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNotNeedingYieldsContact a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Not needing contact is the best way to it"@en, "Den Kontakt nicht zu brauchen ist der beste Weg zu ihm"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked for the best way to be taken aboard, Bashar names not needing it and living one's life fully; physical boarding comes as soon as dream state and body are no longer thought different."@en ;
    skos:note "No deadline is given, and the timing is said always to depend on the individual."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharNotNeedingContact ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharPhysicalContactAboard ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDreamBodyNotDifferent a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Physical boarding follows once dream state and body are not taken as different"@en, "Leibliches An-Bord-Gehen folgt, sobald Traumzustand und Körper nicht mehr als verschieden gelten"@de ;
    skos:definition "All have been aboard ships in dreams; one who wants it bodily will have it once dreaming and the body are no longer held to be two different things."@en ;
    skos:note "The prior condition stated in the text is the ceasing to distinguish dream from body; it is attached here to the practice of not needing contact, which the same reply sets out."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:BasharNotNeedingContact ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharPhysicalContactAboard ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHigherVibrationCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Exposure to a higher vibration brings up what one cannot yet face"@en, "Die Begegnung mit einer höheren Schwingung bringt hervor, dem man sich noch nicht stellen kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "Part of why contact is timed is that meeting a higher vibration often raises things about oneself one is not yet ready to confront, and most of the flight people take is from themselves."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:BasharGoingWhereAttracted ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharGroundworkForContact a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Laying the groundwork for open interaction between civilizations"@en, "Den Grund für offene Begegnung zwischen Zivilisationen legen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Making it unsurprising that humanity and the visitors should interact, through the government sharing what it knows of their existence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLovingGovernmentYieldsGroundwork a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Opening loving communication with government lays the groundwork for contact"@en, "Liebevolle Verständigung mit der Regierung bereitet den Kontakt vor"@de ;
    skos:definition "People can open lines of communication with their government in loving ways and let it share the information of the visitors' existence, which makes interaction less surprising and lays its groundwork."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharTakingBackResponsibility ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharGroundworkForContact ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Going for a Ride; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharBuildingOwnCraft a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Building one's own craft with the technology of Earth"@en, "Mit irdischer Technik ein eigenes Fahrzeug bauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "For one excited by having an interplanetary ship: act on what one can act on now, use the technology already on the planet to build the craft one can, and explore on one's own terms the principles of that level of technology; these are the lessons, and the reason one chose to live in this society at its present technological level is to be tapped. In dreams one is already being taught."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section My Own Ship; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharAccessToAlienCraft a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Access to a spacecraft of non-terrestrial origin, and knowing how to use it"@en, "Zugang zu einem Raumschiff nichtirdischer Herkunft und das Wissen, es zu nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Coming to have a ship not made on Earth, and by then understanding how to operate it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section My Own Ship; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOwnCraftYieldsAlienCraft a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Building one's own craft brings access to an alien craft closer"@en, "Der Bau eines eigenen Fahrzeugs bringt den Zugang zu einem fremden näher"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is not yet the time for an alien craft, but making one's own and so meeting the visitors half way brings that probability closer, and one will know how to use it when it comes; acting on what excites one that one can act on leads to what excites one that one cannot yet reach."@en ;
    skos:note "No time is set; the text says the probability is real but the timing is not yet."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharBuildingOwnCraft ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharAccessToAlienCraft ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section My Own Ship; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNewMexicoLabsNoComment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bashar declines to comment on alien labs in New Mexico"@en, "Bashar lehnt Auskunft über außerirdische Labore in New Mexico ab"@de ;
    skos:definition "A questioner who helped with a book on the 1947 crash at Aztec cites a writer, Paul M., who says the government has handed labs in New Mexico to aliens responsible for cattle mutilation and the abduction of women. Bashar says the idea is somewhat exaggerated, that he is not allowed to comment, and only that it serves the population beneficially and is not as described; the book itself is part of a long-suppressed information leaking out."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section UFO Crash; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharGeorgeChannelingReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "A writer's claim that entities at war, with Sirius involved, spoke through him"@en, "Die Behauptung eines Autors, im Konflikt stehende Wesen, auch Sirius, hätten durch ihn gesprochen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A questioner reports that a writer named George said information was channelled to him by entities engaged in a long conflict with other beings, Sirius also being involved. Bashar answers that it is no conflict as humans understand it, only pressure created where dimensional realities intersect, which translates badly into human terms."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "a writer named George, reported second-hand by a questioner" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "entities engaged in a lasting conflict with other beings, with Sirius involved" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "Said to have been channelled to the writer; no date, place or manner is given." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section UFO Crash; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHangar18Crash a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Hangar 18 craft: a Zeta Reticulum ship brought down in July 1947"@en, "Das Hangar-18-Schiff: ein Zeta-Reticulum-Schiff, im Juli 1947 abgestürzt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The craft of the Hangar 18 story was not shot down but was of Zeta Reticulum origin, exploring during a storm with strong electrical activity; the radar of that time could disturb such craft's guidance, which altered the protective field so parts of the metal hull were exposed to lightning; it was struck, downed and retrieved by the government in July 1947. Other incidents and radar attempts followed, rarely ordinary weapons caused malfunctions; the government holds several craft and remnants, this one still in pieces under watch in many places, chiefly near Virginia. Its crew was dead; they were Reticuli about three to three and a half feet tall, hairless, with large heads and black eyes, thin long bodies, barely any mouth, nose or ears and pasty white skin, others of that people being beige, tan or dark grey-green."@en ;
    skos:note "A dated claim about the past, testable in principle; the radar effect is said to work no longer. The questioner's 7-7-47 is affirmed by Bashar."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section UFO Crash; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFortyYearCycleSince1947 a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The 1947 crash began a forty-year cycle initiating Earth into the Association"@en, "Der Absturz von 1947 begann einen vierzigjährigen Zyklus der Einweihung der Erde in die Vereinigung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked what the crashed beings gained, Bashar says humanity has now been initiated on the forty-year cycle that lets it start its entry into the Association of civilizations. Knowingly or not on those beings' part, the crash set off events that brought humans to their present understanding and ability to join. The beings know in their highest understanding that they served a purpose even at the cost of their physical death, accelerating human awareness and making Bashar's present talks possible; many seemingly accidental events will follow."@en ;
    skos:note "Read against the July 1947 date, the forty years end about 1987, near the time of the sessions; the text gives no other date."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section UFO Crash; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBillyMeier a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Billy Meier"@en, "Billy Meier"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Billy Meier" ;
    pm:nameRole "a Swiss contactee of the Pleiadians, a vanguard who took the brunt of ridicule" ;
    skos:definition "A Swiss citizen whom a questioner visited, said to have had eleven years of contact with Pleiadians and the mission to make the contacts known. Bashar says the mission was done and the ice broken; Meier chose to be a forerunner bearing the ridicule, but much of his material has become twisted and unreliable through admixed false information; he is no longer carrying the whole weight, as Pleiadians now contact others, and his present troubles come partly from his own absorption in intrigue. The model he built to compare with photographs of real ships was later taken as proof of fakery by a television programme that had not done its research, whose real purpose was to familiarize the public with Zeta Reticuli contact."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Billy Meier; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMeierPleiadianReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "Billy Meier's claim that his information came from Pleiadians"@en, "Billy Meiers Behauptung, seine Informationen stammten von Plejadiern"@de ;
    skos:definition "The questioner reports that Meier has had a contact lasting eleven years with Pleiadians and was charged to make all the contact information public; Bashar affirms the contact, though less of it lately than supposed, and says much of the published material is no longer reliable because false information was mixed in."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Billy Meier, a Swiss citizen, reported second-hand by a questioner who visited him" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Pleiadians" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "Said to be face-to-face contacts over eleven years, the last in August of the year of the session, with photographs of ships; Meier is said to have survived attempts on his life and to live in seclusion." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Billy Meier; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSpaceTimeAsProperty a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Space and time as properties of the object; travel by redefinition rather than motion"@en, "Raum und Zeit als Eigenschaften des Objekts; Reisen durch Umdefinition statt Bewegung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar's people can go to any place and time, since an object is not in space and time but has them as changeable properties. Their craft are projected into astral material, given the vibration of the target locale and reinserted into physical matter there, skipping travel altogether: instantaneous teleportation, not faster-than-light motion within our dimension. Navigation keys on vibration, as a radio is tuned, so a pilot could steer by the felt vibration of a single being of the target system; humans do the same out of the body in sleep, becoming a vibration and arriving at once. The ship is an extension of consciousness, connected to the pilot's mind and keyed to his vibration alone."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Space Travel; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharCraftPropulsionAndMaterial a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The visitors' craft: field drive, gravitational bubble and grown crystalline metal"@en, "Die Schiffe der Besucher: Feldantrieb, Gravitationsblase und gezüchtetes kristallines Metall"@de ;
    skos:definition "The drive involves electromagnetic fluctuation but chiefly gravitational dynamic tensor fields; the sealed craft go under water as easily as through space and can shift out of phase to pass into or through solid matter. Each has its own gravity bubble, so the crew feel upright whatever its attitude. Within a reality they navigate by its gravitational and electromagnetic fields and masses. The hull is a grown crystalline metal refined by cold fusion and programmed holographically: given an electrical template it takes that form and collapses again once the template is taken away; it is grown atom by atom on energy templates. The interior is fluid more than the exterior. Their science is mostly intuition, and humans will lack the support systems for this material for some time."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Space Travel; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Navigation; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNavigationalGrid a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "The visitors' navigation by vibrational equations on a spherical grid"@en, "Die Navigation der Besucher nach Schwingungsgleichungen auf einem kugelförmigen Gitter"@de ;
    skos:definition "Objects are vibrational equations with location as one variable; navigation is by tonal vibration on a holographic map in the shape of a sphere plotting extrapolated vibrations at any distance from any point. The reference sphere has a plane through it called the galactic ecliptic or G.E.; a line from the centre through the observer's world is zero and the opposite direction 180 degrees starboard or port; above the plane is positive, below negative; distance from the centre is counted in radials, and an angle fixes the position. The isolation field opens the ship's navigation to every probable universe by their signature frequencies; the intuitive pilot picks one from the imagination, the frequency is imposed through the harmonics of light, and when the field drops the ship resides wherever that frequency belongs."@en ;
    dcterms:date "undated in the full-text layer, which carries no imprint" ;
    pm:compiledBy "Bashar through Darryl Anka, in Blueprint for Change" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Space Travel; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Navigation; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharParallelTimeTracks a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Time travel moves one to a parallel time track; one's own past cannot be changed"@en, "Zeitreisen führen in eine parallele Zeitspur; die eigene Vergangenheit lässt sich nicht ändern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Space and time are one, so a craft can go to fifteenth-century Earth; but any seeming change made in the past happens on a track parallel to the one left. All tracks exist at once: going back from track A one enters track B as part of its natural history, and to see the effect of a change one must go to that parallel track's present or future. Changing one's past means shifting to another history that already contains the desired change and experiencing it as one's new present; the same holds for the future."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Time Travel; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharIsolationField a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The isolation field: a shell of stepped-up light that lifts the craft out of the universe"@en, "Das Isolationsfeld: eine Hülle aus hochgestuftem Licht, die das Schiff aus dem Universum hebt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The field is a microwave effect, a modification of light raised far beyond ordinary electrical discharge by devices including what is called the flash matrix and spread through the hull. Microwaves at that rate disconnect whatever is in the bubble from its universe by matching the frequency of light, the limit of physical dimensionality, in condensed form; light, the stuff of the physical universe, is turned around rather than through the craft, which is then held by the primal template universe far above light's frequency, where one is everything at once and can be anywhere and anywhen."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Isolation Field; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharIsolationFieldPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction: researchers will publicly announce isolation fields from counter-rotating magnetized masses"@en, "Vorhersage: Forscher werden Isolationsfelder aus gegenläufig rotierenden magnetisierten Massen öffentlich bekanntgeben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked whether human technology can make the field now, Bashar says yes: many people are experimenting and will make public announcements; at base it uses counter-rotating masses carrying strong magnetic charge, which generate the field well enough for isolation, with finer control later from more conductive materials. He tells the questioner to watch the media and literature."@en ;
    skos:note "A prediction without a date; the announcement and the effect would both be observable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Isolation Field; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharSolarWind a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Solar Wind, Bashar's mother ship"@en, "Der Sonnenwind, Bashars Mutterschiff"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "the Solar Wind" ;
    pm:nameRole "the mother ship of Bashar's people" ;
    skos:definition "The ship Bashar calls his people's mother ship, shown in the guided journey as a long metal cylinder about a mile in length, entered through an opening in its side into a milky whiteness full of loving, laughing presences; light, moving through its central core, powers it and makes the appearance of its motion through all dimensions. Every mother ship has a chamber where the projections of many civilizations confer."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Field Trip; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharFieldTripToTheMotherShip a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "The field trip: a guided imaginal journey in a crystal bubble to the mother ship"@en, "Die Exkursion: eine geführte Imaginationsreise in einer Kristallblase zum Mutterschiff"@de ;
    skos:definition "With eyes shut the group pictures the room and all present enclosed together in a transparent blue crystal bubble of energy, their elevator and ship, of which they become the activating devices, putting earthly tools aside. They let the room dissolve into grey fog, breathe the same energy deeply three times, align and unite, and feel each other as facets of oneself, one master crystal lit by the white light of their consciousness, which rises above the Earth into space. They look back on Earth and send love, see the mile-long cylinder, enter it into whiteness, leave the bubble and roam and explore, touching, tasting and marvelling, interpreting the chambers as they like, aware that they are projecting part of themselves astrally and will carry the information back into their bodies and Earth's air. Then they regather in the docking bay, re-form the craft, descend, touch the ground with their feet and send roots into the earth."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Field Trip; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFieldTripEffects a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The effects of the field trip: encoded information, vivid dreams, a part of oneself aboard"@en, "Die Wirkungen der Exkursion: verschlüsselte Information, lebhafte Träume, ein Teil von einem an Bord"@de ;
    skos:definition "Each participant has taken in and encoded the journey's information, which will be released in its own way, changing the air and the energy of the planet; dreams may become vivid and vibrant, with more release and pliability and more recognition that the surrounding life is what one dreams it to be. A portion of each remains aboard the craft permanently, shared with Bashar's people; the participants are to know it was a real experience."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: vivid and vibrant dreams and a sense that life is malleable are announced as possible after-effects; hedged with may; no deadline or count; observable only to the participant; their absence is not said to mean anything."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Field Trip; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFieldTripYieldsEffects a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The field trip yields encoded information, vivid dreams and a lasting share in the ship"@en, "Die Exkursion bringt verschlüsselte Information, lebhafte Träume und bleibende Teilhabe am Schiff"@de ;
    skos:definition "By the guided journey participants are said to project a part of themselves aboard the ship, to bring its information back into their bodies and the Earth, and to have it release afterwards in their own fashion, possibly in vivid dreams."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharFieldTripToTheMotherShip ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharFieldTripEffects ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 14 UFOs Identified, section Field Trip; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

#
# Chapter 15, Zeta and the Legacy
#

pmc:BasharDetainmentsByAgreement a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Abductions as detainments made by unconscious agreement to release fear"@en, "Entführungen als Festhaltungen nach unbewusster Vereinbarung, um Angst zu lösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Discussing Bud Hopkins's Intruders, Bashar proposes the word detainments in place of abductions. The pain and discomfort reported are mostly made by fear; some of it is physical, some a telepathic idea so strong it feels physical. One purpose is to free people of fear so that fear, pain and discomfort leave their lives; all is done by agreement, usually unconscious. Those chosen, even those in terror, are near the end of their fears; they have agreed to carry this for everyone and share it so that others may live through it at second hand and integrate their own fear, and later interactions grow more conscious."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Intruders; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFearShowsUnconsciousAgreement a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear shows that the agreement cannot yet be made consciously"@en, "Angst zeigt, dass die Vereinbarung noch nicht bewusst getroffen werden kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked why the visitors do not simply ask openly for consent, Bashar says the agreements are still unconscious; people may say they would agree, but the fear comes up anyway, and the fear itself shows that the agreement cannot yet be made consciously; a request for open consent comes only after the fact."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the detainee's fear is read as the sign that conscious agreement is not yet possible; no deadline or count; the fear is observable; the failure is put on the person, and the visitors' method is not counted against them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Intruders; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBudHopkins a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Bud Hopkins"@en, "Bud Hopkins"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Bud Hopkins" ;
    pm:nameRole "author of Intruders, fulfilling his agreement" ;
    skos:definition "The author of Intruders, a book on people taken aboard craft and examined. Bashar says he is fulfilling his agreement and helping Earth and the visitors' societies to live in harmony."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Intruders; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharVicariousIntegration a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Going through the detainees' ordeal at second hand to meet and integrate one's own fear"@en, "Die Prüfung der Festgehaltenen stellvertretend durchleben, um der eigenen Angst zu begegnen und sie zu integrieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reading or hearing the accounts of detainees so as to share their ordeal vicariously, contact the fear still left in oneself and integrate it; books such as Communion are said to serve this end even when they frighten."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Intruders; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharMoreConsciousInteractions a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Less fear to integrate and more conscious interactions in the next wave"@en, "Weniger zu integrierende Angst und bewusstere Begegnungen in der nächsten Welle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Integrated fear, and a next series of contacts that is increasingly conscious and carries less fear."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Intruders; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharVicariousIntegrationYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Sharing the detainees' ordeal makes the next interactions more conscious"@en, "Das Teilen der Prüfung der Festgehaltenen macht die nächsten Begegnungen bewusster"@de ;
    skos:definition "By going through the shared accounts and integrating their own fear, others leave less fear for the next wave of interactions, which can then become more conscious."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharVicariousIntegration ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharMoreConsciousInteractions ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Intruders; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers", "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharWhitleyStrieber a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Whitley Strieber"@en, "Whitley Strieber"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "Whitley Strieber" ;
    pm:nameRole "author of Communion, a detainee helped to release fear" ;
    skos:definition "Author of the then new book Communion. Bashar says the beings who met him were helping him release fear planted in his life, that nothing occurred he had not agreed to at some unconscious level, and that he now understands his fear came from himself, not from them; it was known he would report his experience so that others could face their fears."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharCommunionAsTool a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A frightening book as the tool that fits those who need it"@en, "Ein beängstigendes Buch als das Werkzeug für die, die es brauchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To a questioner who thinks Communion frightens more than it uplifts and works against Bashar's teaching, Bashar answers that many can relate to the matter in no other way, have received the tools suited to them, and will be reached; the book has already awakened many. The whole planet has agreed at one level to this kind of teaching, though it need not be so: whether the world wakes up or is shaken awake is up to it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDisvalueCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not judge the frightening account as a disvalue"@en, "Den beängstigenden Bericht nicht als Unwert beurteilen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar warns the questioner not to regard such a book as harmful, since doing so reinforces some people's inability to take it in."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:BasharCommunionAsTool ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharTrustingInTheInteraction a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Trusting, during a detainment, in one's own knowing of what one does"@en, "Während einer Festhaltung darauf vertrauen, dass man weiß, was man tut"@de ;
    skos:definition "For anyone who finds himself in such an interaction: trust that one knows what one is doing, since one agreed to it, and bring as much trust and love as one can."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLessFearInInteraction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Experiencing the interaction with less fear"@en, "Die Begegnung mit weniger Angst erleben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Feeling the encounter with the visitors less and less in the form of fear."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharTrustYieldsLessFear a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The more trust and love, the less the interaction is felt as fear"@en, "Je mehr Vertrauen und Liebe, desto weniger wird die Begegnung als Angst erlebt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The more trust and love one has, the less one will experience the interaction as fearful; Bashar says that is all it takes."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharTrustingInTheInteraction ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharLessFearInInteraction ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharHigherVibrationForcesFacing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A higher vibration raises a lower one and forces it to face itself"@en, "Eine höhere Schwingung hebt eine niedere und zwingt sie, sich selbst zu begegnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When a higher vibratory state is exposed to a lower, it lifts the lower being's vibration and compels it to face what it has refused so far to see in itself; that is what terrifies it, and in dealing with it the being integrates the fear and turns it into understanding."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharZetaBufferedAcclimatization a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Reticuli acclimatize humans gradually, from childhood, in buffered ways"@en, "Die Reticuli gewöhnen Menschen schrittweise, von Kindheit an, auf gepufferte Weise"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Zeta intention can always be felt as loving overall, but their methods and thought patterns are alien, so their natural ways generate fear in humans; they will not reshape their whole psychology beyond a point, knowing humans can cope and have agreed to learn to. The right to contact was granted by the agreement. Their task is to accustom many people to contact in a buffered way, far smoother than a sudden full appearance: contact bit by bit over long periods, often from childhood, letting people recall more and more until they see there is nothing to fear. The aliens act with integrity as best they can but are not responsible for how humans made their society or for their reactions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOpenContactWithoutFear a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Open and obvious contact"@en, "Offener und offensichtlicher Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Contact with the visitors taking place openly and plainly, once the person can handle it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNoFearBeforeOpenContact a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Realizing there is nothing to fear comes before open contact"@en, "Die Einsicht, dass es nichts zu fürchten gibt, kommt vor dem offenen Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "People are allowed to remember more of their contacts until they reach the point of seeing that nothing is to be feared and that they can cope; then contact can occur more openly."@en ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:BasharLessFearInInteraction ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:BasharOpenContactWithoutFear ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEncounterReflectsPower a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Meeting the visitors reflects how powerful you are"@en, "Die Begegnung mit den Besuchern spiegelt, wie mächtig man ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Meeting such beings may be the first time in one's conscious life that one sees a reflection of one's own power; the fear is merely a response to believing one could not hold so much power, so that it must come from outside and might destroy one, which it cannot, being wholly a reflection of oneself."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Communion; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharLettingFearDeliverItsMessage a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Treating fear as a friend with a message, and becoming curious about it"@en, "Angst als Freund mit einer Botschaft behandeln und neugierig auf sie werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Know fear as a friend pointing to an unknown part of oneself to be integrated; let it deliver its message by knowing the message is there and can be heard, being fascinated that it may bring one and asking what it is. An example: sudden fear when a stranger approaches who only wants the time shows assumptions and habitual beliefs one may not prefer, which can now be changed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Fear's Message; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFearIntegrated a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear dissolved and the hidden part of oneself integrated"@en, "Aufgelöste Angst und der verborgene Teil des Selbst integriert"@de ;
    skos:definition "The end of a fear and the integration of the facet of oneself it pointed to, so that one becomes more of who one is; the nudges grow gentler until the fear is no longer felt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Fear's Message; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharCuriosityYieldsNoFear a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The moment you become curious, the fear is gone"@en, "Sobald man neugierig wird, ist die Angst fort"@de ;
    skos:definition "Even being fascinated that fear may carry a message can dull its negativity; once one becomes curious there is no more fear and the message has been received. The more one explores, the gentler the nudges, until that fear is no longer felt; acknowledging it as worth exploring ends the habit."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: curiosity itself is announced as the sign the message has been received, and the end of the fear as its outcome; no deadline or count; observable only to the person."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharLettingFearDeliverItsMessage ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharFearIntegrated ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Fear's Message; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFearStaysUntilHeard a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear stays and grows as long as its message is refused"@en, "Angst bleibt und wächst, solange ihre Botschaft abgewiesen wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "Fear is present only because its message is refused as not worth having; refused, it settles in, grows stronger and nags until it is let deliver. Because people believe in habits that run without their knowing, they often reject the message before they can think and do not attend quickly enough."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a fear that persists or grows is explained by the person's refusal of its message and his belief in habit; no deadline or count; the persisting fear is observable to the person; the failure is put on the person."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Fear's Message; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharKnowingRealityWithoutFear a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing one's reality without fear and creating it in a certain vibration"@en, "Die eigene Wirklichkeit ohne Angst kennen und sie in einer bestimmten Schwingung erschaffen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Holding a cognition of what is happening without fear, and creating one's reality at a vibration from which danger is not met; where a confrontation is nonetheless created, using the fear in the moment to deal with it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Fear's Message; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharNeverMeetingTheRobber a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Not meeting the robber at all, or changing the encounter midway"@en, "Dem Räuber gar nicht begegnen oder die Begegnung mittendrin wenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Knowing a danger is present without being touched by it negatively; normally not meeting the armed robber at all, he taking one street and oneself another; or, if one uses the scene to deal with fear, transforming it in the middle, the person attracted being one willing to change too."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Fear's Message; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFearlessVibrationYieldsSafety a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Creating one's reality at a certain vibration means never meeting the robber"@en, "Wer seine Wirklichkeit in einer bestimmten Schwingung erschafft, trifft den Räuber nie"@de ;
    skos:definition "A questioner proposes the case of a man with a gun two feet away; Bashar says that, creating reality at a certain vibration, one generally will never meet that robber, though the situation can also be turned midway, and some do create the confrontation as an exciting way to face their beliefs."@en ;
    skos:note "A claim with an observable outcome, but if the confrontation does happen it is explained as created by the person for his own learning, so no event counts against it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharKnowingRealityWithoutFear ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharNeverMeetingTheRobber ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section Fear's Message; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFacilitatorsReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "The claim that the Facilitators of Zeta Reticulum spoke through Darryl Anka"@en, "Die Behauptung, die Facilitators von Zeta Reticulum hätten durch Darryl Anka gesprochen"@de ;
    skos:definition "An editorial note in the chapter says that, with Bashar facilitating, the following passage was channelled through Darryl and was later identified as coming from the Facilitators of Zeta Reticulum. The passage speaks in a collective first person, thanks the audience for letting it draw out their fear, and presents the calling card of membership in the Association of Worlds."@en ;
    skos:note "This node records the claim, not its truth. It is the second speaker the book claims besides Bashar; the work's main claim for Bashar is recorded in pmc:BasharBlueprintReceiving."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Darryl Anka, the channel, with Bashar's facilitation" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "The Facilitators, beings of Zeta Reticulum who call themselves a collective recognizing their godhood collectively; identified only after the session" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "In the course of a Bashar session before an audience, after a question on fear, the chapter's editors note that the passage was channelled with Bashar's help; the name was given later. No date or place is printed." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Facilitators; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFacilitators a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Facilitators"@en, "Die Facilitators (die Vermittler)"@de ;
    pm:nameForm "The Facilitators" ;
    pm:nameRole "beings of Zeta Reticulum who evoke and release human fear; friends of humanity" ;
    skos:definition "Beings of Zeta Reticulum who call themselves humanity's friends, little known yet; they recognize their godhood collectively as humans do individually, each being the mirror of what the other has feared. In drawing out human fear they also face the fears of individuality in their own past; looking into their eyes one sees only the mirror of one's soul and the potential of one's godhood. They have watched humans for years and centuries and will join the new day with many other worlds in their own good timing."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Facilitators; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharOwningFear a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Feeling the fear the visitors evoke, owning it and acknowledging it as one's own"@en, "Die von den Besuchern geweckte Angst fühlen, annehmen und als eigene anerkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Facilitators invite people to let themselves feel, even briefly, the fear drawn out in the encounter, to see the mirror of their souls in the visitors' eyes, to accept their willingness to own the vibration called fear and to recognize it as what they have pushed away from themselves over the years."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Facilitators; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFearTransformed a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Fear transformed, followed by a longer time of joy"@en, "Verwandelte Angst, gefolgt von einer längeren Zeit der Freude"@de ;
    skos:definition "The transformation of owned fear, a vibration that otherwise hinders easy interaction with the visitors, and for the brief time fear is felt a longer span of joy later on."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Facilitators; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharOwningYieldsTransformation a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "What you feel you own, and what you own you transform"@en, "Was man fühlt, besitzt man, und was man besitzt, verwandelt man"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Facilitators say that as one feels the fear one will own it and as one owns it one will transform it, recalling that many beings have said one cannot transform what one does not own; for the brief time of fear there will be more joy later."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharOwningFear ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharFearTransformed ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Facilitators; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharFearPassingPrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction: fear of the visitors will soon be a thing of legend"@en, "Vorhersage: Die Angst vor den Besuchern wird bald Stoff der Legende sein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The Facilitators guarantee that membership of the Association of Worlds, whose calling card they present, will be exhilarating, and say that the present fear is passing: within a very short time on Earth it will become legend and nightmare that people cannot imagine having felt, like waking from a dream into one they prefer."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the passing of fear is announced with a deadline, a very short time, left without measure; the outcome would be observable in society; no failure is assigned if it does not come."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Facilitators; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharZetaHiveMirror a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Zeta as a hive mind mirroring human individuality, each needing the other"@en, "Die Zeta als Schwarmgeist, der die menschliche Individualität spiegelt; jeder braucht den anderen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A questioner reports a meditation in which she hovered over a planet of pale, sickly, Essassani-sized people forced to leave a dying world, and felt they were her people. Bashar says she perceived the Zeta society: they stand for the unified mind, a hive in which all bodies express one linked mind, which humans fear; humans stand for individual conviction, which they fear. Their sickliness is that they know they are in some way dying without humans, which is why the interaction goes on; from their side Earth might look as sickly. They are polar to humans and mirror them; each needs the other to become what it is becoming, and the blending will continue with more information coming out until both are whole."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Zeta Mirror; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharDreamAssistancePrediction a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Prediction to a questioner: awareness of her dream-level help within three years"@en, "Vorhersage an eine Fragende: Gewahrsein ihrer Hilfe auf Traumebene binnen drei Jahren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar tells the questioner that she is helping at the dream level in ways she may not yet know and may become strongly aware of within the next three years."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the person's own awareness is announced with a deadline of three years from the session, hedged by may; observable only to her; nothing is said of failure."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Zeta Mirror; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharChannelSymbology a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Bashar as made of the channel's symbols while having his own existence"@en, "Bashar als aus den Symbolen des Kanals gebildet und doch mit eigener Existenz"@de ;
    skos:definition "Asked whether Bashar, called Darryl's future self, is a definition of Darryl's higher self built from his symbols, Bashar agrees in many ways: he is made up from the symbolism of the channel's mind as experienced in the human world, yet exists in his own right, and might as well say humans are made of his symbols. What humans call unreal, dream and etheric energy, is his people's solid reality, which is why they are intertwined with human imagination and archetypes and stand for the human archetypal stream; humanity is moving to become someone else's dream in turn. Contact through people is easier than by radio, since the visitors do not operate on that frequency."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the work's own claim of reception, recorded in pmc:BasharBlueprintReceiving."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Legacy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmp:BasharTrainingAsBiologicalReceiver a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Training oneself in identification with love and acceptance"@en, "Sich darin üben, sich mit der Energie von Liebe und Annahme zu identifizieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Training the body and mind as a biological sender and receiver by identifying with love and with acceptance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Legacy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharBiologicalReception a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Efficient biological sending and receiving across civilizations"@en, "Wirksames biologisches Senden und Empfangen zwischen Zivilisationen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Functioning as a sender and receiver far more efficient than physical radio devices, linked by light to all members of one's own and other civilizations."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Legacy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLoveTrainingYieldsReception a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Identifying with love and acceptance makes biological senders and receivers usable"@en, "Identifikation mit Liebe und Annahme macht biologische Sender und Empfänger brauchbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "Biological senders and receivers are said to be much more efficient and of use once trained to identify with love and acceptance."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:BasharTrainingAsBiologicalReceiver ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:BasharBiologicalReception ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Legacy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharEssassaniAsHybrids a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Legacy: Essassani as the hybrid offspring of humans and Zeta Reticuli"@en, "Das Vermächtnis: Essassani als hybride Nachkommen von Menschen und Zeta Reticuli"@de ;
    skos:definition "Bashar calls the statement that his people are some 150 to 300 years ahead of humans an arbitrary nomenclature and now explains a temporal paradox. His people are humanity's future selves allegorically, largely literally in terms of reincarnation, and as a picture of the parallel civilization humans will build; but also they are an exact cross of the human form and the Zeta Reticuli, the children of the blending now going on in human time, a population of their world and another dimension. They kept to that other dimension so as not to interfere with the marriage and its consummation or with humans' right to experience their birth; now timing allows them to greet humans as their children. In their present they live side by side with a future Earth in harmony; each is the other's legacy."@en ;
    skos:note "Testable only in the sense that it ties the visitors' existence to the outcome of the interbreeding programme the book describes; no date is given."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Legacy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .

pmc:BasharLegacyLiteralCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Take the Legacy literally and yet not literally at all"@en, "Das Vermächtnis wörtlich nehmen und doch gar nicht wörtlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "Before the Legacy, Bashar asks his listeners to hear it with all their kinds of ears, taking it literally on one level and not at all literally on another, as it is archetypal energy too, the substream consciousness of the human and the Zeta realms; a construction of dreamtime is beginning."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:BasharEssassaniAsHybrids ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:BasharTransmission ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:BasharBlueprintForChange ;
    dcterms:source "Anka, Bashar: Blueprint for Change, ch. 15 Zeta and the Legacy, section The Legacy; read in a full-text layer without title page or page numbers" .
